{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters","id":1223771,"title":"Tell me about Half-Caste characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-31T17:25:28-07:00","id":1223771,"title":"Tell me about Half-Caste characters","content":"Including Godblooded, Demonblooded, Ghostblooded, Faeblooded","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T17:52:41-07:00","id":1223781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FMA245</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters#post1223771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including Godblooded, Demonblooded, Ghostblooded, Faeblooded</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for the record, the word &quot;Half-Caste&quot; is not being used further in the gameline for a number of understandable reasons (including but not limited to not all Exalt types having castes, the new edition not being as interested in shoving things into neat categorical boxes, and the negative associations attached to the word's history in real life).<br /> <br /> That said, every PC in my Okeanos game ended up being the result of some sort of magical heritage. The more humorous thing was that no one had even planned it as such.<br /> <br /> \u2022Barbus the Storm King had an elemental parent (specifically, a thunderbird).<br /> \u2022Hogane was, though he didn't know it, the child of two Lintha, but <i>not</i> born on Bluehaven.<br /> \u2022Seamstress of Dissolution was Ghost-Blooded and the adopted daughter of the Silver Prince.<br /> \u2022Hectare was the son of a Zenith Caste Solar.<br /> \u2022Pirate King Misu was the grandson of Kireeki and the great-grandson of the Ocean Father.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T18:13:47-07:00","id":1223785,"title":"","content":"&quot;Godblooded&quot; is typically the generic name for such beings, even in 1e and 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T03:02:27-07:00","id":1223866,"title":"","content":"I'll share my godblooded NPC from the playtest game.<br /> <br /> Kamea is the daughter of Resolute Atlas the god of maps and as such her skin is a living map that constantly updates. She's estranged from her father preferring to walk her own path and was a dancer in the temple of a group of Water Elementals called the Three Sisters until she was kidnapped by slavers, when the true value of her skin was realised she was quick witted enough to point out that flaying her would probably destroy the precious map and waited for an opportunity to escape her captors when they reached Port Calin and started looking for a way home among people who'd probably sell her if they had any idea how much she was worth. Luckily for her she was found by the PCs who were willing to travel all the way across the west to bring her home.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://68.media.tumblr.com/e3e3d46ab979f89ab29550c4a4a86526/tumblr_nvb0sf8xJ81u1unnvo1_540.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T13:12:20-07:00","id":1223983,"title":"","content":"Is the syntax meant to be &quot;tell me about YOUR half-caste characters&quot;? Or just a generic comparison of types?<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>If type:</b><br /> <br /> Demon-Blood &gt; Ghost-Blood &gt; God-Blood &gt; Fae-Blooded &gt; Half-Caste<br /> <br /> <b>Demon-Blooded</b> top my list (with <b>Ghost-Blooded</b> a close second). They have the &quot;stuck between two worlds&quot; schtick while simultaneously being the most adept at fighting both lineages. It's a great way to get a &quot;Witcher&quot; or &quot;Devil/Ghost-Hunter&quot; vibe if you want a more subtle game (less hulking Essence 6 demon warlords ripping down buildings - more shapeshifters, parasites and possessive-spirits..... where the X-Blooded are <i>aware</i> of the corruption, but can't necessarily reveal how they know).<br /> <br /> <b>God-Blooded</b> are rather lackluster - and usually I've seen them as higher-end canon-fodder. They're just &quot;human but awesome&quot; and the ability to sense sanctums is &quot;useful&quot; but hardly iconic.<br /> <br /> <b>Fae-Blooded</b> are more lackluster - the ability to resist Wyld mutation is pretty niche - and they don't really apotheosize into anything. Like God-Blooded, they're merely &quot;human - but more awesome!&quot; with no strong signature trick (unless you're exposed to the Wyld a lot.... but the <i>majority</i> of the Wyld is on the outskirts of creation, meaning you're the <i>most</i> useful in places where <i>no one cares</i>).<br /> <br /> <b>Half-Caste</b> are perfectly named. From the perspective of Gods and Exalts, being &quot;Half-Caste&quot; almost suggests your human side is the inferior one. However, the Lunar Exalted are likely the <i>most</i> likely to produce Half-Castes.... many of which would thus be Beastmen.... and thus, from a human perspective, it's the beastial-side which is inferior. So these characters have a strong pull to wrestle with their identity and humanity - but this isn't seen often in play. They often fall into the trope of &quot;human - but more awesome!&quot; (alongside God &amp; Fae blooded) except they also lack a signature &quot;type&quot; ability (like the other 4) and their charm mechanics were bonkers.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Also, worth noting &quot;for the record&quot;:</b><br /> <br /> Just because (group A - who once colonized) finds a term troublesome because of &quot;negative associations&quot; - doesn't mean (group B - who was colonized) find it offensive. The English-language (and culture) tends to obsess on <i>what</i> is said - while other languages (and cultures) focus on <i>how</i> it is said. Nothing about 2E Half-Castes implied insult nor offense.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For comparison, we have dozens of half-caste type terms in Spanish - used regularly - and <i>absolutely none of them </i>are viewed as pejoratives today. Luckily, Spanish speakers don't have that hang-up.... but periodically, an English-speaker hears &quot;mulatta&quot; or &quot;sambo&quot; or &quot;negra&quot; and has a heart-attack. Us &quot;natives&quot; care less about <i>what</i> is said (every time an English word is banned, a new one will just be invented anyways) and more about <i>how</i> it is said (which really is all that matters). <br /> <br /> <b>Worth noting because <i>avoiding half-caste terms</i> can be equally offensive,</b> since it almost implies &quot;instead of half-and-half, let me pretend one of your parents didn't exist&quot;. Calling my step-father a &quot;sambo&quot;, my brother &quot;un moreno&quot;, my cousin &quot;una mulatta&quot;, etc is all simply <i>accurate </i>- doing the &quot;American thing&quot; and lumping them into Red/Black/White/Yellow would just confuse the shit out of them.<br /> <br /> The fact that Half-Castes (in 2E) <b>do</b> fit an &quot;inbetween two worlds&quot; role actually makes the term appropriate. In a game with necrophilia, beastiality, incest, etc - having a term for a group with &quot;complex issues of identity and heritage&quot; is the <i>least</i> offensive thing to have. If anything, kudos to them for using the term correctly and elaborating on the difficulties Half-Castes in Exalted face.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T13:50:26-07:00","id":1223993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1223983#post1223983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Also, worth noting &quot;for the record&quot;:</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This again? You are not the only person of mixed race on this forum and others including myself have made their opinions perfectly clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T23:54:47-07:00","id":1224095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So these characters have a strong pull to wrestle with their identity and humanity - but this isn't seen often in play. They often fall into the trope of &quot;human - but more awesome!&quot; </div> </div> </div>I don't think they do actually.<br /> <br /> God-Bloods, Elemental-Bloods, Fae-Bloods, Demon-Bloods and Ghost-Bloods have a lot to wrestle with.<br /> Half-Solars? Not really. Solars are super-humans with sun-themes. So you're half-human, half-super human. So a weaker super human.<br /> <br /> With the other kinds, an ST can do slightly more interesting things with them. I had some Were-cats, though they ended up not being used much because the PCs weren't interested, they of course were the kids of a Lunar. You could have Dhampyrs as well.<br /> But there's not really much of a struggle between the two halves of their nature the way there is for a Demon-Blood.*<br /> <br /> *This is partly why I consider half-Exalts to be very dull. Half-Solars far more than the other ones though. Although half-Sidereals are fairly dull too.<br /> <br /> Also, Half-Caste isn't a great name, because they're not half-Twilight or whatever.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if you find a word neutral, and others find it offensive, is it that much hassle to avoid it? Especially a word used in a fantasy setting that could easily be replaced with some other mystic term? Half-Caste is a boring, uninspiring, and not very accurate term.*<br /> <br /> *For a boring and uninspiring set of characters, IMO. Though, as I said, more could be done with half-Lunars and half-Abyssals than the game has really bothered with. Still, half-Lunars are less interesting than beastmen anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the syntax meant to be &quot;tell me about YOUR half-caste characters&quot;? Or just a generic comparison of types?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wondered this too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon-Blood &gt; Ghost-Blood &gt; God-Blood &gt; Fae-Blooded &gt; Half-Caste </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I pretty much agree with this. Fae-Blooded are just a bit wacky, and can be intermediaries, but power-wise they're not much use. Most half-Exalts are pretty dull. Whereas Demon-Bloods and Ghost-Bloods have more interesting powers (and Ghost-Bloods are relatively common).<br /> God-Blooded are useful for an ST though, as they are often interlinked with a social structure and organisation, and can be given quite a wide variety of powers.<br /> <br /> In the last game I ran, I wanted to have a social villain who was far weaker than the PCs. His name was Jin the Just, King of the Southern Djala, and he was an god-blood. His powers were a)he could make plants entangle things, and b)he could jump into a tree and jump out of another tree. What this allowed him to do is run away if there was ever a fight. His real strength was his army and political pull (and the fact his mother was a jungle goddess featured a lot as a king in the jungle), I just wanted to give him powers so he didn't die in some random fight, and the PCs couldn't easily just beat him up like they did most kings.<br /> In the end, of course, he stood up to the PCs rather than just manipulating them, and the Full Moon gave him a pox-handshake, but in an Essence 5 Solar/Lunar game, I think an Essence 1 god-blood did pretty well to last 2 years as a villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-02-2018, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T06:20:28-07:00","id":1224145,"title":"","content":"I've tried to revise the Children of Exalts from basic principles rather than accepting &quot;pale shadow of their parents&quot; that the Player's Guide went with as the only option. They've prompted some interesting thought exercises on the ways inherited power expresses itself differently to rewarded power. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T07:43:06-07:00","id":1224156,"title":"","content":"Personally, i have toyed with the idea of exploring Inheritance as an Artifact-like merit of sorts, characters having the capacity to &quot;awaken evocations&quot; related to the legacy of legend coursing through their veins, but have yet to actually test it out in play.<br /> <br /> One thing that i did decide to do is keeping multiple legacies separate, meaning that the children of exalts with supernatural beings or a couple of god-bloods of diverse origins might become <b>very</b> peculiar indeed in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-02-2018, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T12:15:10-07:00","id":1224208,"title":"","content":"did a Solar Half caste game on Rpol during late first edition a bunch of kids trying to survive...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T12:42:22-07:00","id":1224211,"title":"","content":"Yeah, inheritance probably works best as a trait that the storyteller sets at the start of the chronicle based on what tier of play they're aiming for. <br /> <br /> That keeps everyone on the level and lets you do stuff like award so many bonus points per dot to spend on supernatural traits and gate off powers that would be OP (like maybe you need X inheritance to get an essence pool, which opens up a bunch of other stuff)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T18:12:10-07:00","id":1224251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224211#post1224211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, inheritance probably works best as a trait that the storyteller sets at the start of the chronicle based on what tier of play they're aiming for. <br /> <br /> That keeps everyone on the level and lets you do stuff like award so many bonus points per dot to spend on supernatural traits and gate off powers that would be OP (like maybe you need X inheritance to get an essence pool, which opens up a bunch of other stuff)</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have already said that God-Blooded <i>PCs</i> will be assumed to have use of Essence, and that for other God-Blooded, a powerful parent doesn't necessitate the presence of an Essence pool.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23657_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23657\" data-vbnamecard=\"23657\">VioletDreamer</a>: Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-02-2018, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T18:18:34-07:00","id":1224252,"title":"","content":"I don't think automatically is the right word, but it's generally true that if you're playing a god-blooded character that isn't something else, they'll probably be one potent enough to have charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T04:24:01-07:00","id":1224311,"title":"","content":"I should probably talk about the Moonborn that's become increasingly prominent in my game of late.<br /> <br /> Iskra is the daughter of Wandering Nightshade a Lunar who ended up in the service of a Deathlord, during that service he fell in love with a mortal woman who reminded him of his lost humanity and ended up carrying his child. When she died his hopes of redemption died with her. <br /> <br /> The child didn't die though, she'd already been touched by Luna and used that strength to force her own way into the world, to hunt and to adapt in order to overcome the weaknesses of being born so premature. When she reached her 16th year in the wilderness she became aware of humans and recognised some kinship with them, using the hunting techniques that had kept her alive she now preyed upon humans, the PCs took pity and brought her home with them where she's proving a real challenge for Lore and Medicine charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T06:20:09-07:00","id":1224338,"title":"","content":"Since we're sharing half-blooded characters:<br /> <br /> During a 2E game, I had a god-blooded character that exalted as a Solar. My divine parent was a goddess heavily influenced by Athena, the Greek goddess. Our Creation-Athena, named Linnea, was similar to Athena in that she was a maiden goddess. Meaning she really didn't care for men (didn't hate them, just had no use for them). She &quot;lay&quot; with women to have her god-blooded children via a unique charm. Nearly all her children since she came into existence have been daughters. My character was the second son she'd ever had, and it was not a good relationship. When I exalted as a Dawn caste, she felt that my character owed her for my upbringing. She would occasionally show up and make requests/demands of my character, which tended to end with them arguing with each other. The other players in our group always found the interactions amusing, even going so far as to take Linnea's side against their circle mate.<br /> <br /> As for 3E, I have yet to reprise this character, though it has been on my mind lately. As for the nature of my parentage, I'd probably work with the ST to take a unique supernatural Merit or two to signify my heritage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 06-03-2018, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T13:45:17-07:00","id":1224426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1223983#post1223983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Also, worth noting &quot;for the record&quot;:</b><br /> <br /> Just because (group A - who once colonized) finds a term troublesome because of &quot;negative associations&quot; - doesn't mean (group B - who was colonized) find it offensive. The English-language (and culture) tends to obsess on <i>what</i> is said - while other languages (and cultures) focus on <i>how</i> it is said. Nothing about 2E Half-Castes implied insult nor offense.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For comparison, we have dozens of half-caste type terms in Spanish - used regularly - and <i>absolutely none of them </i>are viewed as pejoratives today. Luckily, Spanish speakers don't have that hang-up.... but periodically, an English-speaker hears &quot;mulatta&quot; or &quot;sambo&quot; or &quot;negra&quot; and has a heart-attack. Us &quot;natives&quot; care less about <i>what</i> is said (every time an English word is banned, a new one will just be invented anyways) and more about <i>how</i> it is said (which really is all that matters).<br /> <br /> <b>Worth noting because <i>avoiding half-caste terms</i> can be equally offensive,</b> since it almost implies &quot;instead of half-and-half, let me pretend one of your parents didn't exist&quot;. Calling my step-father a &quot;sambo&quot;, my brother &quot;un moreno&quot;, my cousin &quot;una mulatta&quot;, etc is all simply <i>accurate </i>- doing the &quot;American thing&quot; and lumping them into Red/Black/White/Yellow would just confuse the shit out of them.<br /> <br /> The fact that Half-Castes (in 2E) <b>do</b> fit an &quot;inbetween two worlds&quot; role actually makes the term appropriate. In a game with necrophilia, beastiality, incest, etc - having a term for a group with &quot;complex issues of identity and heritage&quot; is the <i>least</i> offensive thing to have. If anything, kudos to them for using the term correctly and elaborating on the difficulties Half-Castes in Exalted face.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't do this. This board is predominantly made up of English speaking Americans and the term &quot;half-caste&quot; is offensive to many (most) for a variety of reasons. I understand you don't grasp the nuance because you are not a native American English speaker but the fact remains it is an offensive term (as are the terms &quot;Sambo&quot;, &quot;mulatto&quot; etc.)<br /> Those terms were used to denigrate, diminish and dehumanize entire classes and races of people. So while the term &quot;half-caste&quot; may be accurate from an in game perspective you are not conducting this discussion in game, you are discussing it in an environment where many people have already made you aware the term is inappropriate to use. The operating rule here (the forum) is that if someone tells you something is offensive you do not get to tell them it is not and then continue to use the offending term. That is not respecting the conversation Please understand this as I do not wish to have to take any further action beyond this post. Thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T14:27:26-07:00","id":1224809,"title":"","content":"While I enjoy responding to multiple people <i>individually</i>, for succinctness, I'll try to compress this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224095#post1224095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God-Bloods, Elemental-Bloods, Fae-Bloods, Demon-Bloods and Ghost-Bloods have a lot to wrestle with.<br /> <br /> Half-Solars? Not really. Solars are super-humans with sun-themes. So you're half-human, half-super human. So a weaker super human.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have this backwards, friend!<br /> <br /> The various (X)-Blooded play to supernatural tropes - but most of their descriptions describe how <b><i>irrelevant</i> </b>those supernatural heritages are to the world.<br /> <br /> You have Demon-Blooded who hunt demons, Ghost-blooded who exorcise ghosts, Fae-Blooded who can shrug off the Wyld..... <b>the point is</b> that none of their progenitors can influence the setting the way the Exalted can....and the half-humans often can side-step weaknesses explicit to their ancesotrs. And politically, the Immaculate Order might disapprove of liaisons - but they still <i>recruit</i> them.<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>The mixed heritage children who are neither fully Exalted nor fully human</i></span> are a completely different story. At <b>no point</b> are we led to believe one of them could viably usurp their parent. Instead...<ul><li>Their write-up describes them being used as favored slaves and concubines. The Exalted were not necessarily kind.<br /> .</li> <li>Their write-up describes the ensuing genocide (when the Solars were overthrown). Humanity &amp; the Dragon-Blooded were not sympathetic.<br /> .</li> <li>A Dragon-Touched isn't &quot;a cool super human&quot; - it's a <i>failure as a Terrestrial Exalt</i>, someone prone to attract <i>all the same enemies</i> the Terrestrials have - without the power to repel them. A Lunar won't care that you're &quot;merely Dragon-Touched&quot;, so long as you have a useful face to infiltrate Dynasts. If the Tepet Legions massacred half a town, the local mortals won't be forgiving of you just because you're not a &quot;full fledged&quot; tyrant.<br /> .</li> <li>A Moon-Born isn't &quot;a cool super human&quot; - not only the most populous of the batch, they're also kin to Beastmen, Lunars, Chimera, and all the horrors associated with them. The Wyld Hunt <b>will</b> kill you because you might just be a Lunar in disguise (or a spy for a Lunar). You will be dragged into Lunar politics the second anyone recognizes the kind of magic you wield.</li> </ul><br /> <b>This has real world parallels </b>which explains why the term for <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>the mixed heritage children who are neither fully Exalted nor fully human</i></span> was a deliberate (and good) choice. <br /> <br /> Calling them &quot;Anathema Spawn&quot; is too negative. <br /> <br /> Calling them &quot;Grandchildren of the Gods&quot; too positive.<br /> <br /> It's their <i>official 2E term </i>that sits on the fence, leaving the speaker and listener both &quot;up in the air&quot; as to how the other person intends it to be taken. Whether you view them as the &quot;union of two peoples&quot; (positive) or &quot;bastards of an invading empire&quot; (negative), those connotations <b>define</b> the. <br /> <br /> If you change the name, then you scrub out all that history and are left with &quot;uh, boring super humans&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Think of the Haitian Revolution - </b>where <i><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">mixed heritage individuals</span> </i>had an uncomfortable &quot;in-between-ess&quot;. As the mobs massacred the French, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>mixed heritage individuals</i></span> had no way of knowing which way they'd be treated. Would they be embraced as brothers-in-arms? Or demonized as conspirators? Some of them had supported slavery. Some of them were eager to see the French eliminated. Others went both ways, eager to see the French slaughtered - but then planning to step into their roles using their better education and resources.<br /> <br /> It's not a <b>word</b> that has negative/positive implications.<br /> <br /> It's the <b>context</b>. <br /> <br /> Racists Frenchmen and resentful Haitians would <b>both</b> refer to <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>mixed heritage individuals</i></span> <b>negatively. </b>And like with the Golden-Children, you could spend a life enslaved just to then be slaughtered when your masters are overthrown.<br /> <br /> But people who see <i><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">mixed heritage individuals</span> </i>as a symbol of unity see it <b>positively</b>; Frenchmen who think<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> <i>mixed heritage individuals</i> are lovelier than Europeans are using it <b>positively</b>; Haitians who see <i>mixed heritage individuals</i> as possessing education and resources, as well as </span><i>mixed perspective - </i>and who thus see them as a potential good for society - see it <b>positively</b>. And like with the Golden-Children, you could benefit from these stereotypes (for good or ill).<br /> <br /> It's much like playing a Half-Orc or Tiefling in D&amp;D. They are <b>not</b> merely &quot;fancy looking humans&quot; - Orcs and Devils have specific roles in the setting - which affects how their<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> <i>mixed heritage offspring</i></span> are treated. While <b>in-character</b> my characters can feign moral outrage - or be legitimately frustrated - by stereotypes.... <b>out-of-character</b>, I pick those &quot;races&quot; <b>because</b> I want to wrestle with those scenarios. <br /> <br /> <b>This is what<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> the mixed heritage children who are neither fully Exalted nor fully human</span> are about</b>. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1223993#post1223993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This again? You are not the only person of mixed race on this forum and others including myself have made their opinions perfectly clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope you're well!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The <b>1st response</b> on this thread started with a tangential &quot;for the record&quot; (on real-life usage) - as opposed to simply addressing the topic. <b>Therefore, </b>I thought it fair to also &quot;for the record&quot; as a polite rebut (since <b>both</b> sides of the historical aisle help contextualize the useful references being made for a game about <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>the mixed heritage children who are neither fully Exalted nor fully human.</i></span><br /> <br /> Also, I'm well ahead of you on the &quot;this again?&quot; feeling - but since some people consistently repeat &quot;I think this is offensive&quot; (without anyone asking them), I don't see how it is unfair or inappropriate to point out &quot;but this term can be used legitimately in some contexts&quot;. <br /> <br /> It's one of those weird things English does that - in trying to not be offensive - it censors, implying something <i>much more taboo and offensive</i>. You can <b>feel</b> whatever you like - but please understand no one is required to feel the same way - when nothing in the 2E text reads as insulting nor bigoted. To accept your <b>feeling</b> as true, it'd imply we think the author, the editor and others who worked on Exalted were <i>deliberately trying to give offense</i>.<br /> <br /> If I had to &quot;pick teams&quot;, I have to go with the author (who did no wrong), not a few vocal fans (who insist on ignoring context).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> [spoiler]\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224426#post1224426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't do this. This board is predominantly made up of English speaking Americans and the term &quot;half-caste&quot; is offensive to many (most) for a variety of reasons. I understand you don't grasp the nuance because you are not a native American English speaker but the fact remains it is an offensive term (as are the terms &quot;Sambo&quot;, &quot;mulatto&quot; etc.).</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the benefit of a doubt! And doubtless the different histories of our languages flavor how we read these things. I'll give this post a go without using the terms.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">But I really feel like it's the English-speakers lacking nuance. People <b><i>take</i> </b>offense - they don't <b><i>receive</i> </b>it. Context matters. Unless the author and editor of that book wrote something deeply offensive.... I just don't see it. They used a term with real-world parallels the same way we're expected to look at real-world Sun Gods for Solar inspiration, real-world religion for the Hun &amp; Po, real-world (everything) for (cool Exalted version).<br /> <br /> I <b>never denied</b> that some might be offended - it is <b>also</b> worthwhile to note some <i>aren't</i> offended. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">The meaning <b>must</b> go both ways.</span> If only one side gets to speak (the &quot;I'm offended&quot; crowd), then history takes all kinds of weird twists.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Tangent: I thought BLACK PANTHER was superb. The villain was an American zealot - convinced that his regional history/tragedy was relevant to the planet - so off he goes to liberate nations that don't need liberating, and to start wars with nations who weren't even fighting. Meanwhile the Wakandan's are focused on domestic policy far removed from US history.<br /> <br /> By extension, <i>the mixed heritage children who are neither fully Exalted nor fully human </i>are a very good parallel to a real-world issue of empire, a group of people viewed negatively <b>and</b> positively for many reasons. If only the negatives &quot;win&quot;, then great, we call them &quot;Sun Boys&quot; and &quot;Moon Girls&quot; and overlook their historical and political existence in favor of irrelevant one-shot characters. It just does a disservice and cheapens them. I might prefer Demon-Blooded, but I can't deny the &quot;children of empires&quot; angle the others have.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224426#post1224426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please understand this as I do not wish to have to take any further action beyond this post. Thank you.[/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I'll avoid the term (and I think I did so far in this post). But I hope I can continue to respectfully disagree? <br /> <br /> No one used any word to slander anyone. I didn't, the author didn't, the editor didn't.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My post didn't appear in a vacuum. When someone (repeatedly) says &quot;this word is offensive&quot; - I thought it meritous to interject &quot;but it has positive connotations and contexts too&quot;. Unlike the (X)-Blooded, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>the mixed heritage children who are neither fully Exalted nor fully human</i></span> have real-world parallels that are deliberate and interesting and enriching. It's as relevant as calling a group of magical shapeshifters &quot;Lunars&quot; (because you want real-world Lunar imagery) or calling ghosts either a Hun or Po (because you want real-world religious imagery), etc.<br /> <br /> Stay peachy folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T15:00:25-07:00","id":1224817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224809#post1224809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000ff\"><i>The mixed heritage children who are neither fully Exalted nor fully human</i></span>...</div> </div> </div> </div>The children of Exalts, at least the ones who don't go on to become Exalted themselves, are <i>not at all</i> Exalted, and <i>are</i> fully human. Moreover, the presence of inherited traits does not an inhuman make; thus, a Demon-Blooded is half-demon <i>and fully human</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-04-2018, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T15:41:45-07:00","id":1224824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224817#post1224817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The children of Exalts, at least the ones who don't Exalt themselves, are <i>not at all</i> Exalted, and <i>are</i> fully human. Moreover, the presence of inherited traits does not an inhuman make; thus, a Demon-Blooded is half-demon <i>and fully human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know many real-life half-demons or half-ghosts or half-demigods. The second you can wield magic to make problems go away, you fail to be 100% human in the eyes of the world around you (for comparison, see Marvel Mutants).<br /> <br /> More to the point, <i>the children of half-and-half heritage</i> <b>should </b>be recognized for being half-and-half. <b>That's what defines their niche</b>. You are not some random mortal who acquired a spell or artifact - nor even an Endowment by a God. You inherited it. It's as close to being Dragon-Blooded as non-Patricians can get (except, instead of being a symbol of stability - you're a reminder of the former-rulers and aspiring-warlords).<br /> <br /> Again.<br /> <br /> This isn't about <i>magical power</i>. That belongs to the (X)-Blooded whose (type)-abilities are all magical and their parents usually spirits.<br /> <br /> This is about <i>political power</i>. A Moon-Born didn't acquire &quot;kewl powerz&quot; over night - their existence implies a decades long presence of the Anathema who create monsters, prey on settlements and seek eternal war. A &quot;Golden Child&quot; didn't get a kiss on the forehead by Sol as a gift - their existence implies a decades long presence of the once-rulers of Creation's mightiest empire making a come-back.<br /> <br /> <b>Get me?</b><br /> <br /> Viewing the Exalted as symbols of Empire - and humanity as natives - <i>the name given to the children of half-and-half heritage</i> makes a <b>direct</b> allusion to real-world comparisons. World history is <b>not</b> American history, in which <i>half-and-half means you get lumped with the lower-class</i>. There is a fantastic <i>tension</i> in having both sides of your heritage potentially admire and distrust you. The Haitian example comes to mind most readily (the Caribbean is my jam) but it occurs elsewhere too. <b>Neither heritage</b> is homogenous in how they treat the <i>half-and-half heritage offspring</i>.<br /> <br /> I just don't see how you can divorce them from their heritages. The setting - itself - serves to <i>hunt them down</i> (due to their heritage) or seek to control/capture/use them (due to their power). Even if they (the character) wants to abandon it all - the setting will at some point deny them that. <hr /><br /> It might also be telling that I favor Tieflings and Half-Orcs. I <b>enjoy</b> seeing and dealing with these real-world conflict-parallels (whereas an Aasimar or Half-Elf is kind of lame to me). My Tieflings and Half-Orcs are often <b>unhappy</b> with the way they are stereotyped and treated - but that's <b>precisely why</b> I pick those races (since those stories wouldn't be as valid from other backgrounds).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T16:11:25-07:00","id":1224830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224426#post1224426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't do this. This board is predominantly made up of English speaking Americans and the term &quot;half-caste&quot; is offensive to many (most) for a variety of reasons. I understand you don't grasp the nuance because you are not a native American English speaker but the fact remains it is an offensive term (as are the terms &quot;Sambo&quot;, &quot;mulatto&quot; etc.)<br /> Those terms were used to denigrate, diminish and dehumanize entire classes and races of people. So while the term &quot;half-caste&quot; may be accurate from an in game perspective you are not conducting this discussion in game, you are discussing it in an environment where many people have already made you aware the term is inappropriate to use. The operating rule here (the forum) is that if someone tells you something is offensive you do not get to tell them it is not and then continue to use the offending term. That is not respecting the conversation Please understand this as I do not wish to have to take any further action beyond this post. Thank you.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is news to me. (sighs)<br /> <br /> and im a native english speaker.<br /> <br /> Are the term's Slave, Peasant, Serf. tolerated?<br /> <br /> or Casteless? (or will the lunars have to be renamed)<br /> <br /> They were used to denigrate real people too once.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>This isn't the place to debate an administrator's ruling, take a week off.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-04-2018, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T16:26:53-07:00","id":1224832,"title":"","content":"So my thoughts on Golden Children and Starblessed respectively.<br /> <br /> Golden Children are born to the perfection of the Unconquered Sun, at the low levels I see everyday superpowers like being born without birth defects and never taking sick days. Such passive perfection rounds them rather than sharpens them like a Solar Exaltation does. They lack their Solar parent's incredible aptitudes but they either never fail or recover from it very gracefully.<br /> <br /> Starblessed have fate manipulating powers but without the administrative access to the Loom of Fate that makes many of their parent's powers work. Instead the only fate a Starblessed has to play around with is their own, this often means they've got insights into future ordained events and how to bring those about while some are acutely aware of their lifespan as it counts down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T16:50:28-07:00","id":1224838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224830#post1224830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is news to me. (sighs)<br /> <br /> and im a native english speaker.<br /> <br /> Are the term's Slave, Peasant, Serf. tolerated?<br /> <br /> or Casteless? (or will the lunars have to be renamed)<br /> <br /> They were used to denigrate real people too once.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If you want to get your posting privileges suspended arguing with the forum admin is a quick way to get the job done. Here's your official warning, drop the issue. If you don't like the moderation use the contact us link in my signature.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T00:59:24-07:00","id":1224916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224824#post1224824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know many real-life half-demons or half-ghosts or half-demigods. The second you can wield magic to make problems go away, you fail to be 100% human in the eyes of the world around you (for comparison, see Marvel Mutants).</div> </div> </div> </div>Marvel was trying to make comparisons to various civil rights causes, and ultimately failed in a number of ways, such as persecuted people not having magical powers, as well as a noticeably large number of Professor X's gifted youngsters being rich and white. Exalted, meanwhile, has a very different presentation, and tells us outright that if the Exalted weren't human, they wouldn't have become Exalted, so they're quite definitely human. Any opinions to the contrary are in-character, and also objectively wrong by what the precepts of the setting have handed down.<br /> <br /> They also lack ironclad demographic links. They just happen among a teeming throng of all of humanity. Even the Dragon-Blooded don't belong to one ethnic identity, even if a lot of them are politically unified in the Realm, Lookshy, and with the Forest Witches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More to the point, <i>the children of half-and-half heritage</i> <b>should </b>be recognized for being half-and-half. <b>That's what defines their niche</b>. You are not some random mortal who acquired a spell or artifact - nor even an Endowment by a God. You inherited it. It's as close to being Dragon-Blooded as non-Patricians can get (except, instead of being a symbol of stability - you're a reminder of the former-rulers and aspiring-warlords).<br /> <br /> Again.<br /> <br /> This isn't about <i>magical power</i>. That belongs to the (X)-Blooded whose (type)-abilities are all magical and their parents usually spirits.<br /> <br /> This is about <i>political power</i>. A Moon-Born didn't acquire &quot;kewl powerz&quot; over night - their existence implies a decades long presence of the Anathema who create monsters, prey on settlements and seek eternal war. A &quot;Golden Child&quot; didn't get a kiss on the forehead by Sol as a gift - their existence implies a decades long presence of the once-rulers of Creation's mightiest empire making a come-back.<br /> <br /> <b>Get me?</b><br /> <br /> Viewing the Exalted as symbols of Empire - and humanity as natives - <i>the name given to the children of half-and-half heritage</i> makes a <b>direct</b> allusion to real-world comparisons. World history is <b>not</b> American history, in which <i>half-and-half means you get lumped with the lower-class</i>. There is a fantastic <i>tension</i> in having both sides of your heritage potentially admire and distrust you. The Haitian example comes to mind most readily (the Caribbean is my jam) but it occurs elsewhere too. <b>Neither heritage</b> is homogenous in how they treat the <i>half-and-half heritage offspring</i>.<br /> <br /> I just don't see how you can divorce them from their heritages. The setting - itself - serves to <i>hunt them down</i> (due to their heritage) or seek to control/capture/use them (due to their power). Even if they (the character) wants to abandon it all - the setting will at some point deny them that. <hr /><br /> It might also be telling that I favor Tieflings and Half-Orcs. I <b>enjoy</b> seeing and dealing with these real-world conflict-parallels (whereas an Aasimar or Half-Elf is kind of lame to me). My Tieflings and Half-Orcs are often <b>unhappy</b> with the way they are stereotyped and treated - but that's <b>precisely why</b> I pick those races (since those stories wouldn't be as valid from other backgrounds). </div> </div> </div>Exalted, particularly the ones that give rise to God-Blooded offspring when their Essence is particularly high, have already-existent ethnic and cultural identities. They were born humans, and if they aren't from the Scarlet Dynasty or Lookshy gentes, they didn't expect to become Exalted. Even upon taking the Second Breath, their identification changes in that their profession, role, or personal qualities become the strongest thing about them. Being God-blooded born of Celestial, Abyssal, or Infernal extraction is not a form of divided ethnic identity, but of being the child of someone important and living in their shadow. Their blood and cultural heritage is not as important as what their specific parents did; not every orc or tiefling is a dragon-slayer or punches out archdevils, but in this case, that would be the closest equivalent to be had in D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T08:33:34-07:00","id":1224963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224916#post1224916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marvel was trying to make comparisons to various civil rights causes, and ultimately failed in a number of ways, such as persecuted people not having magical powers, as well as a noticeably large number of Professor X's gifted youngsters being rich and white. Exalted, meanwhile, has a very different presentation, and tells us outright that if the Exalted weren't human, they wouldn't have become Exalted, so they're quite definitely human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if you missed my point (because I failed to articulate adequately) or if this is a deliberate dodge (trying to retwist things into irrelevant tangent about minority representation) - but....<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224916#post1224916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Any opinions to the contrary are in-character</span>, and also objectively wrong by what the precepts of the setting have handed down.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>PRECISELY</b>. And where on earth does your character exist - <b>at any point</b> - if not in-character?<br /> <br /> Neither Mystique nor the Moon-Born have the privilege of a white-room in which they can be judged for personality and be deemed nice people.<br /> <br /> They both exist in a world that <b>will </b>see them as monsters, <b>will</b> persecute them and <b>will </b>drag them into setting politics.<br /> <hr /><br /> All the (X)-blooded offer a (in theory) possibility for humanity. In one way or another, mortals have ways to enlighten their essence - and one of them is to seek endowment - and thus, it's feasible for build cults with the promise of empowerment. The Immaculate Dogma even tries to deal with them (such that you can even recruit them into the order). There are even canon Dragon-Blooded (like that air-aspect) of mixed heritage (I believe he had a &quot;storm demon&quot; in his ancestry, which was the explanation for his precocious pre-Exaltation elemental effects).<br /> <br /> <i>The children of mixed heritage between Exalt and man</i> are <b>not that</b>. You're either born one - or not. You are simultaneously privileged and reviled. Exalts and Gods will look down on you as a pampered play-thing who is unlikely to Exalt despite all the advantages you're born with - mortals will look at you as a demi-godly, a wannabe-tyrant-without-teeth, who by power and position never endures the hardships they do.<br /> <br /> Since mechanically, you access your parent's charm-sets - some might not even differentiate you from a legitimate Exalt (and don't be tempted by white-room, omniscient-narrator, metagaming perspective to argue that &quot;that is objectively wrong, because....&quot; ... in the middle of a battlefield, if you summon golden armor or shapeshift into dog, your enemies will simply go &quot;Exalt!&quot; and send the warstrider).<br /> <br /> Use your phrase for <b>anything in the setting</b>.<ul><li>&quot;I want to create Solar Exalt who is nice and kind and loves everyone!&quot;</li> <li>&gt;&gt; Solar Exalted <b>will</b> be hunted down by the Wyld Hunt as demon-possessed monsters</li> <li>&quot;But I'm not a monster!&quot;<br /> &gt;&gt; The people in the setting think otherwise.</li> <li>&quot;Any opinions to the contrary are in-character, and also objectively wrong by what the precepts of the setting have handed down!&quot;</li> <li>&gt;&gt; <b>Nevertheless</b>, Solar Exalted <b>will</b> be hunted down by the Wyld Hunt as monsters</li> </ul>Do you see how that works?<br /> <br /> The world <b>will </b>judge you. For things you had no control over. And it is likely unfair. <i>So roll with the punches</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224916#post1224916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the Dragon-Blooded don't belong to one ethnic identity, even if a lot of them are politically unified in the Realm, Lookshy, and with the Forest Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do they lack ethnic identity? They speak a common language, they have a common religion, they are part of a joint empire and they're very, very, very clearly related by blood.<br /> <br /> If you're referring to phenotypes - what color hair or eye or skin someone has - that is <b>hardly</b> an ethnic identifier. A Hindu won't confuse a Breton with a Brahmin nor a Swahili with a Shudra. I'm Hispanic - and I can differentiate a Dominican from a Puerto Rican, a Columbian from a Chilean and <i>phenotype</i> is the <i>least</i> useful trait to identify each other ethnically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224916#post1224916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted, particularly the ones that give rise to God-Blooded offspring when their Essence is particularly high, have already-existent ethnic and cultural identities. They were born humans, and if they aren't from the Scarlet Dynasty or Lookshy gentes, they didn't expect to become Exalted. Even upon taking the Second Breath, their identification changes in that their profession, role, or personal qualities become the strongest thing about them. Being God-blooded born of Celestial, Abyssal, or Infernal extraction is not a form of divided ethnic identity, but of being the child of someone important and living in their shadow. Their blood and cultural heritage is not as important as what their specific parents did; not every orc or tiefling is a dragon-slayer or punches out archdevils, but in this case, that would be the closest equivalent to be had in D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that Exalts won't lose their pre-existing identities. I disagree to the extent you think their Exalted-identity falls by the way side.<br /> <br /> The point <b>remains</b> that the <b>write-up in the book</b> makes clear that <b>all</b> Golden-Children (regardless of ethnicity) were <b>slaughtered. </b>From Gem to Whiterun, regional differences didn't matter. Switching teams didn't matter, and I quote:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;<i>Half-Castes who surrendered or sided with the Dragon-Blooded were next. Unwilling to risk a Half-Caste uprising, the Terrestrials mercilessly slaughtered every Half-Caste they could find\u2014enemy and ally, infant and adul</i>t.&quot;</div>And when the Wyld Hunt comes looking, they make a great morale-boosting <i>warm-up</i> while in pursuit of their parents. <b>In this setting</b>, anyone who dreads, hates or fears the Solar Exalted - and wants to make them a pawn - <i>targets you too</i>. And I quote:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;<i>Still, most Half-Castes must take care when traveling on their own lest they be slain by the enemies of the Celestial Exalts</i>&quot;</div>And why would anyone think this of them? Let's see what inspiring things the <i>mixed heritage character </i>might say in order to <i>terrify</i> the locals with the prospect of war:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;<i>My father wishes you all to know that the Chosen have returned. We will no longer allow the tyranny of the Realm to rule here. We will build a new golden age on the ashes of the Terrestrial betrayers. Gaze into my eyes, and you will glimpse our glorious future.</i>&quot;</div><hr /><br /> <br /> Nothing forbids me from rolling up an urban Moon-Born from Nexus with no clue as to her heritage -- but the <b>second</b> I learn Deadly Beastman Transformation and Finding the Spirit\u2019s Shape, I <b>cannot pretend</b> the setting has &quot;no right&quot; to impose it's stereotypes upon my character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 06-05-2018, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T08:51:58-07:00","id":1224967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1223983#post1223983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Fae-Blooded</b> are more lackluster - the ability to resist Wyld mutation is pretty niche - and they don't really apotheosize into anything. Like God-Blooded, they're merely &quot;human - but more awesome!&quot; with no strong signature trick (unless you're exposed to the Wyld a lot.... but the <i>majority</i> of the Wyld is on the outskirts of creation, meaning you're the <i>most</i> useful in places where <i>no one cares</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ordinary mortals are <i>way</i> cooler than Faebloods. (In 2e)<br /> They have larger motepools, can respire essence in creation, can learn sorcery or necromancy, can power quest in the wyld (Can't power quest if it can't mutate you), and (while they can't acquire any native charms) don't have the humiliating limitation of being unable to learn native charms without getting their supernatural parent or someone like them to enslave them by forging one of their virtues into an item which said fae owns...which allows a faeblood to use strictly inferior, exclusively illusionary versions of most of their parent's charms, and blocks off any charm with permanent glamour effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T09:19:53-07:00","id":1224973,"title":"","content":"I think the succinct response is simply:<br /> <br /> - Yes, you can play your unique, special, snowflake <i>mixed heritage character of Exalt and Man</i>.<br /> <br /> - However, <i>no one in the setting</i> is required to acknowledge, respect or value your unique, special identity. Their write-up repeats, several times, that faction-foes <i>don't care</i> who you are. 99.999% of the setting population doesn't know you, doesn't want to, and in a think-fast-or-die scenario will judge you based on what creepy unnatural magic you're tossing around. If you shapeshift, you'll be threated like Lunar Anathema.<br /> <br /> - This applies to <i>mixed heritage children of Exalts and Men.</i><br /> <br /> - This applies to <i>Exalts themselves</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224967#post1224967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ordinary mortals are <i>way</i> cooler than Faebloods. (In 2e)</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (this forum needs a &quot;mind blown&quot; emoji).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 06-05-2018, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T09:59:05-07:00","id":1224992,"title":"","content":"I've had the most difficulty with the children of Abyssal and Infernal Exalted due to some pretty core disagreements on what the play experience of their parents should be.<br /> <br /> Shadewalkers:<br /> If the Starblessed in an auspicious child who knows their purpose in life, the Shadewalker is the child who knows they shouldn't exist and is probably being ushered towards a dark purpose. They're a walking ill omen but the bad luck never seems to fall upon them as horrible accidents befall their enemies and even their allies don't come away unscathed.<br /> <br /> Grandchosen (based purely on 2e):<br /> Infernal Exalted don't have their own charms until making the jump to Devil Tiger and without a Solar Exaltation Primordial essence doesn't like to share in the same host. Meaning the end result will be a Yozis' spiritual grandchild. There's immediate similarities with Mortal Akuma but I'd argue the main area of interest for a Grandchosen is that they can be born with the personality warping Yozi charms. Since people who want to explore the psychology of for example, Murder is Meat often has to ignore the fact that the character in question started out within the behaviour range of a normal person until they said to themselves \u201cwouldn\u2019t my life be easier if I only saw mortals as a food source?\u201d<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T10:24:09-07:00","id":1225006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224963#post1224963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they lack ethnic identity? They speak a common language, they have a common religion, they are part of a joint empire and they're very, very, very clearly related by blood.<br /> <br /> If you're referring to phenotypes - what color hair or eye or skin someone has - that is <b>hardly</b> an ethnic identifier. A Hindu won't confuse a Breton with a Brahmin nor a Swahili with a Shudra. I'm Hispanic - and I can differentiate a Dominican from a Puerto Rican, a Columbian from a Chilean and <i>phenotype</i> is the <i>least</i> useful trait to identify each other ethnically.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that Exalts won't lose their pre-existing identities. I disagree to the extent you think their Exalted-identity falls by the way side.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not all dragon blooded are Immaculates (The Forest Witches)<br /> Not all dragonblooded are members of the realm (Lookshy, Outcaste grous).<br /> Not all dragonbloode are related to the Empress. (Lookshy)<br /> Not all dragonblooded speak the same language (Why would those outside the realm speak realm? Or any of its varients?)<br /> Not all dragonblooded are part of the Realm. This seems to be the big point of confusion here. Lookshy <i>does not</i> consider itself a part of the Realm, and is culturally distinct. Parsaad, a part of the realm, is culturally (the term I take you to mean by ethnically) distinct in almost every way (Different religious belief system, differnt governing structure, different power structure, etc).<br /> <br /> Broadly Exalted and nonExaltd can't exist as Imperial and Natives because the Exlatd aren't some collective empire imposing on a native population. Maybe in 2e's first age, that abyss that brought us jealous dragonblood concubine families and dragonblooded treated as expendable for Wyld Millitary Drill that would hold. But in 3e its not a tenable position. <br /> Especially as it's unlikely Xborn are going to get charms of their parents.<br /> Especialy as Lunar Children are noted in 3e's core as some of the champions of thier realms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T10:45:24-07:00","id":1225013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224963#post1224963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't tell if you missed my point (because I failed to articulate adequately) or if this is a deliberate dodge (trying to retwist things into irrelevant tangent about minority representation) - but....</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm brushing X-Men off as relevant because it's in an entirely different genre. Creation is pulp revival swords and sorcery meant to have a much more antique feel and lower stress level for players than a comic book series that can't even really stay consistent about powers and how the public views them. Mutants are scary, but somehow, all the other character types from the Marvel meta-setting get a free pass and public admiration, albeit occasionally with J. Jonah Jameson making &quot;Spiderman: Threat or Menace?&quot; thinkpieces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>PRECISELY</b>. And where on earth does your character exist - <b>at any point</b> - if not in-character? </div> </div> </div>And, in spite of being fictional characters, a number of them come away with no notion that they're disconnected from humanity or meant to be. Lyta is an exception; the fact that she was raised in Dynastic culture is the reason why she suddenly thinks that she can lord over the &quot;mortals&quot; now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither Mystique nor the Moon-Born have the privilege of a white-room in which they can be judged for personality and be deemed nice people. </div> </div> </div>[Narrows eyes at choice of Marvel character]<br /> <br /> It doesn't need to be a white room, though. The prior editions, while pushing this, also made plenty of room for Celestials to cut loose and be judged by their actions alone, while the Abyssals had the company of the dead and the Infernals of demons and the Yozis - or of the same places that Solars did. There was a rather lengthy essay on how being a Green Sun Prince isn't grounds for a summary execution by Solars that they run into, so one presumes that Solars and possibly also Lunars would have it way, way easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They both exist in a world that <b>will </b>see them as monsters, <b>will</b> persecute them and <b>will </b>drag them into setting politics. </div> </div> </div>For one thing, the entire setting doesn't actually entirely see them as monsters; there's no shortage of glowing praise in the outside perspective chapters of the old 1e caste books when they help people. For another thing, the people who do think that they're monsters do so because they think that the Anathema were people of weak character who invited demons in or, for the &quot;in the know&quot; dodge, that they possess power they shouldn't and will inevitably go mad, destroying everything, especially what the Anathema themselves loved. Possession of a few is not exactly something that fuels an identity of culture, community ties, and blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All the (X)-blooded offer a (in theory) possibility for humanity. In one way or another, mortals have ways to enlighten their essence - and one of them is to seek endowment - and thus, it's feasible for build cults with the promise of empowerment. The Immaculate Dogma even tries to deal with them (such that you can even recruit them into the order). There are even canon Dragon-Blooded (like that air-aspect) of mixed heritage (I believe he had a &quot;storm demon&quot; in his ancestry, which was the explanation for his precocious pre-Exaltation elemental effects). </div> </div> </div>Her ancestry; Ledaal Kebok Coren is a she.<br /> <br /> Demons, for their own part, were never human, and second-circle demons were born from the foreheads of the third-circles, representing their drives. That's not really an ethnic identity, being one of the seven most important impulses of a being born of a vast, cosmic horror, and unique in your expression of power. It has been compared to being part of an organization, though, as in the &quot;Yozi as company&quot; analogy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The children of mixed heritage between Exalt and man</i> are <b>not that</b>. You're either born one - or not. You are simultaneously privileged and reviled. Exalts and Gods will look down on you as a pampered play-thing who is unlikely to Exalt despite all the advantages you're born with - mortals will look at you as a demi-godly, a wannabe-tyrant-without-teeth, who by power and position never endures the hardships they do. </div> </div> </div>Being a godling descended from someone who got a one-off shot of power still isn't really comparable to having mixed ethnic heritage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since mechanically, you access your parent's charm-sets </div> </div> </div>Maybe in the past two editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> some might not even differentiate you from a legitimate Exalt (and don't be tempted by white-room, omniscient-narrator, metagaming perspective to argue that &quot;that is objectively wrong, because....&quot; ... in the middle of a battlefield, if you summon golden armor or shapeshift into dog, your enemies will simply go &quot;Exalt!&quot; and send the warstrider). </div> </div> </div>No, they're not likely to know the difference at first glance, or even at the tenth. There's another thread about how using powers doesn't automatically give you away; Demethus manages to tell people that he won a bet with a spirit and brush off all of his feats of prowess, so god-blooded can probably get by even easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Use your phrase for <b>anything in the setting</b>.[*]&quot;I want to create Solar Exalt who is nice and kind and loves everyone!&quot;[*]&gt;&gt; Solar Exalted <b>will</b> be hunted down by the Wyld Hunt as demon-possessed monsters[*]&quot;But I'm not a monster!&quot;<br /> &gt;&gt; The people in the setting think otherwise.[*]&quot;Any opinions to the contrary are in-character, and also objectively wrong by what the precepts of the setting have handed down!&quot;[*]&gt;&gt; <b>Nevertheless</b>, Solar Exalted <b>will</b> be hunted down by the Wyld Hunt as monsters<br /> Do you see how that works?<br /> <br /> The world <b>will </b>judge you. For things you had no control over. And it is likely unfair. <i>So roll with the punches</i>. </div> </div> </div>Already went over this point a few paragraphs up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do they lack ethnic identity? They speak a common language, they have a common religion, they are part of a joint empire and they're very, very, very clearly related by blood. </div> </div> </div>They're related by dint of being Dragons' Chosen, which is like sharing one or two traits that may or may not be visible to others. Everything else is up in the air; Lookshy has a bunch of different linguistic groups, in fact, judging by the names of Gentes and their imperators. Additionally, various houses have adopted or kept very different cultures, and are in the process of splitting apart from their culture very violently, just as all the Dragon-Blooded of the Shogunate did before them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're referring to phenotypes - what color hair or eye or skin someone has - that is <b>hardly</b> an ethnic identifier. A Hindu won't confuse a Breton with a Brahmin nor a Swahili with a Shudra. I'm Hispanic - and I can differentiate a Dominican from a Puerto Rican, a Columbian from a Chilean and <i>phenotype</i> is the <i>least</i> useful trait to identify each other ethnically. </div> </div> </div>The large collections of Dragon-Blooded came from all over Creation when the Scarlet Empress and Lookshy went about building their redoubts and hunching down to fight each other; as such, their blood is going to differ way more than that.<br /> <br /> Also, weren't you arguing for exactly this as a way of differentiating people in a different thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree with you that Exalts won't lose their pre-existing identities. I disagree to the extent you think their Exalted-identity falls by the way side. </div> </div> </div>Well, again, the setting has some ironclad assumptions about this, and it treats Exalted as a cross-section of people from across Creation. That's why we have a lot of analogies about comparing Exalted to gold or silver medalists (the latter in every field), and why they're known as heroes and champions. They're like winners of prestigious awards for arts or sciences, or revolutionaries who changed the world.<br /> <br /> Never through dint of blood identity, though. That's not the way things were set up, what with the reincarnating power and all. When reincarnation gets involved, blood tends to fall by the wayside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point <b>remains</b> that the <b>write-up in the book</b> makes clear that <b>all</b> Golden-Children (regardless of ethnicity) </div> </div> </div>Yes. They had some political importance as the social elites' children, where the elites were from all across the world. They did not have a shared ethnic identity, but rather that they were all demigods with a great deal of political importance. Lots of Dragon-Blooded were probably from the same ethnic groups, making it a purely political revolution. Think of it as being like all of the then-world leaders' kids being knocked off, rather than an entirely different people unto themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> were <b>slaughtered. </b>From Gem to Whiterun, regional differences didn't matter. Switching teams didn't matter, and I quote:[INDENT]&quot;<i>Half-Castes who surrendered or sided with the Dragon-Blooded were next. Unwilling to risk a Half-Caste uprising, the Terrestrials mercilessly slaughtered every Half-Caste they could find\u2014enemy and ally, infant and adul</i>t.&quot;<br /> <br /> And when the Wyld Hunt comes looking, they make a great morale-boosting <i>warm-up</i> while in pursuit of their parents. <b>In this setting</b>, anyone who dreads, hates or fears the Solar Exalted - and wants to make them a pawn - <i>targets you too</i>. And I quote: &quot;<i>Still, most Half-Castes must take care when traveling on their own lest they be slain by the enemies of the Celestial Exalts</i>&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's from an old edition where there were magical character type detectors. Those don't really exist anymore, and it was also a tremendous leap even at the time to assume that such folk would know what they are if not raised by their parents. No one gives out Occult for free, and no one can really hand out concrete assurances aside from the Incarna themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And why would anyone think this of them? Let's see what inspiring things the <i>mixed heritage character </i>might say in order to <i>terrify</i> the locals with the prospect of war:[INDENT]&quot;[I]My father wishes you all to know that the Chosen have returned. We will no longer allow the tyranny of the Realm to rule here. We will build a new golden age on the ashes of the Terrestrial betrayers. Gaze into my eyes, and you will glimpse our glorious future. <hr /> </div> </div> </div>Magical inheritance is not the same thing as ethnic inheritance. This is another precept that the setting decided on. The choice of epithet for God-Blooded descendants of powerful Exalted was a mistake on par with the name for Garou born of Garou - increasingly, it sounds like it was someone's attempt at a really flat joke that didn't even fit with the subject matter, what with Exalted not being distinguishable from other members of their ethnic group on any traditionally ethnic grounds and those particular Garou being born of non-mixed, completely werewolf blood. And that's why the God-Blooded born of Exalted are getting named something else. To try and keep it would just wrap the setting up in failed attempts to be clever, and an important purpose of EX3 was to cut through that Gordian Knot of jumbled canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing forbids me from rolling up an urban Moon-Born from Nexus with no clue as to her heritage -- but the <b>second</b> I learn Deadly Beastman Transformation and Finding the Spirit\u2019s Shape, I <b>cannot pretend</b> the setting has &quot;no right&quot; to impose it's stereotypes upon my character. </div> </div> </div>Sure you do. Most people don't have Occult, and they sure as hell don't have a magic detector for character types in EX3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-05-2018, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T10:52:56-07:00","id":1225015,"title":"","content":"By all accounts, 3e godbloods will have a more or less levelled off power (on a tier by tier basis). Their parents really add flavour more than anything. <br /> <br /> So, there might be a power that lets a GB turn into an animal. That'll work the same whether your daddy is a lunar or a fae or an animal god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T13:51:49-07:00","id":1225074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224992#post1224992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had the most difficulty with the children of Abyssal and Infernal Exalted due to some pretty core disagreements on what the play experience of their parents should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm intrigued - what disagreements?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1224992#post1224992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since people who want to explore the psychology of for example, Murder is Meat often has to ignore the fact that the character in question started out within the behaviour range of a normal person until they said to themselves \u201cwouldn\u2019t my life be easier if I only saw mortals as a food source?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I always took it more as ignoring the nature of charm acquisition. <br /> <br /> Less &quot;I'm acquiring an object/item/tool&quot; that warps my mind and fuels me off extras.<br /> <br /> More &quot;Killing rabbits for meat is no different than killing extras for motes. I always enjoyed the slaughter - but now I <i>truly</i> grok it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225006#post1225006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all dragon blooded are Immaculates (The Forest Witches)<br /> Not all dragonblooded are members of the realm (Lookshy, Outcaste groups).<br /> Not all dragonblooded are related to the Empress. (Lookshy)<br /> Not all dragonblooded speak the same language (Why would those outside the realm speak realm? Or any of its varients?)<br /> Not all dragonblooded are part of the Realm. This seems to be the big point of confusion here.</div> </div> </div> </div>My intent was to respond to &quot;even if they belong to the Realm&quot;. I'm not saying &quot;all Dragon-Blooded are part of a mono-culture&quot; - I was saying &quot;I certainly consider Dynasts part of an ethnic/religious/cultural group.<br /> <br /> However, my broad-post point remains with your other examples.<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Touched in a Realm tributary who uses obvious powers will likely be mistaken for a Dragon-Blooded (and treated as such) by allies and enemies. <b>That same</b> Dragon-Touched then flees to Lookshy territory? An observing Lunars will group the guy with the firey-sword as &quot;one of those guys from Lookshy&quot;. You don't need to be a member of a homogenous group in order to be treated that way.<br /> <br /> <i>Whether you like to or not</i>, all Exalted-derived-children are going to be held accountable for their forebears. <b>Even the text</b> points out that Sun-kids who <i>helped the Dragon-Blooded</i> were <b>still slaughtered</b> just to be safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225013#post1225013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epic</div> </div> </div> </div>I've enjoyed your response - and responding to it - but am tucking it into a spoiler due to length, lol. And I tried to shorten it 3x! Kudos for giving me so much to punch my keyboard over.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>re: Editions</b><br /> Yes, everything I cite is 2E - but until 3E provides revised material, I don't see anything inaccurate in citing it. I actually <b>welcome</b> a revamp in 3E - but you can't judge a conversation without looking to the source.<br /> <br /> <b>re: Powers in Battle</b><br /> There is a reason I <i>specifically </i>used examples of &quot;summoning golden armor&quot; or &quot;shapeshift into a dog&quot; and (later) &quot;Deadly Beastman Transformation&quot;. I appreciate your effort, but no one here is blind to the utility of subtle charm use. If you enter DBT near an Immaculate Monk, <i>they'll guess you're Anathema</i> and that's sufficient.<br /> <br /> <b>re: Genetics &amp; Dragon-Blooded</b><br /> I disagree with your claim that &quot;one or two traits&quot; unify them. Each Aspect has <b>specific </b>traits tied to their personality. It's not mere &quot;elemental magic&quot;..... it's your temperament, the skills you're good at (which will influence personality and behavior) and what kind of magic you excel at. Part of their own <i>religion</i> is featuring mythic heroes who embody values to temper and restrain their elemental excesses.<br /> <br /> So you can be the &quot;nicest, calmest Fire Aspect ever&quot; - people will <b>still</b> stereotype and figure &quot;oh, but I bet he's a powder keg! they say you have to watch out for the quiet ones, I bet he has a fiery temper!&quot;<br /> <br /> Note that the-Children-of-Exalts <b>also</b> get similar descriptions (in their favor seasons, favorite time of day, etc). You can't just give humans &quot;the power to see your future&quot; or &quot;the power to be ridiculously fit and hot&quot; or &quot;the power to spread death&quot; and not see it color their temperaments. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>re: Mutants</b><br /> Biology is scary, hard-to-control, eugenicist - one comic had a teen whose gift was <i>spontaneous mass genocide</i>. Mutants and children-of-Exalts are in a category of <i>monsters</i> who are better than all of us <i>by default</i> and we can never be like them.<br /> <br /> Technology implies intelligence and resources - so smart people &amp; government. Nukes stay safely in storage usually. Ironman and Captain America are in a category of <i>human aspiration</i>, and we've seen other heroes in ironman suits or super-soldier programs.<br /> <br /> <b>re: Air Aspects</b><br /> Thanks! I always confuse Air Aspects with Tepet Arada (he was a hellion as a child, but I guess not infernal).<br /> <br /> <b>re: Ethnic Identity</b><br /> I agree that X-Blooded aren't an ethnic anything. Gods &amp; Demons are too varied &amp; hyper-regional - even the most fecund has yet to forge an empire that conquers humanity. A God-Blood of a Rabbit-Deity might be an emissary for their parent (who, as a god, is merely doing its job).<br /> <br /> The Children-of-Exalts are a different baggage. Lunar? Silver Pact, Beastmen, Cannibalism! Abyssal? Deathlords, Undead, Necromancy! A Moon-Born of a Rabbit-Lunar is a potential spy, warrior and harbinger of doom. A Death-Born in Nexus is going to worry people who know of Thorns.<br /> <br /> And yes, with (in-group) perspective, I <b>like </b>creating more niche groups. I like detailed, non-cliched identities. If you want to play a Moon-Born Immaculate Monk? Dope!<br /> <br /> But from an (out-group) perspective, we don't usually get to determine how we are stereotyped. If your Moon-Born learns Deadly Beastman Transformation to turn into a half-River-Dragon, and a local Abyssal has a grudge against the Silver Pact, the Abyssal is unlikely to engage you in dialogue on the Immaculate Texts - it's surprise-murder and move on.<br /> <br /> Mind you - I <b>hate</b> the Silver Pact in 2E for many of the faux-cultural traits it pretends at.<br /> <br /> But when I play a Casteless Lunar, I <i>cannot get upset</i> when other Lunar-players imply they'd be doing me a favor by &quot;rescuing me&quot; from my circle; nor can I get upset if my character has to jump a few extra hoops to prove my loyalty to the Lover Clad; nor can I get upset if she get associated with beastmen (which she loathes) or if people think it's okay to disrespect ghosts (ancestor cult faith for her). My Casteless Lunar has <i>no more control</i> over regional stereotypes than a Moon-Born bastard. <br /> <br /> My solution, inevitably, is to play on <i>other stereotypes</i> and blend in with my Abyssal Circle - but that's still operating in the (out-group) world of regional stereotypes (that are often lazy and wrong), not (in-group) perspective (which is where my circle gets to know each other).<br /> <br /> <b>re: Disconnection from Humanity</b><br /> You're talking about 5-year-old Solar Exalts who spent most of their lives as humans.<br /> <br /> You're not talking about 1,000 year old Lunars, 100-year old Terrestrial Exalts, or even 10 year old Children-of-Exalts (who seem to be prodigies from birth). I'd wager the Star-Kid's premonitions will make them grow-up feeling wiser/smarter than other people, the Moon-Kid's aptitudes will make them grow-up feeling stronger/sexier, the Death-Kid's aptitudes will make them into some variant of death-spreading maniac or avenger. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225013#post1225013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magical inheritance is not the same thing as ethnic inheritance. This is another precept that the setting decided on. The choice of epithet for God-Blooded descendants of powerful Exalted was a mistake on par with the name for Garou born of Garou -</div> </div> </div> </div>At best, we can only agree to disagree. <br /> <br /> You calling them &quot;God-Blooded&quot; is a misnomer to begin with. <br /> <br /> Secondly, their official name is a reference to British / Hindi offspring. <b>Guess what?</b> <b>Both</b> lineages were empires judging people by which side they're on - and then you have <i>children of mixed heritage</i> that neither side could embrace. It's a great word. Great reference. <br /> <br /> Calling them &quot;Star-Born&quot; or &quot;Sun-Sons&quot; or &quot;Moon-Maidens&quot; just reeks of hippie spiritual garbage. It's &quot;lets make Essence 1 Exalts who are a bit incompetent&quot;. I use the terms but I think most of them are silly as hell, since each one is an individual. Why call them &quot;Star-Born&quot; if so few even exist? I already have enough names for prophets, seers, viziers, Sidereal children, etc.<br /> <br /> Calling them <i>their name in the text</i> <b>immediately </b>invoked history, empires, revolutions, politics. <br /> <br /> I'm not going to ask the writers to &quot;not use the word Kahn because it glorifies Genghis Khan, who committed mass genocide&quot; - nah, I'll appreciate the reference.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to ask them to &quot;delete Lilith because it's an offensive religious artifact that demeans female sexuality&quot; - nah, I'll appreciate the reference.<br /> <br /> A few months back in Magic the Gathering, IXALAN had a whole Vampire Conquistadors vs Dinosaur-Riding Aztecs vs Mayan Mermen vs Mixed Race Pirates... <i>i loved it</i>. There is <b>plenty of space</b> to make reference to real-world events and peoples without needing to be offended (if anything, I was shocked at how much of the lore resonated with real-life parallels - their forums wanted the Spanish to be <i>more monstrous</i>, but no, they gave all factions a fair shake).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225013#post1225013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure you do. Most people don't have Occult, and they sure as hell don't have a magic detector for character types in EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I word this vaguely?<br /> <br /> I explicitly listed 2 shapeshifting charms - so I could transform into an octopus or Ursula.<br /> <br /> Why on earth would I demand an Occult roll from someone who sees me shapeshifting? They can <i>see</i> I'm magical and go tell a monk.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T14:27:32-07:00","id":1225083,"title":"","content":"Your basic understanding and justification rests on the notion that :<br /> Exalted Children will use parent charms (Devs have indicated they wont.)<br /> Dragon Touched will be a thing(...they really shouldnt be as that makes no sense to begin with).<br /> That we can meaningfully compare the Exalted host to a colonial empire (we can't). The phrase is inaccurate in addition to offensive: What natives are the Solars oppressing? What colonial empire exists of the lunars? If anything, Moon Born seem to be champions in Lunar domains opposing colonial powers. We do have a parallel for colonial imperialism. Its the Realm. If you want stories of chractrs torn between empire and people, maybe explore the Realm and the idea of a member of an oppressd satrapy exalting as a dragonblooded? <br /> <br /> this isn't DC where Lex Luthor can take a stand for Humanity and defy Superman. The Exalts aren't aliens. Their mortal. Their human. <br /> <br /> Do some people think their not? Sure. The Realm might ahve some of that going with Sun Chosen but given that we have a fae mutant monk and exigents canon(Immaculat anyway) descendants seeking redemption, I'd be surprised if the Scarlet Empire had high priority of killing children of Solars anymore.<br /> <br /> The official name is also unlikely to be that phrase anyway.<br /> <br /> Now to the OP: I've not played a child of an exalt myself. The closest we had was a child who was ghostblooded and got thautmurgy from it. The Night Caste adopted her and used sorcery to bring out her bloodline and make her a queen of ghosts and wood creatures. It was rather fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:58:56-07:00","id":1225274,"title":"","content":"Must admit that while i found them curious from a mechanic standpoint, i made little use of them that i can remember. Once or twice as &quot;ersatz Exalted&quot; through temporary divine endownment and one major group of antagonists in a solars game was a lineage of ghost-blooded necromancers further empowered (2nd circle necromancy, Arcanoi and some bits to enhance them) by the Whispers and ancient entreaties to a particular Neverborn whose agenda they served.<br /> <br /> Beside this, in the last solars game i STed, the PCs eventually found out the &quot;sergeant&quot; of their blood ape pack, who they already knew could assume human and a variety of primate forms, had been seducing a bunch of women in almost all stops of their travels and left a few of them heavy with child.<br /> <br /> No big bad plan actually, just a little fallback resource to maybe make a new clan/gang/pack in case he ever lost the cushy position leading demonic grunts for them. Sayaj having all the intelectual depth of Titus Pullo, though (occasionally) a little more cunning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-06-2018, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T12:10:27-07:00","id":1225396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225083#post1225083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your basic understanding and justification rests on the notion that :<br /> Exalted Children will use parent charms (Devs have indicated they wont.)</div> </div> </div> </div>When 3E gives us their proper charms, I will be <b>thrilled</b>.<br /> <br /> But the 2E text gives explicit examples (and limitations) of them using Exalted charms. Deadly Beastmen Transformation was an <i>explicit </i>one they named. <br /> <br /> Moreover, the specific mechanics don't matter - only the <i>appearance for onlookers</i>. So until they clarify &quot;it's impossible for villagers to confuse their charms with that of an Exalt&quot;s&quot;, it's all moot. I was creating psuedo-Lunar shapeshifters in 1E using some of the mutations in the book - and even though it was 0% Lunar by blood, people still confused them for Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225083#post1225083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Touched will be a thing(...they really shouldnt be as that makes no sense to begin with).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm on the fence with this, since yes - I can see the tension of Exalting vs not-Exalting...<br /> <br /> ....but since they're already limiting how often Dragon-Blooded create &quot;pure&quot; offspring, then Dragon-Touched might not be so overwhelming. And since they won't use legit Exalted charms, all the better. It could serve as a legit mechanical definition for &quot;Patricians&quot;.<br /> <br /> PLUS issues of &quot;thin-blood&quot; could be good for exacerbating Dragon-Blooded breeding woes. If you're either &quot;full or not&quot;, it's easy to just restrict breeding to the pure. If you have all this &quot;blurring of the lines&quot;, then Dragon-Blooded might intermingle with Patricians (slowly but steadily diluting their lineage - without them fully appreciating just how bad it is - since they think the Dragon-Touched are &quot;close enough&quot; or whatever).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225083#post1225083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That we can meaningfully compare the Exalted host to a colonial empire (we can't). The phrase is inaccurate in addition to offensive:</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me know what fictitious Exalt is offended by my comparison. I'll make sure to write a fan fic apology.<br /> <br /> IE - When you throw around the claim that something is &quot;offensive&quot; around so casually, it loses it's weight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225083#post1225083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What natives are the Solars oppressing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoever the Solars beat.<br /> <br /> Every minor henchmen or soldier slain by a Solar - is another victim who, if you spend 2 seconds sympathizing with, has a legitimate reason to cry out as to why some other human was arbitrarily given magical powers with which to murder them. <br /> <br /> The signature Infernal Slayer - Cearr - had <b>his entire people wiped out </b>in a war between the Bull of the North and the Realm and the Haltans. His <i>entire reason for becoming an Infernal Exalt</i> starts with a sympathetic demon arguing that the world was unjust and unfair - and if he had also been Exalted, he could have saved his people.<br /> <br /> Your claim that it's inappropriate to compare magically-empowered one-man-army's that commit genocide to colonial empires is offensive to the victims of Cearr's tribe. (but no worries, I'm sure Cearr forgives you)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225083#post1225083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What colonial empire exists of the lunars? If anything, Moon Born seem to be champions in Lunar domains opposing colonial powers</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2E, the Silver Pact served as an empirical &quot;anti-empire&quot; who often sabotaged civilizations that <b>want</b> to exist in favor of their faux neo-tribal caricature of wannabe primitivism.<br /> <br /> They are my absolute <b>least favorite</b> concoction from 2E.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I have a list somewhere of 2-3 dozen points where they...ugh.<br /> <br /> The fake ethno-culture they create:<br /> <br /> <b>Clawspeak?</b><br /> What IS Clawspeak.<ul><li>Did whomever invent this only speak one language? Do they think languages are cyphers?</li> <li>Why would someone who speaks Flame-tongue agree to the same meanings and concepts as someone who speaks High Realm?</li> <li>What if &quot;X&quot; symbol in Clawspeak is a highly offensive or taboo symbol in Riverspeak?</li> <li>Why should clawless-totem Lunars even use Clawspeak? Would a jellyfish <i>want</i> to be clawed up? An octopus? A fish?</li> </ul><b>Clawspeak (Round 2)</b><br /> WHY is Clawspeak? The implication is that we can read the tattoos - and that they serve as a magical-narrative shielding you against the Wyld (in a sense, inscribing <i>who you are</i> and therefore locking in your story such that the Wyld can't re-write you into something else).<ul><li><b>So</b> <b>no diversity of symbol sets?</b> <br /> No Nordic runes, Arabic script, Sumerian cuneiform or braille-inspired scars... not only do Lunars need to learn this made-up tongue (a waste of Linguistics) but we need to use the same script for us to read it. This isn't <i>decorative</i>, it's functional. And ugly.</li> <li><b>Implied prohibition against character growth? </b><br /> Your story is scarred into your flesh - so what if you grow? Great, at 18, some bumbling leaf-draped buffoon covered in woad and mushrooms decided I proved myself a &quot;Warrior&quot; at 18 so now I'm a Full Moon for eternity. What if after 3 decades of life, I regret the bloodshed, I regret warfare, I've buried all my family, friends and children - and I turn into a devout priest and scholar of Luna? Why am I eternally branded a &quot;Warrior&quot;?</li> </ul><b>Shamanism</b><br /> What if my Lunar grew up in the Realm and believes in the Immaculate Order? What if I'm part of an Ancestor Cult? What about <i>literally any belief system unrelated to shamanism?</i> Why should some unwashed savage who just met me dictate my caste - when my ancestor cult already includes 6 generations of ghosts who have known me all my life and can well speak for the type of person I've grown up to be?<br /> <br /> Why should a Lunar Immaculate overnight drop their belief system - and adopt this neo-primitive reconstructionist claptrap - instead of wrestling with their place within the Order?<br /> <br /> <b>Kidnapping!</b> <br /> They depict kidnapping as a virtue and duty. They pretend it's &quot;rescue&quot; - except they belittle Casteless who refuse as clueless - and they disparage them as dangerous (they might turn Chimera!) - they offer rewards (Artifacts, etc) for retrieving them - and they list these rescues as a type of typical duty for story. <br /> <br /> Moreover, Creation is vast - what if Riverspeak-fluent Lunars capture a Flame-tongue fluent Casteless? In how many gestures can I tell them to &quot;go away&quot;? Even within a language family, communication might be impossible (is Flame-Tongue as vast as a Romance language? Because Spanish makes Portuguese &quot;workable&quot;, Italian &quot;familiar&quot;, French sounds fake and Romanian into gibberish. How would a Lunar from Gem communicate with a Lunar from Chiaroscuro to tell them &quot;I don't want your help - go away&quot;?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">My god, 2E Silver Pact Lunars get my blood boiling in a heartbeat.</span><br /> <br /> And then put it into context!<br /> <br /> These aren't arbitrary complaints - <i>they lead to experiences in game</i>. I've played online in large mixed groups (with multiple circles).... and the <i>second</i> a Lunar realizes you're Casteless, the tropes pile up. I'll use a previous character I've mentioned (on another thread) as an example:<ul><li><b>&quot;Why don't you want to join us?&quot;</b><br /> My character Exalted while fighting off beastmen attacking her settlement. She has no interest in other Lunars. <br /> .</li> <li><b>&quot;But we look totally badass! The guards fear us!&quot;</b><br /> Your flagrant depictions of muscle-and-tattooed &quot;badassery&quot; are a complete turn off. It'd be cool if you respected the locals.<br /> .</li> <li><b>&quot;But the tattoos protect you from the Wyld!&quot;</b><br /> Not visiting the Wyld in the first-place protects me from the Wyld. Plus not glowing moonsilver protects my identity.<br /> .</li> <li><b>&quot;But Shapeshifting! Chimera!&quot;</b><br /> I can play a Lunar without (or with minimal) shapeshifting. <br /> .</li> <li><b>&quot;But the trails would be cool to roleplay!&quot;</b><br /> My character is an urbanite in a landlocked Realm tributary with an Octopus totem - and, privately, a member of an ancestor cult. As long as she can quietly put out offerings to her dead grandparents and sibling, she's fulfilling her sense of religious duty.<br /> <br /> The nearest bordermarches are 400 miles away and full of frigid snow. <i>It will kill her</i>. Her Octopus totem won't let her fly away or survive on land. My &quot;tribe&quot; are the human inhabitants of this city (and the nearby settlement), not a bunch of barbarians in fur who prey upon them.</li> </ul>In 2E, Lunar Exalts are as <b>invasive</b> and <b>persistent</b> as you could ask for. I've had <i>less problems</i> dealing with Dragon-Blooded and Immaculate dogma. After Infernals came out - <i>despite absolutely loving Glories of Luna and all things Luna</i> - I never played a Lunar again, since I could easily build a warform (By Rage Recast) and shapeshift (Ebon Dragon charms) and move quickly (Adorjan speed charms) and even adorn myself with silver while surviving inhospitable regions (thank you Cecylene). </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In short, 2E Silver Pact Lunars expect you to shed 20-40 years of human life <i>(anywhere</i>) to suddenly make their Silver Pact chapter relevant.<br /> <br /> It's on par with neo-Nazis wanting to create a faux ethno-state.... but lacking an ethnicity, they simply say they're &quot;white&quot; - and anyone else who is &quot;white&quot; should &quot;obviously&quot; join them because they're brothers-in-arms! <i>Nevermind</i> the vast differences in values, beliefs, language, religion, culture and history that an Italian/Hungarian/Swede/Irish or someone from Gem/Sijan/Skullstone/Whiterun might have. 2E Lunars just go &quot;you shapeshift like us, so you're one of us, so lets help you look like us, speak like us, act like us, and together &quot;we can secure the existence of our people and a future for beastmen children&quot;. <b>As a bonus</b>, they can all share a hatred of those inferior Dragon-Blooded, a literal race of multi-colored footsoldiers who didn't &quot;stay in their place&quot; and stole the Realm away from their betters by out-populating them.<br /> <br /> I <i>really, really, really</i> dislike the 2E Silver Pact. There is <b>plenty</b> of imperial behavior (while being blind to it).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225083#post1225083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do have a parallel for colonial imperialism. Its the Realm. If you want stories of characters torn between empire and people, maybe explore the Realm and the idea of a member of an oppressed satrapy exalting as a dragonblooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're the obvious choice and I agree.<br /> <br /> But their ubiquitousness also means that Realm opinions on Celestial Exalts will flavor how other people see you. If you're a Sun-Child, the <i>first, second and third</i> concern any aware local has is &quot;oh shit, a Solar Exalt has been around at least (your age) years.... and if the Wyld Hunt didn't kill them, it's been growing in power since then&quot;. <br /> <br /> Case in point, Bull of the North. Tons of massacres on both sides. The Goblin King is another horror. Any decent Solar given 1-2 decades is going to bring bloodshed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225083#post1225083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this isn't DC where Lex Luthor can take a stand for Humanity and defy Superman. The Exalts aren't aliens. Their mortal. Their human.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're human. And humans do shitty things to each other. The Bull of the North was <i>so bad</i> that the Yozis recruited one of his victims as a champion. Panther also killed people or left them to die (and one of them became an Abyssal Exalt). <br /> <br /> Lyta? A Dragon-Blooded monk sought to humble and probably kill her - so sure, she fought. But then she Exalted <i>and killed every other monk in the area</i>. Bravo mass murder. I'm sure all those families who just had their most pious, religious members <i>torn apart</i> will be thrilled to hear about Lyta's humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225083#post1225083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do some people think their not? Sure. The Realm might have some of that going with Sun Chosen but given that we have a fae mutant monk and exigents canon(Immaculat anyway) descendants seeking redemption, I'd be surprised if the Scarlet Empire had high priority of killing children of Solars anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>3E might be changing things - but until it covers the topic in detail, 2E is the core material we work with.<br /> <br /> And exigents aren't the descendants of <i>war criminals</i>. <br /> <br /> To go back with real-life examples, try Spain. The peninsula was splintered into regions that often loathed each other - but they unified via the Reconquista and the Inquisition to kick out the foreign empire (700 years of Islamic invaders).<br /> <br /> Spain had black Conquistadors - and moreno Conquistadors (moreno = moorish) - and white Conquistadors (even Columbus was a foreigner). But notice which word is miniscule and which word is Capital in each of those examples. Being &quot;white&quot; didn't make you a defacto ally - and being &quot;other&quot; didn't make you a defacto enemy of the state. The Inquisition focused on those who weren't <i>Spanish</i>. Were you loyal to the previous invading Caliphate? <i>Out</i>. Did you engage in business with foreigners at the expense of locals? <i>Out</i>. The only locals the Inquisition really pounced on were the Basque (who the Moors favored for concubines - and who still don't speak a Romance language).<br /> <br /> Comparing this to the Realm, it lines up perfectly. Are you a devout Immaculate with some exotic lineage? Fine - awesome - welcome aboard, you can help us bring civilization to our enemies. A one-shot exigent isn't a representative of an <i>entire army</i> of world-shaking juggernauts.<br /> <br /> But do you have a magical heritage directly tied to the golden-god-monsters and cannibal-shapeshifters that we died by the thousands to eradicate? <i>Yeah, out</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T12:12:44-07:00","id":1225399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225396#post1225396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When 3E gives us their proper charms, I will be <b>thrilled</b>.<br /> <br /> But the 2E text gives explicit examples (and limitations) of them using Exalted charms. Deadly Beastmen Transformation was an <i>explicit </i>one they named.</div> </div> </div> </div>The children of Exalted will explicitly not use their parents' Charms, as that has never not broken things to hell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm on the fence with this, since yes - I can see the tension of Exalting vs not-Exalting...<br /> <br /> ....but since they're already limiting how often Dragon-Blooded create &quot;pure&quot; offspring, then Dragon-Touched might not be so overwhelming. And since they won't use legit Exalted charms, all the better. It could serve as a legit mechanical definition for &quot;Patricians&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Touched explicitly don't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T12:38:53-07:00","id":1225410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225396#post1225396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me know what fictitious Exalt is offended by my comparison. I'll make sure to write a fan fic apology.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I'm sorry, are you deliberately ignoring who is offended by the term? Let me be clearer then: The phrase is inaccurate as there is no actual real world comparison. It is simeltaneously offensive to real human beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225396#post1225396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoever the Solars beat.<br /> <br /> Every minor henchmen or soldier slain by a Solar - is another victim who, if you spend 2 seconds sympathizing with, has a legitimate reason to cry out as to why some other human was arbitrarily given magical powers with which to murder them.<br /> <br /> The signature Infernal Slayer - Cearr - had <b>his entire people wiped out </b>in a war between the Bull of the North and the Realm and the Haltans. His <i>entire reason for becoming an Infernal Exalt</i> starts with a sympathetic demon arguing that the world was unjust and unfair - and if he had also been Exalted, he could have saved his people.<br /> <br /> Your claim that it's inappropriate to compare magically-empowered one-man-army's that commit genocide to colonial empires is offensive to the victims of Cearr's tribe. (but no worries, I'm sure Cearr forgives you)</div> </div> </div> </div>A man is not an institution.<br /> A Solar that exalts among his people and becomes king, even a tyrant, is a fundamentally different problm than an external force imposing itself. Solars aren't a unified caste who oppress humanity on a systemtic level. Again, we have an oppresive class of imperial rulers. The Realm. If we want to talk about awful exalts, we can. But there is a fundamental difference between &quot;Native tyrant&quot; and &quot;Colonial power&quot;. The tensions you want to explore, about torn heritag, do not exist with a native born tyrant. Not in the same way.<br /> And again, who in univrse sees the Solar Empire marching in and subjugating poor humanity? Solars are human. They rise from humanity--hell, unlike dragonblooded, they aren't even born special. Someone might be enraged that the sun chose them instead of someone else, but at the end of the day &quot;Solar&quot; is not a political class that systematically dispossess humanity (Nor is lunar, for that matter. Dragonblooded maybe).<br /> <br /> also, as an aside....are you arguing that...lets come back to the bull of the north in a omment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225396#post1225396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> silver pact</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that we have a modus operandi on 3e Silver Pact that points to them as poractively winning the war...I don't care. I just don't. In the same way that I don't find Cearr compelling(Not, Infernals are also, even in 2e, not a colonial empire. A raging sycopath isn't the same as a colonial instituiton. Arguably, the Cecylene charms could make such an empire however.). 2e sources are not terribly persuasive reasons to keep bad ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225396#post1225396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, they're the obvious choice and I agree.<br /> <br /> But their ubiquitousness also means that Realm opinions on Celestial Exalts will flavor how other people see you. If you're a Sun-Child, the <i>first, second and third</i> concern any aware local has is &quot;oh shit, a Solar Exalt has been around at least (your age) years.... and if the Wyld Hunt didn't kill them, it's been growing in power since then&quot;.<br /> <br /> Case in point, Bull of the North. Tons of massacres on both sides. The Goblin King is another horror. Any decent Solar given 1-2 decades is going to bring bloodshed.<br /> <br /> They're human. And humans do shitty things to each other. The Bull of the North was <i>so bad</i> that the Yozis recruited one of his victims as a champion. Panther also killed people or left them to die (and one of them became an Abyssal Exalt).<br /> <br /> Lyta? A Dragon-Blooded monk sought to humble and probably kill her - so sure, she fought. But then she Exalted <i>and killed every other monk in the area</i>. Bravo mass murder. I'm sure all those families who just had their most pious, religious members <i>torn apart</i> will be thrilled to hear about Lyta's humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, yeah. Their monsters. Annnd? There are monsters that aren't imposing colonial race dynamics, especially since the vision of solars isn't universal (the Bull's really popular among the ice walkers after all). When solars have instituted a colonial regime, sure.<br /> <br /> Hell, lets talk bull of the North and his inspiration! The Khanate wasn't a colonial empire. It committed genocide and murder, and was oppressive in many ways! But no, was not colonial. It kinda...didn't build colonies? Or, to my knowledge, establish racial hierarchies? It promoted free trade and freedom of religion after the mass murders and left huge swaths of bureaucracy intact and didn't pursue systemic oppression of specific racial groups? Or establish such groups?<br /> <br /> I'm a bit confused as why Cearr and the Abyssal are your points...I mean, the bigger deal for Cearr was that he lost his nerve. It could have been the realm killing his people, it'd be the same difference.<br /> <br /> Lyta, if her hair brained scheme of replacing the realm with a Solar realm, would be colonial. But notice that that's a product of her basically recreating th existing colonial empire, not a trait inherent of solars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225396#post1225396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And exigents aren't the descendants of <i>war criminals</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Actually! They are. The Exigents are the reincarnations of the Anthema's servants! So yes. They are the recreation or spiritual children of what immaculates would consider war criminals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225396#post1225396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To go back with real-life examples, try Spain. The peninsula was splintered into regions that often loathed each other - but they unified via the Reconquista and the Inquisition to kick out the foreign empire (700 years of Islamic invaders).<br /> <br /> Spain had black Conquistadors - and moreno Conquistadors (moreno = moorish) - and white Conquistadors (even Columbus was a foreigner). But notice which word is miniscule and which word is Capital in each of those examples. Being &quot;white&quot; didn't make you a defacto ally - and being &quot;other&quot; didn't make you a defacto enemy of the state. The Inquisition focused on those who weren't <i>Spanish</i>. Were you loyal to the previous invading Caliphate? <i>Out</i>. Did you engage in business with foreigners at the expense of locals? <i>Out</i>. The only locals the Inquisition really pounced on were the Basque (who the Moors favored for concubines - and who still don't speak a Romance language).<br /> <br /> Comparing this to the Realm, it lines up perfectly. Are you a devout Immaculate with some exotic lineage? Fine - awesome - welcome aboard, you can help us bring civilization to our enemies. A one-shot exigent isn't a representative of an <i>entire army</i> of world-shaking juggernauts.<br /> <br /> But do you have a magical heritage directly tied to the golden-god-monsters and cannibal-shapeshifters that we died by the thousands to eradicate? <i>Yeah, out</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Hm. So. I don't know much history of the Reconquista. I'll leave that respone on the door, regarding the awfulness of the affair.<br /> <br /> THe crux here is that a) there was an inherited lineage that ruled over a region for a long time that b) was driven out of a region so c) it's descendants would still be prosecutd.<br /> <br /> Alright. Cool. So the Realm <i>might</i> after so many hundred of years make a point of killing descendnts of anathema. Might. Honestly, that sounds like Usurpation era concerns (the realm is, after all, what ? a few hundred years removed from the First Age?). It'd be like the modern Spainish state trying to expunge peopel that were suspected of being jewish or muslim today, but of course that'd be fasc--<br /> oh, pardon me. Slipped into politics.<br /> <br /> The point your responding to, and the crux you maintian, is that the Solar First Age resembled colonial rule. This is a point that seems untenable. Even if your an Age of Nightmares Fan, and think th end of the first age was full of terrible and glorious actions that made &quot;Murder the most powerful figures in the world and seal them away for ever&quot; a viable option out of desperation, the Solars dont work as a colonial power. Mostly.<br /> The one exception I'll give is the Solar vs Sea Niobarran war, were the solars acted as a united front.<br /> <br /> If you want a story about somone caught between a lineage of atrocity and oppression and thos oppressed, you have slave in a satrapy Dragonblooded.<br /> Solars just...just don't do that. Neither Solars nor Lunars are colonial powers, establishing legaces and lineages of conqureros and castes. Not that we've seen anyway (lunars might, now that I think on it, with beastmen blessings? But again, the 3e lunars and Silver Pact seem more &quot;anti-imperial&quot;. I look forward to reading on them.) Solar's children don't do that either. They have no thrones to claim, no power in the world waiting for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 06-06-2018, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T13:51:45-07:00","id":1225444,"title":"","content":"Point of order on Lyta's Second Breath: she was being singled out by an Exalted student for rejecting the advances of the Exalt's mortal buddy. The Dragon-Blooded and said mortal buddy double-teamed her during what was essentially an exam to test their martial arts skills. Then the Second Breath happened. No monks got involved until after she became a Dawn, at which point none of them stood a chance in hell of &quot;humbling&quot; her on their own and that wouldn't have been their aim in the first place, since she was, by that point, Forsaken to them in every sense of the word.<br /> <br /> Point of order for 2e Silver Pact's goals for various societies: They didn't really have any. They were pulling a Cave Johnson with the TSR - throwing stuff at the wall to see if it stuck. That was the problem; there was nothing there to be had in the attempt to be Silver Sidereals, because they didn't have any of the tools to be Sidereals or do what they did, and never would, since they were not Sidereals. This is completely a failure of writing direction; metatext is the only relevant engagement here. In-setting arguments have no weight, and arguing about what characters were doing or wanted in 2e is thus irrelevant even for 2e, the edition for which this material was written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T17:51:59-07:00","id":1225492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'm sorry, are you deliberately ignoring who is offended by the term? Let me be clearer then: The phrase is inaccurate as there is no actual real world comparison. It is simeltaneously offensive to real human beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>No - I'm sincerely not seeing the offense.<br /> <br /> I'm saying &quot;the Exalted tend to dominate non-Exalted everywhere they go&quot;. If you don't like (any real world empire) coming to your home town and imposing their will on the locals through guile and force-of-arms, <b>then</b> you're going to like it <b>even less</b> with a magically-empowered aspiring-dictator shows up promising a utopia (and in the interim, enjoy being crushed as the Realm and the local Celestial go to war with each other).<br /> <br /> I need you to elaborate - really clearly, since I'm missing it - how on earth any of this is offensive in real life.<br /> <br /> How is saying &quot;magically empowered people dominating others kind of sucks from the perspective of the dominated&quot; offend.... who? Am I offending real-world empires who wish it was that easy? Or am I offending real-world colonies for sympathizing with the perspective of the colonized? I'm not picking up what you're putting down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A man is not an institution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalts quit being men the second you have access to bureaucracy charms that substitute actual bureaucracies - war charms that let you make-up for militaries - and well, Bull of the North is just a great example (the guy is as local, aged and niche as you could ask for.... literally walking out into the snow <i>to die</i>.... but add Exaltation and he's <b>the guy</b> that resulted in massive Realm casualties, a rebalancing of power-politics in the North and a few slaughters inbetween.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that we have a modus operandi on 3e Silver Pact that points to them as poractively winning the war...I don't care. I just don't. In the same way that I don't find Cearr compelling(Not, Infernals are also, even in 2e, not a colonial empire. A raging sycopath isn't the same as a colonial instituiton. Arguably, the Cecylene charms could make such an empire however.). 2e sources are not terribly persuasive reasons to keep bad ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since <i>the Children of the Exalted</i> are predominantly covered in 2E - I contextualize their existence within 2E political dynamics - and since you mention the Lunars in a positive light.... I therefore countered that.<br /> <br /> If you're operating on 3E, cool. I eagerly await their 3E splat (them, Exigents and Infernals). But I don't care if they're winning or losing the war - if their social-chapter is <i>remotely</i> like 2E, it'll be the same disappointment. Going back to empires, I don't care if the French are winning or losing - if you were Haitian or Algerian, <i>you wanted them to stay in France</i>. <br /> <br /> And did you miss my point on Cearr? Cearr is <b>the victim</b>. His entire people.... wiped off the map.... because of Exalts. <br /> <br /> Humanity tends to find a balance when its man vs man. Add in supernatural might and things go haywire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, yeah. Their monsters. Annnd? There are monsters that aren't imposing colonial race dynamics, especially since the vision of solars isn't universal (the Bull's really popular among the ice walkers after all).</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need different &quot;races&quot; to define colonialism. The planet (in real life) is populated by groups that crush one another the second one gets some power. Not just Germans curb-stomped other Europeans or China claiming Tibet, Shiites badgering Zoroastrians or the like. <br /> <br /> Some of the worst &quot;colonial&quot; influence was <i>local. </i>When the French were in North Africa, they showed favoritism to Muslims (monotheistic, easier to learn one language and let the locals be the translators, etc). The French didn't mass-murder non-Muslim locals..... their favoritism encouraged conversion into a new unified entity (whereby a minority in some regions now became the majority). You don't need a full-fledged empire to ruin people's lives - just some power and a few favored locals (and watch the power dynamic ripple along).<br /> <br /> And the Bull's popularity with Ice Walkers is irrelevant - <b><i>whoever</i></b> doesn't like the Ice Walkers is now shitting in their pants that a bunch of psuedo-barbarian tribes are on the move. And like with Cearr, if you just happen to be <i>stuck</i> between two armies when they choose your territory as a battlefield, you're going to go extinct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, lets talk bull of the North and his inspiration! The Khanate wasn't a colonial empire. It committed genocide and murder, and was oppressive in many ways! But no, was not colonial. It kinda...didn't build colonies? Or, to my knowledge, establish racial hierarchies? It promoted free trade and freedom of religion after the mass murders and left huge swaths of bureaucracy intact and didn't pursue systemic oppression of specific racial groups? Or establish such groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus Christ.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping you're defending genocide as a tongue-in-cheek thing. The point is their victims (if they were alive) wouldn't be bemused.<br /> <br /> Entire cities (men, women, children) were decapitated <i>for giving offense</i> to the wrong person. One of Khan's daughters had everyone killed - and the skulls collected into a pile - such that descriptions claim the bodies made the mountains look small - and the fields were watered red. Another region - known for it's artisans - was annihilated, with the paltry few survivors never restoring the crafts/art they were famous for - until the city was burned a few centuries later and abandoned.<br /> <br /> And when 10% of the DNA in Asia is his - <i>did he need colonies?</i> Murdering or raping the locals <i>made them his</i>. <br /> <br /> You're turning this whole thing into a <i>racial</i> issue which is bizarre. You don't need to be blue, green or purple skinned in order for a clash to be oppressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused as why Cearr and the Abyssal are your points...I mean, the bigger deal for Cearr was that he lost his nerve. It could have been the realm killing his people, it'd be the same difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because both of them would have been <i>regular people for the rest of their lives </i>had not the Bull or Panther shown up.<br /> <br /> Cearr might be a regular leader. He'd have his friends, his family, his culture, his language. He'd have children some day, local skills and arts, whatever you want. Cearr is not &quot;less worthy&quot; of these things just because he's the same skin color as the Bull (as if skin color is remotely relevant to one's humanity).<br /> <br /> If not for the Exalted, he'd have had a &quot;fair chance&quot; at life - growing old - and dying peacefully. <b>Instead</b> everything he ever aspired for fell apart because you got Dawn Castes with fear-auras and Dynasts summoning demons. I don't see the confusing part about thinking that - if any of us were in his shoes - we'd think compassion is meritous. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lyta, if her hair brained scheme of replacing the realm with a Solar realm, would be colonial. But notice that that's a product of her basically recreating the existing colonial empire, not a trait inherent of solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care if she creates one or doesn't. We're discussing <i>the children of Exalts</i>.<br /> <br /> And when <i>anyone remotely aware of the incident hears about it</i>, they're going to hear &quot;oh yeah, 30+ monks were all mass-murdered by a Solar who just <i>spontaneously</i> erupted - mass-murder of the most pious is one of their level 1 powers&quot;. <b>From there</b>, I argue, &quot;no, mortals will not take Solars <i>lightly</i> - including their offspring - because all the famous Celestial Exalts inevitably become famous for the sheer amount of death they can spread&quot;. <br /> <br /> It's a cool power as a player - but a horrific one as an NPC - ergo, NPCs don't owe <i>the children of Exalts</i> any wiggle room.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Actually! They are. The Exigents are the reincarnations of the Anthema's servants! So yes. They are the recreation or spiritual children of what immaculates would consider war criminals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that part - but need to see the Dragon-Blooded write-up on the issue to see what angle they take.<br /> <br /> As aforementioned, Spain had black Conquistadors (complete with their own knightly orders and working side-by-side along Pizarro and co) - as well as morenos and trigue\u00f1o (I don't think either of these translates as slurs into English - but they're phenotypes that don't fit into the &quot;neat&quot; black/white dichtonomy that English favors). Spain was always more interested with their Spanish-ness (language, religion, culture) than bloodline or color.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Hm. So. I don't know much history of the Reconquista. I'll leave that respone on the door, regarding the awfulness of the affair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the 700 years of Moors enslaving, robbing and killing Iberians <i>in the first place</i>. Everyone was pretty awful, but the Reconquista was always <i>a reaction to</i> that awfulness.<br /> <br /> Spanish provinces are <b>not</b> like US States - they are regional <i>rivalries </i>that go back to <i>Roman times</i> - complete with different dialects, phenotypes, culture and religion. And despite <i>hating each other for centuries</i> (complete with modern separatist movements in Catalonia, Galicia, Basque, etc)..... despite all that, they were still willing to temporarily set aside their differences to kick out the Moors. A <i>Moreno</i> is okay (that's just a phenotype) - a <i>Moro </i>is not (full-on foreign-loyal invader). There's still slavery in Mauritania and Morocco <b>today</b> along the same ancestral lines and it's not the Europeans guilty for that.<br /> <br /> The world isn't all &quot;evil guilty monsters&quot; and &quot;innocent peoples&quot; - <i>everyone</i> on this planet has been a monster at some point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe crux here is that a) there was an inherited lineage that ruled over a region for a long time that b) was driven out of a region so c) it's descendants would still be prosecuted.<br /> <br /> Alright. Cool. So the Realm <i>might</i> after so many hundred of years make a point of killing descendnts of anathema. Might. Honestly, that sounds like Usurpation era concerns (the realm is, after all, what ? a few hundred years removed from the First Age?). It'd be like the modern Spanish state trying to expunge peopel that were suspected of being jewish or muslim today, but of course that'd be fasc--<br /> oh, pardon me. Slipped into politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I thought the books describe the Wyld Hunt persecuting associates of the Anathema too. Was this changed in 3E? Because if they'll hunt a Solar's friends and loved ones, they <i>definitely</i> should include the kid.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded.... <i>whose power is from birth</i>. I <i>suspect</i> they will be less forgiving about a Sun-Kid or Moon-Born. &quot;Being born into power&quot; is <i>exactly</i> what made them strong enough to rule an empire. Unless they have a strong grasp of the power-limits of <i>Children of Exalts</i>, it's a dumb risk to take. <b>Plus</b> if you're still hunting Anathema, then <b>no</b>, you don't want to normalize Anathema-lite. It's going to be <b>way</b> more difficult to find a Lunar if you've taught the populace that the Lunar-lite kid with a shapeshifting charm and silver jewelry is okay to overlook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225410#post1225410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point your responding to, and the crux you maintian, is that the Solar First Age resembled colonial rule. This is a point that seems untenable. Even if your an Age of Nightmares Fan, and think th end of the first age was full of terrible and glorious actions that made &quot;Murder the most powerful figures in the world and seal them away for ever&quot; a viable option out of desperation, the Solars dont work as a colonial power. Mostly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars aren't Knights in Shining Armor. They're One-Man-Armies. <br /> <br /> You don't need 300 Solars acting in concert to have something akin to &quot;colonial rule&quot;.<br /> <br /> You need 1 Solar <i>with fucking magic powers</i> rewriting the social, economic and military landscape to do it.<br /> <br /> Who needs a three dozen diplomats to achieve a century-long peace-treaty (say you want to end the Anglo-French Hundred Year's War) when <i>Speed the Wheels </i>says I can achieve any feat within 1 Season (at most). <br /> <br /> Who needs 300 researchers, investigators and statisticians analyzing a bureau for corruption - when Bureau-Rectifying Method can single-handedly let me purge the least useful members, clear corruption, eliminate spies.... for 8m and 1wp? <b>Bam</b>, I can tell an organization to just <i>keep hiring 10% of the staff</i> and my charm will <i>automatically</i> make the least useful members quit, get fired or die - snowballing into hiring only the best-of-the-best within a few weeks of the hiring spree.<br /> <br /> Who needs <i>assassins?</i> At Essence 3, I can use Heavenly Mandate Marking <i>on a mortal servant</i> - send them as an ambassador - and when she meets a king, <i>I can use my charms through her</i>. I can also <i>see everything she sees</i> to create a layout if I plan to kill a target anyways. Awesome. Even if they kill or imprison her, <i>their job is done</i>.<br /> <br /> Solar magic is (and should be) <i>terrifying</i>. And you only need 1 Solar to wreak this havoc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T18:13:11-07:00","id":1225498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225399#post1225399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The children of Exalted will explicitly not use their parents' Charms, as that has never not broken things to hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great to hear!<br /> <br /> I know these walls of text are <b>huge</b> - but I think we all <b>agree </b>on this point. <br /> <br /> My point with Deadly Beastman Transformation was that - <i>even if in my mind I know that mechanically it's supposed to be something else</i> - <b>visually, </b>will Creation's inhabitants be able to differentiate? If Moon-Born are supposed to have (in 2E) &quot;some kind of non-Exalted charm that resembles DBT enough for us to get a free-pass to using it in its stead&quot;, <b>then </b>&quot;will Creation's inhabitants see a difference?&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think the Player's Guide was even published for 1E back then - but when Lunars came out, I had a psuedo-werewolf built entirely out of Mutations. 100% not a Lunar. <i>But it mattered little</i> because my powers were so clearly Lunar-esque, villagers and town guards thought it was Anathema or Beastman (and the hunt proceeded from there).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225444#post1225444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order on Lyta's Second Breath: she was being singled out by an Exalted student for rejecting the advances of the Exalt's mortal buddy. The Dragon-Blooded and said mortal buddy double-teamed her during what was essentially an exam to test their martial arts skills. Then the Second Breath happened. No monks got involved until after she became a Dawn, at which point none of them stood a chance in hell of &quot;humbling&quot; her on their own and that wouldn't have been their aim in the first place, since she was, by that point, Forsaken to them in every sense of the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> 1) This conversation is about <i>the Children of Exalts</i>, not about Lyta's motives.<br /> <br /> 2) The argument is that <i>fresh fear of the Solar Exalted</i> will motivate <i>anyone who values their lives</i> to report anything remotely (obviously) Solar.<br /> <br /> 3) Lyta's motives are <i>irrelevant</i> except to mind-readers. The end-result is 30 or so dead monks (including Dragon Blooded) because 1 Solar Anathema suddenly &quot;sold her soul to the Yozis for power&quot;. All law-abiding citizens are expected to report potential Anathema sightings if they value their lives. We repeat, 30 something dead citizens because of 1 crazed, blood-thirsty anathema stole a few drops of Sun-powered magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225444#post1225444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order for 2e Silver Pact's goals for various societies: They didn't really have any. They were pulling a Cave Johnson with the TSR - throwing stuff at the wall to see if it stuck. That was the problem; there was nothing there to be had in the attempt to be Silver Sidereals, because they didn't have any of the tools to be Sidereals or do what they did, and never would, since they were not Sidereals. This is completely a failure of writing direction; metatext is the only relevant engagement here. In-setting arguments have no weight, and arguing about what characters were doing or wanted in 2e is thus irrelevant even for 2e, the edition for which this material was written.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a dodge.<br /> <br /> We're discussing <i>the Children of Exalts</i>. The bulk of which we know about being in 2E.<br /> <br /> <b>The point is</b> you suggested Lunars were &quot;anti-colonial&quot; - <b>and I disagreed vehemently</b>. They're a wannabe ethno-state where if you happen to have (X) power, an entire chapter awaits you to regale you with how you can basically abandon your pre-Lunar existence - you have a whole new set of values, language, codes, goals, etc to adopt - complete with mechanical penalties for refusing to join and rewards for dragging other nascent Lunars kicking-and-screaming to your local den. <br /> <br /> They are <i>every bit as invasive, domineering and cocksure</i> as any Dynast - and if mortals dislike Lunars and Beastmen <i>to start</i>, a Moon-Born who flagrantly shows off their ties isn't going to win any allies locally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T18:21:42-07:00","id":1225499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No - I'm sincerely not seeing the offense.<br /> <br /> I'm saying &quot;the Exalted tend to dominate non-Exalted everywhere they go&quot;. If you don't like (any real world empire) coming to your home town and imposing their will on the locals through guile and force-of-arms, <b>then</b> you're going to like it <b>even less</b> with a magically-empowered aspiring-dictator shows up promising a utopia (and in the interim, enjoy being crushed as the Realm and the local Celestial go to war with each other).<br /> <br /> I need you to elaborate - really clearly, since I'm missing it - how on earth any of this is offensive in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking about the term in this cf's title. Go check with other people for why it's bad.<br /> Your also ignoring that, you know, the Exalt might be coming to your home town...from your hometown.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And did you miss my point on Cearr? Cearr is <b>the victim</b>. His entire people.... wiped off the map.... because of Exalts.<br /> <br /> Humanity tends to find a balance when its man vs man. Add in supernatural might and things go haywire.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;because of exalts&quot; yeah, I'd find it weird if Cearr was enraged at all solars, as opposed to just the bull.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need different &quot;races&quot; to define colonialism. The planet (in real life) is populated by groups that crush one another the second one gets some power. Not just Germans curb-stomped other Europeans or China claiming Tibet, Shiites badgering Zoroastrians or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>HmmmI'll concede that. Romans had a colonial empire, and their notion of 'barbarian vs roman' was less developed. But no usually there's an understnading of race when you build a colonial empire. Certainly in the cases your citing (Esp. in the Reconquista).<br /> <br /> Some of the worst &quot;colonial&quot; influence was <i>local. </i>When the French were in North Africa, they showed favoritism to Muslims (monotheistic, easier to learn one language and let the locals be the translators, etc). The French didn't mass-murder non-Muslim locals..... their favoritism encouraged conversion into a new unified entity (whereby a minority in some regions now became the majority). You don't need a full-fledged empire to ruin people's lives - just some power and a few favored locals (and watch the power dynamic ripple along).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Bull's popularity with Ice Walkers is irrelevant - <b><i>whoever</i></b> doesn't like the Ice Walkers is now shitting in their pants that a bunch of psuedo-barbarian tribes are on the move. And like with Cearr, if you just happen to be <i>stuck</i> between two armies when they choose your territory as a battlefield, you're going to go extinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've repeatedly presented the suffering of exalted children as being held in contempt by humanity, being pulled in two directions like people of mixed race in colonial scenerios.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus Christ.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping you're defending genocide as a tongue-in-cheek thing. The point is their victims (if they were alive) wouldn't be bemused.<br /> <br /> Entire cities (men, women, children) were decapitated <i>for giving offense</i> to the wrong person. One of Khan's daughters had everyone killed - and the skulls collected into a pile - such that descriptions claim the bodies made the mountains look small - and the fields were watered red. Another region - known for it's artisans - was annihilated, with the paltry few survivors never restoring the crafts/art they were famous for - until the city was burned a few centuries later and abandoned.<br /> <br /> And when 10% of the DNA in Asia is his - <i>did he need colonies?</i> Murdering or raping the locals <i>made them his</i>..</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Defending genocide&quot;? Alright, now your looking at things stragne. Ghengis Khan was a terrible terrible person. (Although your description are exaggerations). He destroyed the greatest library at Baghdad. <br /> My point was &quot;He's not a colonial empire, he's just a monster&quot;. The tension your repeteadly looking for (Between mortals and Exalts as 2 classes of bein recognized as seperate) relies on a racial understanding of the two (as your hati analaogy suggests). Said doesn't exist. But we'll come back to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because both of them would have been <i>regular people for the rest of their lives </i>had not the Bull or Panther shown up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. That's not the ressult of the sort of relationship your describing. Their lives aren't made worse because of the systemic use of power employed by solars that would breed resentment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't care if she creates one or doesn't. We're discussing <i>the children of Exalts</i>.<br /> <br /> And when <i>anyone remotely aware of the incident hears about it</i>, they're going to hear &quot;oh yeah, 30+ monks were all mass-murdered by a Solar who just <i>spontaneously</i> erupted - mass-murder of the most pious is one of their level 1 powers&quot;. <b>From there</b>, I argue, &quot;no, mortals will not take Solars <i>lightly</i> - including their offspring - because all the famous Celestial Exalts inevitably become famous for the sheer amount of death they can spread&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except where their hailed has heroes (See, Mongols still love Genhgis Kahn). There's a difference between taking lightly and &quot;their children are neither human nor god, and are resented by both and torn betweent them&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the 700 years of Moors enslaving, robbing and killing Iberians <i>in the first place</i>. Everyone was pretty awful, but the Reconquista was always <i>a reaction to</i> that awfulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I again will refrain from commenting on the Reconquista, except that I find any claims of vengance to be out of time after nearly a millenium suspect, and generally take a dimmer view of it then you do by all accounts. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225492#post1225492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded.... <i>whose power is from birth</i>. I <i>suspect</i> they will be less forgiving about a Sun-Kid or Moon-Born. &quot;Being born into power&quot; is <i>exactly</i> what made them strong enough to rule an empire. Unless they have a strong grasp of the power-limits of <i>Children of Exalts</i>, it's a dumb risk to take. <b>Plus</b> if you're still hunting Anathema, then <b>no</b>, you don't want to normalize Anathema-lite. It's going to be <b>way</b> more difficult to find a Lunar if you've taught the populace that the Lunar-lite kid with a shapeshifting charm and silver jewelry is okay to overlook.<br /> <br /> Solars aren't Knights in Shining Armor. They're One-Man-Armies.<br /> <br /> You don't need 300 Solars acting in concert to have something akin to &quot;colonial rule&quot;.<br /> <br /> You need 1 Solar <i>with fucking magic powers</i> rewriting the social, economic and military landscape to do it.<br /> <br /> Who needs a three dozen diplomats to achieve a century-long peace-treaty (say you want to end the Anglo-French Hundred Year's War) when <i>Speed the Wheels </i>says I can achieve any feat within 1 Season (at most).<br /> <br /> Who needs 300 researchers, investigators and statisticians analyzing a bureau for corruption - when Bureau-Rectifying Method can single-handedly let me purge the least useful members, clear corruption, eliminate spies.... for 8m and 1wp? <b>Bam</b>, I can tell an organization to just <i>keep hiring 10% of the staff</i> and my charm will <i>automatically</i> make the least useful members quit, get fired or die - snowballing into hiring only the best-of-the-best within a few weeks of the hiring spree.<br /> <br /> Who needs <i>assassins?</i> At Essence 3, I can use Heavenly Mandate Marking <i>on a mortal servant</i> - send them as an ambassador - and when she meets a king, <i>I can use my charms through her</i>. I can also <i>see everything she sees</i> to create a layout if I plan to kill a target anyways. Awesome. Even if they kill or imprison her, <i>their job is done</i>.<br /> <br /> Solar magic is (and should be) <i>terrifying</i>. And you only need 1 Solar to wreak this havoc.</div> </div> </div> </div>...so, you seem to be confusing things. I'm not saying &quot;Solars are always LG paladins woot woot.&quot;<br /> Solars are human. Their flawed humans. Their very flawed humans, with lots of power.<br /> <br /> Buuuuuuuut. In order for the relationship Exalted children have with the populace to exist as you describe it (Comparable to mixed race individuals in colonial empires in the Americas) won't come about from Celestial exalted, bc those tensions are the result of a system of oppression not 1 lunatic. Being the son of Alexander the Great will hve tensions, but those aren't the same tensions as being a mixed race kid in Mexico city. Your accusing me of shifting the topic, so let me spell out why I'm talking about grown up solar vs colonial empires clearly.<br /> <br /> Every example you've given, except argubly the reconquista, has been about the tensions in an existing colonial empire that relied on racial categories and tensions. These examples and compelling narratives rely on a system and hierarchy of oppression in order to exist on a wide scale. After all, what your describing is bing recognized as a solar child not the child of a specifc solar. &quot;the kings kid&quot; is not the same as &quot;the kid of mixed race&quot;. THere are tensions there but the first one can often be regarded and treated well by those who that are ruled over (Again Solars might be awful people but hey. Greeks love Alexander, Mongols love the Khan, the Brits love Arthur, that's how ancietn heroes work.)<br /> <br /> So. Can there exist a scenerio in creation where tensions of that sort exist? Where you are judged as a 'type' of child not a specific child? Probably! Dragonblooded certainly. Maybe lunars in the Realm or Blessed Isle (although probably not the rest of the threshold, where reception of the exalted is more mixed and where lunars run a large chunk of the world). Solars though? If Cearr hates the Bull, its just the bull. I doubt he hatespanther for being a Solar, or an exalt. The Solars just don't have the unity of presence to be judged or treated a singluar group--except again, in the Realm where they've actively constructed said identiy.<br /> <br /> In most of Creation, being a Solar's kid is more about the specific parent less about 'Solars' as a group. If you want tension that resembles the colonial examples you've given Celestial won't do that for you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T18:32:16-07:00","id":1225500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225498#post1225498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great to hear!<br /> <br /> This is a dodge.<br /> <br /> We're discussing <i>the Children of Exalts</i>. The bulk of which we know about being in 2E.<br /> <br /> <b>The point is</b> you suggested Lunars were &quot;anti-colonial&quot; - <b>and I disagreed vehemently</b>. They're a wannabe ethno-state where if you happen to have (X) power, an entire chapter awaits you to regale you with how you can basically abandon your pre-Lunar existence - you have a whole new set of values, language, codes, goals, etc to adopt - complete with mechanical penalties for refusing to join and rewards for dragging other nascent Lunars kicking-and-screaming to your local den.<br /> <br /> They are <i>every bit as invasive, domineering and cocksure</i> as any Dynast - and if mortals dislike Lunars and Beastmen <i>to start</i>, a Moon-Born who flagrantly shows off their ties isn't going to win any allies locally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey my man, maybe check how it's describe in official press and the core:<b>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> lays out the Silver Pact, the mutual aid society that protects young Lunars from the Wyld Hunt and which organizes the centuries-long war against the Realm<br /> <br /> Core:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So too did the bond\u2019s destruction. The Old Realm fell; the Solars were murdered, their spirits banished beyond Lunar ken. The Lunars changed. They\u2019re still changing. A deep rage lives in their Essence, and a deep wound. Their sleep is tormented by visions of loss, of murder, of the past. The Lunars are compelled to shatter the chains binding them to the past\u2014to tear down the stolen remnants of the First Age, to raze the Sidereal and Terrestrial hegemony that dares to wear the ancient name of the Realm. The Silver Pact exists to facilitate this. (Huh, vengance for a seires of wrongs over the centuries sounds vaguely familair....)(46)<br /> <br /> Some Lunars resist the primal howl that shivers in their Essence. They harness their rage to fight for that which they cherish, or bend their powerful instincts to their own benefit as they walk another road. There is tension between these Lunars and the Silver Pact traditionalists, but also common bonds; the two trade favors and mark debts more often than they shed one another\u2019s blood.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Silver Pact is an alliance of Lunar Exalted united in purpose: to tear down the Realm and free themselves from </span>the ancient bonds they once failed to uphold. The Pact is founded on mutual aid, defense of Luna\u2019s chosen, and opposition to the Realm and its Sidereal masters. The most fundamental duty of any member is to find and rescue newly-Exalted Lunars\u2014a daunting task, given the scope of Creation, but one the Lunar lifestyle is well-suited to. In addition to keeping an ear to the ground as a matter of survival, Silver Pact members have a long-standing practice of rewarding any spirit that brings them news of newly- Exalted brothers and sisters. Once a young Lunar has been taken beyond the immediate reach of the Wyld Hunt, they\u2019re brought before a No Moon affiliated with the Pact, and given the true story of Luna\u2019s Chosen\u2014what they were, what befell them, and why each Lunar Exaltation brings with it a hungry turmoil of the soul.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">After the young Lunar\u2019s caste has been fixed by his No </span>Moon mentor, the Pact\u2019s obligation to him ends unless he decides to participate in its loose, extended network of favor-trading, support, and anti-Realm operations. A young Lunar stands to reap benefits far in excess of what older Pact members ask in return\u2014the Silver Pact\u2019s war against the Realm is a long-term stratagem, one that depends on today\u2019s boon-asking youth to grow into the next century\u2019s indoctrinator, strategist, and war-counselor.(106)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Silver Pact doesn\u2019t try to make </span>its members operate according to some greater battle plan\u2014 Luna\u2019s gifts lend themselves to adaptability and unpredictability, not the grind of empire against empire, and the Realm\u2019s stolen magic and superior numbers make that a losing strategy in any case. Instead, Lunars operate according to their own plans and desires, calling upon other Pact members for assistance where necessary; success and generosity bring greater standing and influence within the Pact.(107)<br /> <br /> (I'm gonna stop here, this was from Ctrl+F of 'Silver Pact' in the core)<br /> <br /> Also, IMHO, you should ignore 2e and fall back on 1e when 2e's conclusions seem contrary to canon. 2e is not in fact the best we have at the moment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T19:10:42-07:00","id":1225506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225498#post1225498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great to hear!<br /> <br /> I know these walls of text are <b>huge</b> - but I think we all <b>agree </b>on this point.<br /> <br /> My point with Deadly Beastman Transformation was that - <i>even if in my mind I know that mechanically it's supposed to be something else</i> - <b>visually, </b>will Creation's inhabitants be able to differentiate? If Moon-Born are supposed to have (in 2E) &quot;some kind of non-Exalted charm that resembles DBT enough for us to get a free-pass to using it in its stead&quot;, <b>then </b>&quot;will Creation's inhabitants see a difference?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Having discussions based on the way things worked in Second Edition\u2014especially when it comes from one of the books with particularly bad setting material and mechanics\u2014is not a thing that's going to lead to productive discussion. <br /> <br /> (Incidentally, people in Creation are unlikely to mistake a Golden Child or Moon-Touched for a Solar or a Lunar. Solars and Lunars have very blatant distinguishing marks, which their children don't inherit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T19:50:15-07:00","id":1225513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225498#post1225498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope.<br /> <br /> 1) This conversation is about <i>the Children of Exalts</i>, not about Lyta's motives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And you flubbed the details of Lyta's Second Breath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) The argument is that <i>fresh fear of the Solar Exalted</i> will motivate <i>anyone who values their lives</i> to report anything remotely (obviously) Solar. </div> </div> </div>I was not actually making an argument. However, I will reiterate one now that the reason that people fear Solars is because they think of them as demons, and that the people who become them do so because they have a moral failing that allows a sorcerer of old who stole the power of the heavens to hollow them out. Any attempts to the contrary are countered with &quot;they're just acting the part now until you drop your guard!&quot;<br /> <br /> This isn't an empire. This is, from the view of an Immaculate believer, The Corruption, followed by Hard Women Making Hard Decisions (to kill the unfortunate and free them from this suffering). Anathema-Spawn are not regarded as being of mixed ancestry, but flat out cursed by the residue of said Corruption. This is, of course, assuming that someone doesn't ask questions that require the fallback position of &quot;they're actually Exalted, but their power is too great and causes them to become unhinged and dangerous&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is the central piece of everything involving the term Anathema. It overrides any factors of culture or blood as a matter of course. You even acknowledge it in this next paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Lyta's motives are <i>irrelevant</i> except to mind-readers. The end-result is 30 or so dead monks (including Dragon Blooded) because 1 Solar Anathema suddenly &quot;sold her soul to the Yozis for power&quot;. All law-abiding citizens are expected to report potential Anathema sightings if they value their lives. We repeat, 30 something dead citizens because of 1 crazed, blood-thirsty anathema stole a few drops of Sun-powered magic. </div> </div> </div>30 Dead Monks is the name of my Castlevania/Chant tribute band!<br /> <br /> Judging from the Immaculate martial arts across editions, she'd never be able to accomplish this, even in EX3 with supernal martial arts boosting her up to higher-Essence Tiger style Charms and possibly also using a Dragon style's mid-tier. Her &quot;rampage&quot; is mostly taking out those two students who were sexually harassing her in the caste book. 2e was very... extra about this. The account of her escape in her original appearance has her killing two Dragon-Blooded and then running like hell, finding a Manse, and then getting Mr. Wizarded out by a Sidereal. She only kills two more Dragon-Blooded before getting on the boat out, and they weren't even Immaculate martial artists. Someone must have thought that this was too grounded for a Solar in the supremely Solar-loving (yet also hating) 2e, so we got that account from CoCD: Blessed Isle, which I recall as always having been lambasted when it came up. I never thought that the day would come that someone would take it seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a dodge. </div> </div> </div>No, the TSR was a dodge. I'm not dodging just because I'm bringing up how badly it was conceptualized and written to hide the giant hole (lack of Lunar heat) that no one saw fit to try and repair until 3e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're discussing <i>the Children of Exalts</i>. The bulk of which we know about being in 2E. </div> </div> </div>No, the bulk of what I recall stretches originally from 2001 with the glossary drip to around 2005 or 2006. I can include the latter, because the 2e core was mad delayed - a february release turned into april.<br /> <br /> And, originally, the mentions of the children of Exalted started out as just being prone to having the second sight or some other quirks; otherwise, they were normal humans in every respect. Then came the chart in Exalted: the Abyssals, page 270, and then there was the player's guide. Ah, the player's guide... such a charlie foxtrot. You could dump the merits and flaws, the god-blood section, the martial arts, and you'd have a much more sensible title. Truly, it set the way for Scroll of Heroes in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The point is</b> you suggested Lunars were &quot;anti-colonial&quot; - <b>and I disagreed vehemently</b>. They're a wannabe ethno-state where if you happen to have (X) power, an entire chapter awaits you to regale you with how you can basically abandon your pre-Lunar existence - you have a whole new set of values, language, codes, goals, etc to adopt - complete with mechanical penalties for refusing to join and rewards for dragging other nascent Lunars kicking-and-screaming to your local den.<br /> <br /> They are <i>every bit as invasive, domineering and cocksure</i> as any Dynast - and if mortals dislike Lunars and Beastmen <i>to start</i>, a Moon-Born who flagrantly shows off their ties isn't going to win any allies locally. </div> </div> </div>You can't be an ethno-state if you don't champion an ethnicity... or anything else at all, for that matter, which was about the state of Lunars in 2e. Just 300 souls shackled to assholes who kept reincarnating, and who had to shuffle the mortal coil to accomplish anything of note. I've been saying good riddance to it since the EX3 announcement back in 2012, and I'll say it again today.<br /> <br /> (Seriously, Celestials reincarnating across lives and the power going to adults was supposed to be a setup to avoid this thread and others like it. This is only the second time I've seen someone insist otherwise, and the other example was back during the heyday of the Exalted Compendium, when someone was shouting about the Dawn caste mark being &quot;a WW2 Japanese battle-flag.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T22:18:36-07:00","id":1225522,"title":"","content":"I just realized I'm talking with multiple people but similar chains. I will try to reduce:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225499#post1225499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;because of exalts&quot; yeah, I'd find it weird if Cearr was enraged at all solars, as opposed to just the bull.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing the point.<br /> <br /> One Exalt. The Bull. Was sufficient. To organize and lead. An Icewalker movement. Resulting in a massive war. Which killed off his people.<br /> <br /> Cearr didn't need to hate all 299 other Solars banded together into a League of Villains. He doesn't even need to know about the Bulls other allies. One Solar was sufficient for him to realize &quot;yeah, the Dragon-Blooded were 100% right, now my entire life is ashes, and unless I want to join them all in Oblivion, making a deal with hell itself is my best chance of evening the odds.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exalts are scary people if you're not on their good side.<br /> <br /> <b>re: Genghis Khan</b><br /> A cursory look at his destruction includes &quot;killing 5% of the world population&quot;. That includes 500,000 Ukranians, 700,000 Mervians (extinct), 1,000,000 Hungarians (50% of the population), 1,000,000+ in Nishapur (extinct), a staggering 2,250,000 Persians (90%) and allegedly 60,000,000 dead in China according to Chinese Dynast census records. <b>His policy</b> was to spare engineers and artisans (and sometimes doctors) - <b>not farmers</b> - so the bigger two were a mix of warfare and subsequent famine.<br /> <br /> And when Muslim states wanted Halal food, and I quote &quot;By the aid of heaven, we have pacified you - <b>you are our slaves</b> - yet you do not eat our food or drink! How can this be right?&quot; And after <i>making them eat</i>, added &quot;If you slaughter sheep, you will be guilty of a crime&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is <b>not &quot;woke&quot;</b> or &quot;enlightened&quot; to defend genocide just because a non-European committed it.<br /> <br /> <i>And by the way</i>, Hispanic here. A <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/article/us-mexico-archaeology-skulls-idUSKBN19M3Q6\" target=\"_blank\">new <i>skull covered tower</i></a> was unearthed last year in Mexico City, including the skulls of men, women and children from tributary-states that the Aztecs dominated. In Peru, there's an awesome statue <i>of a <a href=\"https://wayfaringadventure.files.wordpress.com/2015/04/img_3919.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Tarabicos ripping out a human heart and eating it</a> </i>- this is a <b>modern</b> statue, because a decoration was needed for a park. And <i>my own ancestors</i> included <i>head-hunters</i> - <b>please don't feel a need</b> to correct me on how any of these heritages &quot;weren't really colonial empires&quot; or &quot;not that violent&quot;. <i>Minorities in the US</i> aren't minorities <i>in the world</i> and we certainly have our fair share of awesome warlords.<br /> <br /> <b>re: Reconquista</b><br /> I don't see what is &quot;out of time&quot; when the Reconquista was in the 1400s and so were the Moors. It was 700 years of Conquest because the Caliphates <i>kept replacing each other </i>- often with something worse - so each generation in each province had <i>their own</i> experience with the invaders + ancestral hatreds. This is not &quot;esoteric history&quot;. It might be arcane to an Anglo-Saxon or Nord - but the Greeks, the Italians, the Spanish and Portuguese <i>were all fighting for centuries</i> against invading civilizations. So if you can't differentiate <i>Andalusia</i> from <i>Aragon</i>, <i>thank you for refraining</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>re: the term in the CF's title</b><br /> <i>Oh that</i>. Crazy how convoluted discussion becomes when you can't even use the proper term, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's almost like <i>all these other languages and cultures</i> - in which <i>tone and intent</i> matter more than an arbitrary combo of letters - <i>might be on to something, eh?</i><br /> <br /> <b>re: regional favorites</b><br /> I'm not ignoring &quot;Exalts&quot; (nor <i>Children of Exalts</i>) &quot;from your home town&quot;. Sure, you have a few locals who like you.<br /> <br /> That means nothing positive to.... rival towns? trade caravans? pilgrims passing through? bandits you beat up? local mercenaries you trumped (and now the survivors go back to the city-state that hired them to report they need more help)? Once word spreads - and the Wyld hunt shows up to interrogate or kill the locals - then you're stuck without your &quot;friendly villagers&quot; and are stuck in a world that only judges you on appearances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225499#post1225499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HmmmI'll concede that. Romans had a colonial empire, and their notion of 'barbarian vs roman' was less developed. But no usually there's an understnading of race when you build a colonial empire. Certainly in the cases your citing (Esp. in the Reconquista).</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Christ, no.</b> Their sense of barbarian was fully developed. Slavery is derived from Slavs (who were the slaves) - it wasn't until you have the Ottomans and Moors invading Europe for 700 years - that it began to take a &quot;racial&quot; overtone. If you think what Roseanne Barr tweeted was offensive, I know some Omani who think Europeans <i>look like swine</i>. <b>Same intent to offend</b>. Except this slur goes back 1.5 thousand years when &quot;the swine&quot; refused to convert.<br /> <br /> Romans didn't care about your phenotype (what most Americans consider race). There were Romans from throughout the Empire - if you speak Latin, act Roman, embrace Roman gods and Roman custom, you're Romanized. If you don't, you're barbaric. Nords? Barbarian! Celts? Barbarians! Slavs? Barbarians! Even the Iberians were <i>barbarian</i> until they became <i>Latinized</i> (and I think the joke goes &quot;Romans - but with trashy accents&quot; lol). And the Iberians <i>themselves</i> weren't some fictitious &quot;white race&quot; - even the Romans were aware you had at least 3 <i>unrelated</i> groups (the Basque to the NE who <i>2,000 years later</i> still speak a non-Indo-European tongue... a multitiude of Celts from Galicia to Catalonia, who were different enough that <i>they killed each other</i>.... and a 3rd Med mix of Phoenician, Libyan, Greek and other sailors on the coast. Whether Rome spared or destroyed you was up to whether or not you assimilated to their culture or continued being <i>barbaros</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>And the Spanish copied this model</b>. Do you think <i>black Conquistadors</i> were slaves? Here's one of my <a href=\"https://www.sdmart.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/08/Capture-1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">favorite Casta Paintings</a> - a relationship that would have gotten someone <i>lynched</i> in America 50 years ago was <i>accepted by Church and Crown 400-fucking-years ago</i>. <b>Venezuela </b>had a <i>race war</i> defined by Creoles vs Peninsulares (not skin color). <b>Puerto Rico</b> outlawed slavery <i>to encourage Anglo &amp; French slaves to come</i> because those countries <i>aren't Spanish</i>. <b> Paraguay</b> outlawed same-race marriage in 1814 <i>to encourage more mixing </i>(which was prevalent with Spaniards) and convince English/French to <i>get the fuck out</i>. There are <i>multiple</i> <b>Central American</b> statues to Gonzalo Guerrero celebrating <i><a href=\"http://www.theyucatantimes.com/2014/09/how-did-the-first-mestizo-children-were-born-in-the-yucatan-peninsula/\" target=\"_blank\">his children</a> (</i>warning - English might consider the <i>proper term which we all use</i> a slur, but the fact that we glorify the mixture <i>with statues</i> of a Spanish-soldier who refused to leave his Native-wife - should dictate that it's not a pejorative).<br /> <br /> <b>Please</b> do not conflate the North American obsession with skin color - to some eternal war-of-the-phenotypes that <i>every other culture and civilization on the planet</i> is expected to have experienced. Yes, bigotry exists in the world - but everyone has their own flavors, unrelated to the British and French models (who weren't even <i>popular</i> with other Europeans).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225499#post1225499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3E Lunars</div> </div> </div> </div>This forum needs an eggplant emoji. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225506#post1225506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having discussions based on the way things worked in Second Edition\u2014especially when it comes from one of the books with particularly bad setting material and mechanics\u2014is not a thing that's going to lead to productive discussion.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, people in Creation are unlikely to mistake a Golden Child or Moon-Touched for a Solar or a Lunar. Solars and Lunars have very blatant distinguishing marks, which their children don't inherit)</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread is named after the 2E term - because that's where the bulk of experiences are probably at - ergo, I don't see anything unproductive making reference to that context.<br /> <br /> And in that edition - where one <i>already figures</i> the <i>Children of Exalts</i> aren't some Exalted-lite - when it references Moon-Touched having some kind of (warform-like-power, <i>regardless of mechanics</i>) - one figured that if a villager saw it in action, they'd go tell a monk (or the like). I can't imagine Bob the Farmer telling Timmy the Woodcutter &quot;oh no friend, wait - in Anathema class, a clear sign of the soulless ones is a silver emblem on their forehead once they use too much Peripheral essence - let's not pre-judge our 8ft tall half-wolf monster-friend by informing the monks&quot;.<br /> <br /> If 3E <i>Children of Exalts</i> have no such thing to clue locals in.... then good for them.<br /> <br /> I don't defacto see it as unproductive tho to appreciate the implied and explicit tensions (in the 2E) text, much like it's not unproductive for a Tiefling or Half-Orc to be singled out as &quot;yeah, you're not a full Devil or full Orc - but you realize that doesn't assuage the woes of locals - so don't expect a free pass.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't be an ethno-state if you don't champion an ethnicity... or anything else at all, for that matter, which was about the state of Lunars in 2e. Just 300 souls shackled to assholes who kept reincarnating, and who had to shuffle the mortal coil to accomplish anything of note. I've been saying good riddance to it since the EX3 announcement back in 2012, and I'll say it again today. </div> </div> </div>I think we have differing definitions of ethnicity.<br /> <br /> As aforementioned, I <b>don't </b>think the &quot;white race&quot; folks <i>are logical</i>. And Italian, an Irishman, a Swede and a Romanian have fuck-all in common ethnically. But they <b>still </b>think there's some sort of &quot;ethnic&quot; identity in being &quot;white&quot;. <b>Therefore</b>, I don't need Lunars to behave <i>logically</i> to compare them. They're <b>both </b>groups who latch on to some <b>superficial </b>trait - and imagined that's enough to work together, share values, language, customs, etc - quickly overriding an entire lifetime of pre-existing, pre-defining values, culture, beliefs, etc.<br /> <br /> Plus I always imagined that the implication was that one's Beastmen <b>are</b> your tribes. It's a way to &quot;rebuild&quot; Werewolf the Apocalypse. If the Werewolves were essentially shifters who learned &quot;gifts&quot; from totemic spirits.... then the goal is to Breed-True, using Lunar charms that let you custom-pick inherited mutations, favoring things like &quot;Hidden Mutation&quot; so your offspring can revert to human form (or start as it). <b>And then</b> if your Lunar breeds with local animal/totem gods? If the divine essence is higher, you could produce <b>God-Blooded Beastmen </b>that Breed-True. <b>Voila!</b> You've created a race of moon-worshipping humanoids with a couple mutations for healing and shapeshifting - but most of their actual charms have to be Spirit Charms.<br /> <br /> And if it's a powerful totemic spirit? Even better. At least by 2E rules, you could have a higher Inheritance score - so more bonus points - so you don't need as many flaw-mutations to balance the merit-mutations. So your beastmen could be <b>very human</b>, acquiring mutations - and then bonus mutations that hide the blatant ones. Powerful spirits would thus have powerful servitors in a tribe, long after their Lunar progenitor dies off.<br /> <br /> I think 1E and 2E <i>implied</i> the &quot;society&quot; of Werewolf the Apocalypse, without actually calculating <i>if it should exist in the 2E</i>.<br /> <br /> But I'm done quibbling. I love your finish on them and I look forward to giving them a round 2 (even if I <i>probably</i> still do my own thing). <hr /><br /> <b>TLDR:<br /> re: Children of Exalts</b><br /> Going off 2E - which the word in the title <i>is explicitly from</i> - the descriptions in the book <b>and</b> the nature of charms both give good reason to think the Wyld Hunt (and others) <b>will</b> be problematic for <i>the Children of Exalts</i> the second you use some blatant power that scares off a local villager. Examples like Deadly Beastman Transformation (or something visually <i>like it</i>) would alarm most humans. <b>If 3E </b><i>children of Exalts</i> have nothing to fear from the Wyld Hunt? <i>Good for them</i> I guess. But I don't see the fault in presuming <i>they'll have issues due to their lineage</i> when the 2E book <i>explicitly says they have issues due to their lineage</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>re: History</b><br /> I've said it before - <i>non-Europeans</i> <b>don't need</b> self-flaggellating Americans to deny <i>the atrocities that are some of our foundational histories</i>, just because the misinformed think-gooder wants to imagine we're all benign noble savages who never hurt a fly before colonialism. <i>We had badass warlords, conquests and destruction too</i>. And there have been times when it's the Europeans who were on the wrong end of a sword.<br /> <br /> With respect to <i>the topic of the thread</i>, the <i>Children of Exalts</i> shouldn't thus be limited to comparisons to being mixed-blooded. It's about <i>politics</i>, not blood. The Aztecs, Genghis Khan or even Simon Bolivar didn't give a shit about your complexion - being born to the wrong lineage was <i>sufficient</i>. And being a Celestial Exalts child just doesn't seem healthy if anyone finds out.<br /> <br /> <b>re: Lunars</b><br /> More eggplant emojis regarding 3E. This is probably where <i>I'm self-flaggellating</i>, but they're the dopest. And I'm really curious about their <i>fecundity</i>, since everything suggested they'd have the most <i>Children of Exalts</i>, and yet I'm not sure if this was ever explicit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":".  typos, restructure, more typos 06-07-2018, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T07:06:30-07:00","id":1225566,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a>, the reason Vance said that using 2E material is non-productive is MOST 2E material has been or probably will be tossed out. Especially anything close to approaching squick areas (going from my following of the Devs I think I am confident in stating this). Hence their repeated emphasis that if any canon point should be used it\u2019s FIRST edition not second. Even then, I would expect potentially heavy overhauls of lore such as what has occurred with the Realm and Dragonblooded society in general in third edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:46:17-07:00","id":1225597,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the only splats I expect to go on 2e stuff are alchemicals and infernals.<br /> <br /> And even then, infernals is gonna get a heavy rewrite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:51:35-07:00","id":1225600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225597#post1225597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the only splats I expect to go on 2e stuff are alchemicals and infernals.<br /> <br /> And even then, infernals is gonna get a heavy rewrite.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s where I am at, heck, even 1st edition material probably can be chucked in cases like Dragon-blooded, where the basic changes to how dragon-blooded work with progenitive essence has huge downstream implications that knock a decent chunk of even 1st ed DB lore flat on its ass iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T09:01:14-07:00","id":1225602,"title":"","content":"The new paradigm does mean that it'll be harder to tell the child of an abyssal or infernal from a ghost- or demon-blooded, but given that the two haven't existed long enough for anyone with that pedigree to be PC material in the standard setting it's not a huge issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T09:09:41-07:00","id":1225605,"title":"","content":"@Salagimsim<br /> <br /> I think the issue here is that most of the people you're engaging in debate with think of the 2e lore and mechanics you are referencing as, at best, poorly considered and at worst badly written and detrimental to the overall quality of the game and setting.<br /> <br /> It's not good, and that's why it's basically being completely binned and redone from the ground up by the devs for 3e.<br /> <br /> So, your arguments aren't super compelling when they're propped up by, or use as reference supporting points, the very rules that most of the people on the forum have already rejected as being a flaming dumpster fire of poorly considered and imbalanced mechanics.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't expect most people to be able to distinguish between a Moon Touched and, say, a god or godblooded or any number of other weird supernatural things. Sure, an immaculate monk or a scholar or shaman may be able to tell that this is a child of a Lunar, but most people don't have the knowledge base to know that- many of them may not even know that Moon Touched can even exist.<br /> <br /> There's a huge variety of different weird supernatural things in Creation, and most people don't know the clean-cut categories that we do- they might not be able to distinguish a obscure demon from a god or elemental. If someone turns into a wolf, there might be an number of explanations for the average commoner or what have you. They could be a god or spirit, or they could be a sorcerer, or some other weird thing that happens to exist. Cursed by a sorcerer, or blessed by a god generations ago.<br /> <br /> That's why you have people with the specialized knowledge to be able to tell them apart and, if need be, placate or exorcise them. So the idea that literally everyone will look at someone turning into a wolf-man and go, &quot;Aha! A Moon-Touched child of a Lunar Anathema! It's time to form a mob!&quot;.. well, it strikes me as unlikely.<br /> <br /> And of course, that's assuming people aren't just.. ok.. with it. Not everywhere in the world hates Lunars. Some people won't care that much. Others will eagerly accept a powerful ally with magical powers, regardless of their provenance. Having a person on your side who can turn into a big wolf can be really, really handy when your world is full of terrifying supernatural monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T11:12:02-07:00","id":1225634,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4578_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4578\" data-vbnamecard=\"4578\">Zale</a> <br /> <b>Re: Editions</b><br /> I'm 100% with moving on to 3E. I'm not remotely opposed to this. I'm <i>excited</i> for that material.<br /> <br /> But <i>the title of the thread itself</i> <i>explicitly uses the 2E term</i>. Ergo, pretending 2E context or experience is <i>irrelevant</i> is.... anachronistic? Is that the world? You can't use 3E to judge a 2E term, much like you can't use (for the historical tangents) &quot;3E American identity politics&quot; to explain &quot;2E Iberian-Moorish warfare&quot; or &quot;1E Roman Empires&quot;. <br /> <br /> A lot of the back-and-forth has been people wanting to just <i>shrug</i> and ignore 2E even when discussing 2E terms or 2E experiences in a thread <i>titled by</i> a 2E term.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Distinguishing Supernaturals</b><br /> This is the crux of the matter.<br /> <br /> Operating off previous editions, I always conceptualized the world as one in which <i>the supernatural is repressed</i>. It's abundant! But the Immaculate Order does not approve of gods setting up cults; does not show kindness to ghosts (except to beat them into reincarnation); does not like demons wandering..... and (explicitly) does not tolerate Anathema (including persecuting known allies, family, etc all to help hunt them down sooner). <b>In addition</b>, the Deathlords, ancient Lunars like Ma-Ha-Suchi and similar horrors reinforce that <i>supernatural stuff is bad for humanity </i>and the Bull of the North reminds us that <i>even our heroes will bring bloodshed</i>. <b>There is magic everywhere</b>, but <i>it's the Age of Sorrows</i>.<br /> <br /> In such a setting, out-of-character knowledge of &quot;just how you got your magic powers&quot; is <i>irrelevant</i>. A human who is <i>shapeshifting</i> is neither 100% human nor a Terrestrial Exalt - ergo, <i>you get scrutinized</i>. As aforementioned, I could build a viable shapeshifter using <i>just mutations</i> in 1E - long before the Player's Guide - and it was treated like any other Moon-tainted man-monster. Local villagers <i>don't need</i> specialized knowledge to fear you - there's a metric fuckton of supernatural horrors <i>in the setting</i> to remind mortals that danger lurks.<br /> <br /> If 3E Exalted is a more light-hearted affair akin to 5E D&amp;D seeing Genasi, Half-Orcs, Dragonborn, Tieflings running around willy nilly in the Imperial City and the local humans no longer freak out? Cool. I'm not objecting. But that's a tonal shift far from what I thought was the status quo. And in case it needs repeating, <i>the thread uses an explicitly 2E term</i>, so the presumption that 2E is preemptively deleted from the convo just doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225597#post1225597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the only splats I expect to go on 2e stuff are alchemicals and infernals.<br /> <br /> And even then, Infernals is gonna get a heavy rewrite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved the 2E Infernals (even if their fluff chapter was <i>overlookable</i>). Their charm rework fills me with dread and anticipation. The nature of charms with in-built compulsions and penalties was perma-narrative fuel (essentially letting players tell their ST what kind of twists interest them based on the side-effects they embraced in their charms). It was a huge leap over <i>eh, spend magic, get successes</i>.<br /> <br /> But if Exigents are awesome enough, there will probably never be a splat-focused argument <i>again </i>since people will just home-brew their personal project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:33:39-07:00","id":1225697,"title":"","content":"It's not a second edition term. It's a first edition one. In virtually every possible fashion, first edition is a better reference with stronger continuity with material that will appear in Third Edition in terms of lore material.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a previous edition which is relevant to discussions of Third Edition fluff, then First Edition should be your point of reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:07:18-07:00","id":1225740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225697#post1225697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a second edition term. It's a first edition one. In virtually every possible fashion, first edition is a better reference with stronger continuity with material that will appear in Third Edition in terms of lore material.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a previous edition which is relevant to discussions of Third Edition fluff, then First Edition should be your point of reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, this is what I was trying to get at <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a>, it\u2019s mostly if you are going to reference specific things, I\u2019d recommend going with the even older material of 1st edition if looking backward. Now, that is not to say there won\u2019t probably be changes from that (dragon-blooded are imo extremely different than either previous incarnations) but it places the market down on where to start from. Between players I am gearing up to run for and a game I\u2019m participating in, it will take time to adjust to the new paradigms, but on the whole it\u2019s removed a lot of the...as zale said problematic parts of 2nd edition\u2019s framing of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T18:29:02-07:00","id":1225786,"title":"","content":"EX3 isn't light-hearted, I'd say. More that 2e was not done any favors by the old hats from the WoD who thought that Lunar elders should be as painfully awful id dumping grounds as Sabbat elders, which is what gave us the Rutting Pens and an aimless, terrible Silver Pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T19:33:18-07:00","id":1225799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1225634#post1225634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If 3E Exalted is a more light-hearted affair akin to 5E D&amp;D seeing Genasi, Half-Orcs, Dragonborn, Tieflings running around willy nilly in the Imperial City and the local humans no longer freak out? Cool. I'm not objecting. But that's a tonal shift far from what I thought was the status quo. And in case it needs repeating, <i>the thread uses an explicitly 2E term</i>, so the presumption that 2E is preemptively deleted from the convo just doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wouldn't call it light-hearted, in the sense of the existence of certain supernatural powers being something that people respond to casually. But I would say it's something that a greater variety of communities have more agency over.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs an example, the Southeast has Ysyr, with its widespread mutation and sorcerers. I wouldn't describe that as light-hearted, given how it's used as a basis of social stratification and a tool of imperialist expansion. At the same time, it's something that exists apart from the Exalted, and is empowering a society without regards to them. The Creation of Third Edition has things of such a nature scattered all over; the Western Isle where the forge goddess teaches superlative metal working, Medo's ghost janissaries, lots of things.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would say that it's not treated casually, but <i>cautiously</i>; it's potentially dangerous, and in many cases their capacity to wield and harness it is limited, but it's something that they can negotiate with to mutual benefit, and most communities can probably be assumed to have members that are a dab hand at such negotiation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T14:21:38-07:00","id":1226295,"title":"","content":"A major objective with 3e lore is to address where previous editions have done a questionable job at presenting what Creation looks like on the ground level.<br /> <br /> For example the Immaculate Order has suffered immensely from the fact that the gameline imposed Peleps Deled on them as a figurehead when Kasif is much closer to a 'normal' Immaculate Monk while Deled is basically a Warhammer 40,000 character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 06-11-2018, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T17:53:18-07:00","id":1226620,"title":"","content":"It is in general a lot less 40k, &quot;burn the heretic, the xeno, and the mutant&quot;, but that doesn't mean &quot;happy catgirl adventures forever&quot;. It just means a beastperson will be regarded with suspicion and caution, and probably used as a scapegoat in the event of bad events, but without the default answer being &quot;get the lynch mob&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T07:14:28-07:00","id":1226767,"title":"","content":"There confirmation bias concerning beastfolk and how they generally come about that's been informing what the common person thinks of them.<br /> It's easy to fall for the visceral aspect of Ma-Ha-Suchi's Rutting Pens and ignore the snakefolk community in Great Forks that Ophilis Ses comes from, the latter isn't exactly liked and is heavily associated with the Tang-Zen crime syndicate (the former probably caused the latter but logic is rarely a component of racism) but they're not monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T10:29:51-07:00","id":1226834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226767#post1226767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">logic is rarely a component of racism</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth. Nails it on the head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226767#post1226767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There confirmation bias concerning beastfolk and how they generally come about that's been informing what the common person thinks of them.<br /> It's easy to fall for the visceral aspect of Ma-Ha-Suchi's Rutting Pens and ignore the snakefolk community in Great Forks that Ophilis Ses comes from, the latter isn't exactly liked and is heavily associated with the Tang-Zen crime syndicate (the former probably caused the latter but logic is rarely a component of racism) but they're not monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastmen don't spawn from people banging the family dog. It's either:<br /> <br /> (a) <i>anathema </i>(the cannibal-shapeshifters who think destabilizing the Realm is a virtue, despite that humans might <i>like</i> stability)<br /> <br /> (b) Wyld Mutants (those crazy, stupid or desperate enough - be they savages or criminals - to muck around near soul-eating Fair Folk)<br /> <br /> Unless half-animal god-blooded (from totemic gods) are super common in 3E, I don't see much change in this problematic origin story. <hr /><br /> And mutations aren't just <i>physical</i> - they're <i>behavioral</i>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Do the An-Teng snakemen separate themselves by gender for <i>cultural</i> or <i>instinctual</i> reasons? Does the Tang-Zen snakemen association have origins in how their breed of snake &quot;view the world&quot;?<br /> <br /> Would a &quot;cat girl&quot; not have the impulse to <i>torture and kill small animals</i> for practice? At what point does it go from &quot;she likes hunting for food&quot; to &quot;why does she collect dead rats and kill doves?&quot;<br /> <br /> How about a &quot;cute neighborhood hamster girl&quot; - <i>who devours her children </i>when stressed? What if she (prior to this) was watching over village children as some local duty when suddenly some demon attacks (and the village finds her freaking out in a basement with a half-dozen devoured children)?<br /> <br /> How about cow or deer beastmen who <i>stomp birds to death and eat them raw</i>? These &quot;herbivores&quot; do so for minerals to promote antler/horn growth.<br /> <br /> Snake-men who practice cannibalism? Or who have thuggee-style strangulation of travelers?<br /> <br /> Chimp warfare. <i>They literally rip each other apart</i> without weapons. How would Nexus crowds react to seeing competing gangs rip limbs-and-meat off bone from living rivals? No knives needed, just brute-force &quot;arm leaves socket&quot; and &quot;your eye/cheek/nose have been torn off&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sexually frustrated sea otters sometimes rape baby seals.<br /> <br /> Ducks have been known to <i>crash</i> females out of the air - and still <i>fornicate</i> with the broken-necked corpse. They have penis and vagina <b>specifically</b> evolved because of rape-as-breeding-method. How are duck-men going to behave locally?<br /> <br /> Bowerbird-men might be great artists - or thieves who steal shit to build their nests.<br /> <br /> Cuckoo-bird-women! They lay their eggs in the nests of other birds (so they'll be raised by someone else) <b>and</b> sometimes roll existing eggs out of the nest (so they smash on the ground below). What happens when cuckoo-women engage in Changeling-like &quot;oooo maybe I can murder someone's baby and switch in mine, while they're small, before they notice the difference, yes that makes sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> Woodpeckers who <i>peck babies to death</i> (from other species). There are some great/horrific videos of them cracking over baby bird skulls to eat the brains.<br /> <br /> Dung-beetle beastmen who constantly smell like shit?<br /> <br /> Mantis or spider-women who kill and eat their mates?<br /> <br /> Octopus-women who maybe <i>rip your genitals off</i> in the &quot;heat of the moment&quot; because that's how they reproduce? Or Octopus-men who rip their penis and throw it at you - and then suffer from a strange wasting dementia until they die?<br /> <br /> There are <b>wonderful horrors</b> to be explored in applying beastial-traits to human society.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I like shapeshifters. I like monsters. These are not niches I want to &quot;punish&quot;.<br /> <br /> But centaurs, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jor\u014dgumo\" target=\"_blank\">jor</a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jor%C5%8Dgumo\" target=\"_blank\">\u014d</a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jor\u014dgumo\" target=\"_blank\">gumo</a>, harpies, sirens, etc - were always <i>monsters</i> in some fashion to humanity. They weren't cosplayers with faux cat-ears at a con.<br /> <br /> And even if they don't have animalistic-instincts.... there's no way for regular humans to <i>know</i> that as true. The hypothetical racists might be right.<br /> <br /> <i>Plus</i> don't forget humans eating <i>bushmeat</i>. If humans have no problem devouring &quot;our cousins&quot; (I saw a video yesterday cooking a fresh-kill with a blow torch, their face and hair and everything still visible as flames singed the corpse)..... why would beastmen take issue devouring us?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":".  typos 06-12-2018, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T10:58:25-07:00","id":1226846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226834#post1226834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226767#post1226767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">logic is rarely a component of racism</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth. Nails it on the head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure didn't take you long to get from there to\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226834#post1226834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hypothetical racists might be right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talk about a 180\u00b0!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226834#post1226834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beastmen don't spawn from people banging the family dog. It's either:<br /> <br /> (a) <i>anathema </i>(the cannibal-shapeshifters who think destabilizing the Realm is a virtue, despite that humans might <i>like</i> stability)<br /> <br /> (b) Wyld Mutants (those crazy, stupid or desperate enough - be they savages or criminals - to muck around near soul-eating Fair Folk)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're leaving off a veritable cornucopia of options, from a people living on demesnes that warp their bodies over time, to transfigurations from the gods, to being the product of sorcery (including being put together by a neomah, <b>which you know is an option</b>), to just being the children of two beastfolk!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226834#post1226834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And mutations aren't just <i>physical</i> - they're <i>behavioral</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to cite that being the case in any of the Exalted books? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226834#post1226834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a &quot;cat girl&quot; not have the impulse to <i>torture and kill small animals</i> for practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeesh. The game runs with the assumption that cosmetics aside, <i>Beastfolk are human</i>. If the Wings mutation came with the urge to hide your baby in someone else's crib, <i>the books would give that a mention</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226834#post1226834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great! Monsters <i>are not beastfolk</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226834#post1226834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hypothetical racists might be right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hypothetical or not, racists are wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-12-2018, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T11:04:16-07:00","id":1226849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226834#post1226834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beastmen don't spawn from people banging the family dog. It's either:<br /> <br /> (a) <i>anathema </i>(the cannibal-shapeshifters who think destabilizing the Realm is a virtue, despite that humans might <i>like</i> stability)<br /> <br /> (b) Wyld Mutants (those crazy, stupid or desperate enough - be they savages or criminals - to muck around near soul-eating Fair Folk)<br /> <br /> Unless half-animal god-blooded (from totemic gods) are super common in 3E, I don't see much change in this problematic origin story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess what, sometimes things in Creation happen without apparent explanation. The pro-mystery angle of EX3 means that there are just some beastfolk who have never not known a time when their people were anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And mutations aren't just <i>physical</i> - they're <i>behavioral</i>. </div> </div> </div>Only if they say they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the An-Teng snakemen separate themselves by gender for <i>cultural</i> or <i>instinctual</i> reasons? </div> </div> </div>Explicitly from acculturation, noted in the very same paragraph where they were introduced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the Tang-Zen snakemen association have origins in how their breed of snake &quot;view the world&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Probably never going to be answered, on account of how this edition isn't interested in putting small portions under a microscope. Probably not, in any case, because they have a culture of their own, from Great Forks, that is probably way more important than early pulp barrel bottom-scraping for characterization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would a &quot;cat girl&quot; not have the impulse to <i>torture and kill small animals</i> for practice? </div> </div> </div>I'm going to guess no, on the same basis that Lunars aren't going to be forbidden from having familiars antagonistic to their totem beasts in this edition, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At what point does it go from &quot;she likes hunting for food&quot; to &quot;why does she collect dead rats and kill doves?&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's probably an individual thing. A lot of cats can be socialized to not do this, so a human with some cat features might not feel a pull. If there are changes to the digestive system, then vegetarianism and the like are out of the question, but that doesn't need to jump off the edge and become a more profound sadist than Okita Sougo from Gintama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about a &quot;cute neighborhood hamster girl&quot; - <i>who devours her children </i>when stressed? What if she (prior to this) was watching over village children as some local duty when suddenly some demon attacks (and the village finds her freaking out in a basement with a half-dozen devoured children)? </div> </div> </div>This is getting very silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about cow or deer beastmen who <i>stomp birds to death and eat them raw</i>? These &quot;herbivores&quot; do so for minerals to promote antler/horn growth. </div> </div> </div>If they have another source of calcium, they probably won't bother. Also, being humans, they're more likely to just make a typical meal and crunch the bones down... which humans also do if they need sources of calcium. Keeping birds to lay eggs and eating the shells is another option. So, there is some influence here, if there are huge racks getting grown as status displays (they probably would be, since anything that someone can lord over another will probably be used as such), but it doesn't mean crushing a bird in the field and eating the raw gore and bones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Snake-men who practice cannibalism? </div> </div> </div>There are humans who practice cannibalism without having snake features.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or who have thuggee-style strangulation of travelers? </div> </div> </div>A common misconception is that constrictors strangle. They actually pulsate their abdominal muscles to stop the circulatory system altogether. This isn't going to happen unless they're near-completely limbless and need to kill something with a working circulatory system, though, so it's probably not going to come up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chimp warfare. <i>They literally rip each other apart</i> without weapons. How would Nexus crowds react to seeing competing gangs rip limbs-and-meat off bone from living rivals? No knives needed, just brute-force &quot;arm leaves socket&quot; and &quot;your eye/cheek/nose have been torn off&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Humans in Exalted can actually be incredibly strong (it only takes Strength 3 to lift up a warhorse), so, again, not really seeing much of a difference from typical gladiatorial spectacle. Combatants might not be liquefying their opponents' limbs like Raoh, but Ninja Scroll still had Jubei headbutting someone's skull (mostly the frontal bone) open.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sexually frustrated sea otters sometimes rape baby seals.<br /> <br /> Ducks have been known to <i>crash</i> females out of the air - and still <i>fornicate</i> with the broken-necked corpse. They have penis and vagina <b>specifically</b> evolved because of rape-as-breeding-method. How are duck-men going to behave locally?<br /> <br /> Bowerbird-men might be great artists - or thieves who steal shit to build their nests.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <i>Plus</i> don't forget humans eating <i>bushmeat</i>. If humans have no problem devouring &quot;our cousins&quot; (I saw a video yesterday cooking a fresh-kill with a blow torch, their face and hair and everything still visible as flames singed the corpse)..... why would beastmen take issue devouring us? </div> </div> </div>You've pretty much made a long, pointless list of mostly vertebrates being shitty and capped it off with something that makes it absolutely indistinguishable from human behavior at its worst. As such, I'm going to say that there isn't much influence to be had, especially since there's an entire nation of raitonfolk and snakefolk that manages to get along quite well, and also that the snakewoman merchant sample character in the core is pretty much completely uninfluenced. Given the very human structure of beastfolk, their umwelts (umwelten?) will be overwhelmingly human; the snake lady might be able to smell and taste a whole lot more, but she's ultimately still going to be inviting guests to dinner that's passable in mixed company, because that's what hosting dinner is about when dealing in business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T12:52:08-07:00","id":1226893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226846#post1226846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure didn't take you long to get from there to\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226846#post1226846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talk about a 180\u00b0!</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not mutually exclusive concepts.<br /> <br /> Yes, racists don't need a lot of info to be racist.<br /> <br /> No, racists don't have to be wrong.<br /> <br /> And I quote Celestial Directions - the Wyld:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;<b>Not that the people of Creation\u2019s rim are innocent.</b> Whether human, once-human or part-human,<b> they meet attack with counterattack, slave-raid with slave-raid, hatred with hatred.</b>&quot;</div> <br /> No friendly neighborhood Spiderman. <br /> <br /> More Witcher-style &quot;the racists want to kill the elf - but if you save the elf, the elf then poisons the village - so yeah, both sides are scum to each other and 100% justified in wanting to see the other exterminated&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226846#post1226846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're leaving off a veritable cornucopia of options, from a people living on demesnes that warp their bodies over time, to being the product of sorcery (including being put together by a neomah, <b>which you know is an option</b>), to just being the children of two beastfolk!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point on demenses - but still falls into the territory of &quot;chaos magic that soul-eating faeries like&quot;. Page 148 and 149 of Celestial Directions (Wyld) cover <b>Derangements </b>(so being a squatter in a ruined manse is hardly proof of your civility and rationality).<br /> <br /> Babies made by demons <b>also</b> fall into the &quot;dubious&quot; origin story.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes I know of them</i> - and <i>I'm fond</i> - but just because I like something doesn't mean I'll embrace hypocrisy out of convenience. I play all my <i>horrific little things</i> with 100% acceptance of discrimination if/when such things are discovered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226846#post1226846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to cite that being the case in any of the Exalted books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do I need one? You can literally build any combination of Beastmen - so that includes Wyld-induced plague-carriers and derangement - and canon examples include meat-only sharkmen and blood-only batmen. How are local farmers going to feed humanoids who only consume blood? But more to the point:<br /> <br /> Page 40 of Celestial Directions - Wyld:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Imperial armies <b>generally slaughter any beastmen they capture</b>, because they think beastmen are <b>savage, untamable </b>creatures <b>tainted </b>by the touch of the Anathema. The Immaculate Philosophy clearly states that like any creatures derived from or related to the Anathema, beastmen are <b>soulless monstrosities</b> who deserve <b>slavery or death</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Opinions about beastmen<b> rarely improve</b> in civilized nations that do not follow the Immaculate Philosophy: beastmen are frightening and inhuman, but because they are far less deadly than gods or Exalted, human fears more readily turn to<b> hatred or scorn</b>. Some countries <b>attack beastmen</b> as zealously as the Realm.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Beastmen <b>sometimes gain marginal </b>acceptance in the Threshold\u2019s most open and cosmopolitan cities, such as Nexus and Chiaroscuro, but they <b>still risk enslavemen</b>t. The <b>few </b>free beastmen find employment as gladiators, bodyguards to wealthy eccentrics or in the criminal underworld. They remain <b>second-class citizens</b>, however, if they receive citizenship at all. The law seldom punishes humans who cheat, rob, assault or kill a beastman; people usually smirk and say, \u201c<b>The freak had it coming</b>.\u201d And of course, everyone \u201cknows\u201d that male beastmen lust for human women.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The forest-dwelling folk of the Haltan Republic form the chief <b>exception </b>to this prejudice. Haltan humans, however, feel more friendship for the country\u2019s sentient animals than for the half-human beastmen. Halta treats its beastmen with careful formality, and they do not mingle casually. For instance, if a beastman enters a Haltan tavern, the human patrons immediately leave to give him privacy.&quot;</div> <br /> Page 46 continues:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Remember that most people <i>don\u2019t know</i> the different origins of humanity\u2019s offshoots. For all the average citizen of Whitewall or the Haslanti League knows, a person with wings was transformed by the Wyld as surely as any furred, fanged savage. The average person knows a jumble of stories about Wyld mutation, bestial miscegenation and vile Anathema sorcery. Appearance is no help, either. Some Wyld barbarians look human\u2014or at least as human as any beastman or relic race\u2014but<b> the Wyld has made them monsters on the inside</b>. Maybe the gorgeous woman with the white wings, or the handsome fellow with gills,<b> really does enjoy torturing people to death or feeding on the brains of children</b>. Centuries of <b>propaganda make things worse</b>. The Immaculate Order\u2014arguably the most powerful cultural institution in Creation\u2014says that evil forces taint relic races, beastmen and Wyld mutants alike. The Scarlet Empire, Creation\u2019s greatest military power, backs up that position. Repeat a message long enough and even people who hate you can start believing it.</div> <br /> Notice &quot;<b>really does enjoy torturing people to death&quot; </b>and &quot;<b>makes things <u>worse</u>&quot;</b> (meaning that propaganda <b>isn't</b> the default... beastmen be <i>horrific</i> and propaganda only <i>worsens</i> it). A bat-beastmen might &quot;only prey on bandits&quot; - but propaganda riles up the entire settlement into hunting it down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226846#post1226846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeesh. The game runs with the assumption that cosmetics aside, <i>Beastfolk are human</i>. If the Wings mutation came with the urge to hide your baby in someone else's crib, <i>the books would give that a mention</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And humans are monstrous things, in-game and in-real-life. See above.<br /> <br /> If your village is so pro-tolerance that you'll befriend the shark-toothed, raw-meat-only barbarians from beneath the sea, natural selection will weed out the gullible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226846#post1226846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's great! Monsters <i>are not beastfolk</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Read the Wyld book. Even if not inherently true (by birth), society will treat them as monsters (and thus make them monsters). It's great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226846#post1226846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hypothetical or not, racists are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when they're not.<br /> <br /> I know this is another <b>linguistic</b> problem with English, but you need to differentiate between <b>a bigot</b> and <b>racist.</b><br /> <br /> There are offensive stereotypes that bigots toss around - <b>but there are also true ones</b>.<br /> <br /> If I read statistics about Hispanic &quot;family sizes are larger than Anglo-Americans&quot;, or larger birth rates, or (a bunch of other things).... I generally nod and agree &quot;yup, that's my family and friends&quot;. And if a bigot says &quot;I hate how loud you all are&quot; or (whatever), <i>if its true</i>, I can only shrug and go &quot;well, sucks to be you&quot; (I can't deny that Cuban-Americans &quot;talk loud&quot; (by American standards) just like they &quot;talk too fast&quot; (by Cuban standards).<br /> <br /> If I say &quot;West Africans are predisposed to sickle-cell anemia&quot;, that's inherently <i>racist</i> but <i>not bigoted. </i>In fact, acknowledging a unique local trait is the first step in <i>improving </i>health care for them. The idiot screaming &quot;untrue! equality! we're all 100% the same!&quot; is the guy who is going to get someone killed by failing to acknowledge and respect their unique needs.<br /> <br /> And back to fantasy - a racist who says &quot;this race of batmen drinks blood&quot; <i>is probably right</i>. <hr /><br /> If I offended any beastmen, please feel free to direct them to this thread - I'm sure they'd have more meritorious claims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 06-12-2018, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T13:15:19-07:00","id":1226903,"title":"","content":"Round 2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226849#post1226849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess what, sometimes things in Creation happen without apparent explanation. The pro-mystery angle of EX3 means that there are just some beastfolk who have never not known a time when their people were anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my response to Alucard. But in general (at least in 2E), <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">no one cares about special snowflake origin stories</span></b>. <b>No one knows</b> in 2E either - they <b>still</b> get thrown into &quot;Wyld aberrations&quot; and &quot;freaks&quot; and shunned if you have any sense.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> For some reason, you then felt the need to go example-by-example... <b>why?</b><br /> <br /> You don't need to convince <b>me</b>. I don't care. I promise. I'm not running around stabbing beastmen.<br /> <br /> You need to convince <i>whoever</i> lives around those animals - who then extrapolates those traits to beastmen.<br /> <br /> You need to convince:<ul><li>&quot;Imperial armies&quot; that &quot;generally slaughter any beastmen they capture&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Immaculates&quot; who think &quot;beastmen are soulless monstrosities who deserve slavery or death&quot;</li> <li>Non-Immaculate &quot;civilized nations&quot; who &quot;attack beastmen as zealously as the Realm&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Cosmopolitan cities&quot; where beastmen &quot;still risk enslavement&quot;, are &quot;Second-class citizens&quot; and laws don't punish whoever kills them.</li> </ul>And then convince the Wyld-book itself when it argues &quot;the Wyld has made (some of) them monsters on the inside&quot; who &quot;really (do) enjoy torturing people to death&quot;.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> And when you DO make those arguments, please remember to roll (Attribute)+(Ability) and let us know if you're spending motes on charms. <br /> <br /> There's no need to convince real-life people about make-believe races. <br /> <br /> And if you have a special investment in playing an Anime-style &quot;local catgirl and dogboy save the village&quot; game, <i>I'm not stopping you</i>. I just see Beastmen as more <b>The Island of Dr. Moreau</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T13:17:29-07:00","id":1226904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226893#post1226893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, racists don't have to be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>\u200bdo</i> have to be wrong, because racism has no basis in reality.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I quote...</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the examples from the books that you cite <i>show that the condition of being a beastfolk inherently carries behavioral traits from the animal half</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the Wyld book.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, thanks. I've read it before, and honestly, its relevance here is pretty minimal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is another <b>linguistic</b> problem with English, but you need to differentiate between <b>a bigot</b> and <b>racist.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>do</i> differentiate between the two. A person who believes that a particular race is superior to another is a <b>racist</b>. A person who is intolerant toward those with different opinions is a <b>bigot</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I offended any beastmen, please feel free to direct them to this thread - I'm sure they'd have more meritorious claims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I wouldn't want to direct <i>anyone</i> to this unpleasant discussion, except maybe the mods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T13:36:00-07:00","id":1226909,"title":"","content":"I had a Godblooded character once. Sanyu, 25th child of Peerless Sanzu, God of Perception. Each child of that powerful Attribute Lord was denied a sense, and given another in truly wondrous fashions, so that Peerless Sanzu might experience the world anew and see the labors, or ease, such a transformed sense might have in mortal form. Sanyu, for his part, was born Blind, yet could perceive Essence through his nose and tongue as a snake might. Often did he complain that Braile was not common across Creation, moaned any extended trip across saltwater ('everything tastes like Salt!) yet was a bastion of humor and surprisingly good exorcist, since few malign spirits bothered to hide what they <i>smelled and tasted like</i> when becoming incorporeal. Sanyu worked alongside a 'Breeding 0 DB outcaste'/24 yrear old exiled patrician, and Half-Caste Lunar tiger totem(all played by other players in a sort of 'How far can we go without Exalting?' game).<br /> <br /> The answer?<br /> <i>We blew up Gem trying to stop the slave revolt we accidentally started.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T13:51:42-07:00","id":1226916,"title":"","content":"Jesus I feel sorry for FMA245.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T13:54:06-07:00","id":1226918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226904#post1226904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>\u200bdo</i> have to be wrong, because racism has no basis in reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm baffled. Are you using a different kind of English? A quick glance at a dictionary, and I quote: &quot;the belief that all members of each race possess characteristics or abilities specific to that race, especially so as to distinguish it as inferior or superior to another race or races.&quot;<br /> <br /> Note that the initial segment isn't contingent on the &quot;especially&quot;. You don't need to go into inferior/superior arguments.<br /> <br /> And then there are groups like: <a href=\"http://www.jewishgeneticdiseases.org/jewish-genetic-diseases/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.jewishgeneticdiseases.org...etic-diseases/</a> -- are you saying that a bunch of Jewish doctors trying to cure Jewish diseases.... have no basis in reality? This boggles the mind.<br /> <br /> Or are you saying that &quot;bird men who can fly and have enhanced vision&quot;, &quot;sharkmen who can breath underwater and only eat meat&quot; or &quot;elkmen with awakened essence&quot; <b>are </b>human? If these are not unique &quot;characteristics specific to them&quot;, then why can't I fly, breath underwater and wield magic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226904#post1226904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNone of the examples from the books that you cite <i>show that the condition of being a beastfolk inherently carries behavioral traits from the animal half</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I didn't convey tone in my first post - but why do you continue after I clarified that it's irrelevant? <br /> <br /> The Out-of-Character <i>reality</i> is irrelevant. <br /> <br /> Imperial armies, Immaculates, and even people from &quot;cosmopolitan cities&quot; like Nexus only care about the <b>in-character</b> reality - which is that <i>they look like monsters, we think they're monsters, everyone else &quot;knows&quot; they're monsters, ergo they're monsters</i>. The Haltan Republic is an <b>exception</b> (and even then ostracizes them). Has 3E completely reversed the tone <i>of the entire setting</i>? Or did they just add a few more niche areas where they won't stone beastmen on sight?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226904#post1226904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, thanks. I've read it before, and honestly, its relevance here is pretty minimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is 1E and 2E material irrelevant to a thread named after a 1E/2E term? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I reiterate, some of you guys want to &quot;pick and choose&quot; despite that 90% of the content we have on these abberrations is from previous editions.<br /> <br /> And <b>more importantly</b>, you seem to want to side-step the <b>inherent premise</b> that carries beyond edition. <b>In most fictions</b>, humans aren't super-tolerant around mutants (of any kind, not just Marvel). <br /> <br /> Even in a <b>human-only</b> <b>reality</b>, humans don't get along - and you want us to accept the premise that humanity is <i>more tolerant</i> in a <i>more dangerous</i> world where bandits and barbarians have fangs and claws?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226904#post1226904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>do</i> differentiate between the two. A person who believes that a particular race is superior to another is a <b>racist</b>. A person who is intolerant toward those with different opinions is a <b>bigot</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Honest question: </b>What do you call someone (in English) who acknowledges legitimate racial differences? Because the Dictionary tells me &quot;racist&quot;. <br /> <br /> Admitting that &quot;yes, X population is more likely to have diabetes&quot; or &quot;Y population is more likely to digest milk&quot; or &quot;Z population is more likely to do (whatever)&quot; is inherently <i>racist</i> without being.... what? What's the term? When 23AndMe.com says people from my region &quot;are more likely to like caffeine&quot; or &quot;less likely to be vegetarian&quot;, what do you call it - it's certainly making a <i>racial</i> claim but not a malignant one. <br /> <br /> I double-checked &quot;bigot&quot; and you're right on that one (although Thesaurus had it as a synonym for Racist). So what's the word? Misanthrope doesn't sound right. Zealot I think has religious overtones. What do you call a (generic kind of asshole) when a sexist or racist or (X-ist) argument is legitimate?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226904#post1226904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I wouldn't want to direct <i>anyone</i> to this unpleasant discussion, except maybe the mods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> We're discussing fantasy races who <b>in the books</b> are hated and distrusted. <br /> <br /> And you sound as if I'm defending real-world bigotry (which I don't and haven't). <br /> <br /> Please don't conflate in-game, in-world, in-setting hatred with out-of-game, real-world sentiments. <br /> <br /> <b>Going back to D&amp;D examples</b>, if I play a Half-Orc or Tiefling - and the DM decides the average person will discriminate? IC, my character might hate it - but <b>OOC</b>, <b>I accept it</b>. There is a <b>strong difference</b> between our fictional characters and our real-lives. My embrace of such Half-Orc or Tiefling <i>issues</i> might even be the reason I was <i>motivated</i> to play one in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:06:28-07:00","id":1226925,"title":"","content":"<b>TLDR: Version</b><br /> <br /> Real life analogies, setting material in previous editions, and just about <i>every other fantasy setting</i> has reinforced that humans <b>aren't very kind</b> to one another, let alone to fanged half-beast humanoids. Even the <b>nicest</b> (in 2E) ostracize beastmen, while the <b>cosmopolitan</b> either enslave them or consider them non-citizens it's okay to kill or rob.<br /> <br /> And the books <b>do</b> admit beastmen &amp; Wyld mutants (who are often conflated) sometimes <b>earn</b> that reputation. Demenses aren't &quot;happy cool fairy magic land&quot; - they're <i>chaos magic</i> that <i>makes you inhuman</i> and can <i>give you derangements</i> or turn you into <i>alien monsters</i>. And even without magical derangements, people will generally treat you shitty (which becomes a self-fulfilling prophecy of beastmen retaliating and then humans pointing to say &quot;see? I told you they were savages&quot;.<br /> <br /> Please don't try to paint me as a &quot;racist bigot xenophobe&quot; (whatever the term is) just because I <b>stick with the material</b> and expect most humans to distrust, defame or even attack beastmen. If a newsreporter says &quot;there is war in the Middle East&quot;, you don't blame the newsreporter as &quot;having cause the war!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T15:14:49-07:00","id":1226952,"title":"","content":"I guess baby-eating hamster girl could theoretically be a thing, the world is a big place and the wyld is very weird but... <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I doubt there's a successful subspecies of hamster folk where eating your children due to stress is a common trait because that's a crippling weakness for humans.</li> <li>Joe Mortal doesn't have television or the internet and probably can't read. Unless he breeds hamsters or is friends with someone who does it's unlikely he's aware of this trait to declare &quot;hamster girl eats babies!&quot;</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226904#post1226904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNone of the examples from the books that you cite <i>show that the condition of being a beastfolk inherently carries behavioral traits from the animal half</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> The only place where I remember seeing such a thing was Ma-Ha-Suchi's horde where it should be noted that he's using wyld assimilation to indoctrinate them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T15:30:57-07:00","id":1226958,"title":"","content":"I just think of how Beasttribes are treated in Final Fantasy 14.<br /> <br /> The Evil Empire does all lump them together into one giant pile of dubious 'murder this shit', and even some of the familiar governments treat them like garbage, and people are scared of some of them.<br /> <br /> But these people- who aren't going to be that much more educated then a standard Exalted Peasant-, can recognize different tribal markers from different tribes of beastfolk even when they look otherwise quite similar, and recognize which ones are fine to deal with and which ones you're better off staying away from. Most peasents realize that the ones who are nice are probably suffering just as much under the hands of the other assholes, and working together is mutually beneficial.<br /> <br /> In fact, the statement about 'bandits having fangs and claws' makes me bring it up on the other point; When the Big Bad Fae brings an army to attack your house, or the bandit boss whose been pressuring your family, or the Guild Slavers show up, the big strong Rhino-Guy is gonna be a significant asset in making sure you and your family get away safe, and it's probably in your best interest to at least try to be nice to them.<br /> <br /> There may be some suspiciousness, or distaste, particularly from older people, but as far as I know, most racist behavior isn't learned, it's acquired, and with time spent with individuals like that, children, who then grow up, can learn, or will be, accepting and caring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T15:52:48-07:00","id":1226963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226918#post1226918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then there are groups like: <a href=\"http://www.jewishgeneticdiseases.org/jewish-genetic-diseases/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.jewishgeneticdiseases.org...etic-diseases/</a> -- are you saying that a bunch of Jewish doctors trying to cure Jewish diseases.... have no basis in reality? This boggles the mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat looks to me like an instance in which people researching treatment for genetic conditions that happen to be prevalent in a particular collection of ethnic communities are drawing upon the legacy of their collective cultural identity (which has historically been a very helpful defence mechanism for them when they've been widely persecuted), as a means of drumming up internal financial support.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, one of the diseases that they're looking for treatment for is cystic fibrosis, and there is nothing specifically Jewish about that disease. I know for a fact that it also has an unusually high prevalence in Ireland (one of my genetic engineering lecturers had a particular interest in it). I wouldn't use that as a basis for people from Jewish communities employing this method as a means of creating awareness and acquiring support, but it would be inaccurate for somebody outside to look at the situation and conclude that there is something distinctly Jewish about fibrosis.<br /> <br /> A high incidence is really just a combination of an unfortunate coincidence and marginalization being a historical barrier to getting higher diversity within a genetic lineage.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, a particular case such as this probably doesn't have much relevance to racism as it is actually practiced in places such as the modern United States. The matter of racism being basically irrational... it can come from a few places (making a presumption about people based on their background, seeing cultural traits that are viewed negatively in terms of essential features rather than complicated historical backgrounds, a general attitude of using highly developed terminology as a means of hurting or condescending to people), but it all ultimately boils down to using incidental features, often exaggerated past the point of reality, as a process for attacking a marginalized or oppressed social group.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd that matters to what people mean because how the term &quot;racism&quot; is used in everyday language is not something strictly confined to (or validated by) a dictionary definition.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd it's no good making comments on the distinctions between English language use and whatever other, because... what does it prove? When you say &quot;English puts too much emphasis on what is said&quot;, what do you mean by it? Sure, it's an interesting observation of distinctions between language in neutral terms, but too often you seem to be trying to push a view that the manner in which the English language is used is inferior or wrong.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, I can't speak for anybody else, when I say that I, personally, am willing to give you a bit of leeway in terms of some of the terms that you employ as a result of cultural background and English not being a first language. I think that's fine, even a bit beneficial, as long as it doesn't go too far into casually employing terms that people have told you they find offensive.<br /> <br /> But I take issue with how often you seem to feel a need to employ extremely elaborate arguments that go beyond just providing some cultural background, and into something between a combination of &quot;that background justifies me in saying whatever&quot; and &quot;the way that comes from my background is actually better&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen you are continuously insistent upon it despite people's objections, and make a fight out of it every single time, it's just impolite. Not conductive to a friendly and effective community. And weighs down the discussions that it takes place within.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-12-2018, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T19:52:23-07:00","id":1227020,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>re: Hamster-folk &amp; Joe Mortal</b></span><br /> TBH, I wasn't even imagining a whole breed of them Hamster-folk. My mind's eye had an image from Beauty and the Beast - with a furry Belle as the &quot;single slightly furry female, the darling of the village, who everyone knows and loves&quot;..... and the derangement or behavior doesn't kick in until after some horrific trauma (and then dead kids). A one-shot tragedy, not a race of self-destructive monsters, lol.<br /> <br /> Very good point regarding Joe Mortal, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a>. My attempt with the list was to (ideally) find better-known behaviors that locals might recognize in local threats.<br /> <br /> <b>Ergo</b>, in the Far North, I wouldn't grief Serpent-guys or Riverdragon-gals so much. Ignorant locals might equally think it's some kind of god-blooded with &quot;the blood of the Dragons!&quot; (cue Skyrim music). But in the South or East, negative stereotypes about such reptiles will color perceptions of hybrids.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>re: Behavior Traits</b></span><br /> As aforementioned, the Wyld book outright states:<ul><li><i>You don't need derangements</i> - Creation treats them like such shit, many become that shitty</li> <li><i>....but derangements are a legit possibility</i> - beware the &quot;pretty winged princess&quot; <i>who likes torture</i></li> <li><i>Debilities will warp your thinking</i>. The &quot;Diet: Blood&quot; or &quot;Diet: Raw Meat&quot; are excellent examples. No human lives like that (exclusively). And human-prey runs/swims much slower than deer or fish. A beastmen with qualms against preying on humans will (a) <i>get over it</i> the day some random bigot attacks them (so that's fair game) or (b) <i>starve</i> and then re-evaluate the slow-moving hairless apes in the village. If humans eat apes, why wouldn't an ape-man eat a human?</li> <li><i>Positive mutations will warp your thinking</i>. If I could &quot;breath underwater&quot; - and was a pirate - do you <i>think</i> I'd risk my life in honest combat against a bunch of (probable) bigots who rather skin me? <i>Nope</i>. I'd burn merchant ships and then peacefully scavenge the wreckage when it sinks. That'd be <i>just as bloody</i> as a pirate with a sword - except the locals are <i>more freaked out</i> because they see it as a &quot;monster who likes cooking people alive and eating the drowned&quot;.</li> </ul><b>Ma-Ha-Suchi</b> is a good reference. So is that <b>Monkey-Queen Sorceress-Thing</b> (the one with the banquets full of human corpses). Any Beastman who emulates Lunar heart-consumption and cannibalism is an example (yes, I hate these types; yes, I know OOC it doesn't &quot;work&quot;; but neither OOC realities changes IC behavior). As aforementioned, the <b>Island of Dr. Moreau </b>comes to mind.<br /> <br /> But above all, <i>I never suggested imposing this as a penalty on players</i>. I'm 100% that they're &quot;human&quot; OOC. It's IC where I'd reason &quot;oh yeah, these locals are terrified of your obviously inhuman features&quot; or &quot;those poachers want your tusks&quot; or &quot;the Inexhausitble mutation? after your stunts the last month, the apothecary thinks he can make Exalted-viagra from your skin&quot; (or whatever). Even <i>nice people</i> get accused of being monsters (and expendable).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>re: Rhino Beastmen Heroes vs Fair Folk</b></span><br /> This is a plausible scenario for a happy ending.<br /> <br /> It's <b>also</b> plausible that the locals <b>can't </b>differentiate a beastman from a Wyld mutant (the book explicitly mentions this) and the locals think the Rhino-dude is just a spy or emissary of the Fair Folk, .sent to sabotage or manipulate or feign allegiance. Then killing the Rhinoman (while he's alone) is a smart move (before his Fae allies show up).<br /> <br /> I'm not against happy allegiances. But I <b>never presume them</b>.<br /> <br /> Plus this &quot;expect the worst&quot; scenario leads to more creative roleplay - instead of expecting the locals to be friendly, imagine you try to engineer a conflict to then swoop in and &quot;save the day&quot;. Now your group needs to play (real threat) vs (local paranoia) and manipulate them into trusting you (which is inherently ironic). You might even fake injuries, claim you're a human who was &quot;only recently cursed as a Rhino man&quot; or concoct a rumor about &quot;a local hero who beseeched a Rhino god for a blessing&quot; (and try to spread it so the locals don't freak out when they see you).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">re: Diseases </span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> \u200b&amp; English Vocabulary</span></b><br /> My point is that (a) they identify as &quot;a race&quot; and (b) they consider this distinctly &quot;racial&quot;. They're not trying to cure 1 disease - there's <i>a whole suite of diseases</i> they are uniquely predisposed to (complete with them making each other worse) - due to (like you say) marginalization and lack of genetic diversity. They literally called the website &quot;Jewish Genetic Diseases&quot; <b>because</b> they consider it Jewish. It's no different (again) with West Africans and sickle-cell, or East Asians and alcohol tolerance. Different populations have different needs.<br /> <br /> We can't &quot;believe in diversity&quot; if we don't want to accept that people are diverse.<br /> <br /> I appreciate what you mean about American racism - but <i>dictionaries are how non-Americans learn English</i>. Dictionaries define meaning. Isn't it a little unrealistic for some people to expect <i>the entire world</i> to share their personal grievances? <i>Wouldn't it be more tolerant</i> if we gave each other the benefit-of-a-doubt -- as opposed to these &quot;fans&quot; I've attracted who confuse my <i>acknowledgement</i> of <i>normalized bigotry</i> in a <i>fantasy setting</i> as some kind of endorsement?<br /> <br /> I've even curbed my vocabulary to try playing along - <i>even asking</i> what a suitable replacement word would be - but <b>yes</b>, some people seem more interested in banning/demonizing a word (even when it hampers communication) <i>and then</i> discussions go downhill. There <b>has</b> to be a term for <b>legitimate</b> acknowledgement of 'racial' differences (without implied hatred or loathing) <i>just so English can communicate with the rest of the planet</i>. <b>At the least </b>(if we go into the &quot;social construction of race&quot; tangent), it remains relevant to <i>a fantasy setting</i> in which some populations <i>have wings and claws</i> and no amount of human evolution is going to give hairless apes those traits.<br /> <br /> All in all, I appreciate your post. I've said before, I think I <i>always</i> enjoy your posts.<br /> <br /> But time-and-again, Alucard thinks something I write is mod-worthy.... because? Merely <i>acknowledging</i> that bigotry/racism/xenophobia <b>exists</b> <i>in in the books</i> and is <i>common</i> in a <i>fantasy setting</i> is somehow misinterpreted as an <i>endorsement</i> of it and that's insane.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> And I should also point to his &quot;care to cite the books&quot; quip - but when I <b>did</b>, he shrugs the Wyld-book off as &quot;minimally irrelevant&quot; (despite that it covers beastmen in bulk). <b>Ergo</b>, he doesn't <i>really care</i> about the books - and I can only deduce he just wants to express some odd moral outrage that racism exists in a fantasy world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":".  typos typos syntax typo 06-12-2018, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:24:14-07:00","id":1227027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1226925#post1226925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>TLDR: Version</b><br /> <br /> Real life analogies, setting material in previous editions, and just about <i>every other fantasy setting</i> has reinforced that humans <b>aren't very kind</b> to one another, let alone to fanged half-beast humanoids. Even the <b>nicest</b> (in 2E) ostracize beastmen, while the <b>cosmopolitan</b> either enslave them or consider them non-citizens it's okay to kill or rob.<br /> <br /> And the books <b>do</b> admit beastmen &amp; Wyld mutants (who are often conflated) sometimes <b>earn</b> that reputation. Demenses aren't &quot;happy cool fairy magic land&quot; - they're <i>chaos magic</i> that <i>makes you inhuman</i> and can <i>give you derangements</i> or turn you into <i>alien monsters</i>. And even without magical derangements, people will generally treat you shitty (which becomes a self-fulfilling prophecy of beastmen retaliating and then humans pointing to say &quot;see? I told you they were savages&quot;.<br /> <br /> Please don't try to paint me as a &quot;racist bigot xenophobe&quot; (whatever the term is) just because I <b>stick with the material</b> and expect most humans to distrust, defame or even attack beastmen. If a newsreporter says &quot;there is war in the Middle East&quot;, you don't blame the newsreporter as &quot;having cause the war!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The 2e material. Which we've told you multiple times is not an accurate reflection of Exalted, and tends to just be raw grimdarkness spilled out over so many pages. We know the 2e material; it's been a long time since it was released, it's had a lot of circulation time, but it is, ultimately, not the direction that Exalted is using anymore, and it doesn't really help to keep bringing it up. For reference, What Fire Has Wrought has a parrotfolk monk walking the Blessed Isle with a fellow monk, a mute giant. They're framed in the context of &quot;the odd couple&quot; and seem to be beloved itinerants. People do pretty much seem to know that they're full of shit when they yell out for mob violence against beastfolk, especially if the beastfolk end up preyed upon by the Fair Folk as well, or subject to any of the other multitude of horrors present in Creation. You may have doubts, but adorned with the same iron talismans and standing side by side against actual chaos monsters tends to clear the air very quickly.<br /> <br /> Chaos monsters, mind you, that can also disguise themselves as perfectly normal-looking humans. At the end of the day, racists are broken clocks, and while they might end up pointing out the correct time by accident twice a day, the rest of the day reminds you <i>that they have no fucking clue what they're talking about</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:31:06-07:00","id":1227032,"title":"","content":"I suppose it's fair to say 'I never assume the happy ending' but I think that also means you don't really have right to say everyone else is doing it wrong when they say 'ehh, sometimes good things happen.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T23:50:40-07:00","id":1227062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A beastmen with qualms against preying on humans will (a) <i>get over it</i> the day some random bigot attacks them (so that's fair game) or (b) <i>starve</i> and then re-evaluate the slow-moving hairless apes in the village.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, C, use his superior human intellect and tool use to overcome the inherent limitations of his body without resorting to cannibalism - he may not be as swift as a fish, but he doesn't have to be, to make a net.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But above all, <i>I never suggested imposing this as a penalty on players</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having everyone in town want to run out a character or skin him for his pelt, because his player wanted to play a cute boy with cat ears <i>seems like</i> imposing a penalty on players to me. Sure, once or twice, it might seem fun as an opportunity for drama, but not if it's the default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">even asking what a suitable replacement word would be\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Child of the Mighty. Sun-Born. Moon-Touched. Star-Blessed. Silver-/Golden-/Star-/Shadow-Child. God-Blooded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But time-and-again, Alucard thinks something I write is mod-worthy.... because?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it seldom is in-line with the rules for respecting the conversation, other people, the mods, et cetera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I should also point to his &quot;care to cite the books&quot; quip - but when I <b>did</b>\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>When I asked for you to cite your &quot;mutations are behavioral, sometimes racists are right&quot; bit, you mean. You know, where catgirls and cuckoo-folk will just up and torture animals and abduct babies.<br /> <br /> And your cite of the book does not convince me that this is the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">he shrugs the Wyld-book off as &quot;minimally irrelevant&quot; (despite that it covers beastmen in bulk).</div> </div> </div> </div>I said its relevance is minimal, not because it's 2e, but because it doesn't once establish that beastfolk are in any way prone to the animal behavior you attributed to them. Even when derangements <i>are</i> conveyed by the Wyld, it's not contingent on any animal features you might have been given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ergo</b>, he doesn't <i>really care</i> about the books\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly probably care about the books more than I should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can only deduce he just wants to express some odd moral outrage that racism exists in a fantasy world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the least bit outraged, though I <i>am</i> rather weary of you constantly bringing it to this racial place when there's a rich tapestry of subjects in this pulp revival fantasy game that <i>doesn't</i> make millions of real-world people miserable on a daily basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-13-2018, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T00:01:51-07:00","id":1227063,"title":"","content":"Now, for something approaching on-topic, my seafaring game also made use of a group of sorcerers detailed in 2e, the Children of the Storm. They were living on a trio of islands in Okeanos called the Keys of Matscha, and believed that having divine blood in your veins was an avenue to sorcery.<br /> <br /> This proved troublesome for them when only scant handfuls of their God-Blooded prot\u00e9g\u00e9s would awaken into the Children's occult mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-13-2018, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T01:53:35-07:00","id":1227086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which we've told you multiple times is not an accurate reflection of Exalted, and tends to just be raw grimdarkness spilled out over so many pages. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but... <b>what </b>is the accurate reflection of Exalted? The world ruled by people whose souls are warped with Great Curse... the world full of monsters trying to kill you or eat your soul... The world, the greatest heroes of which, are feared and despised as A-letter-word. (very offensive for every orthodoxal Christian, so should be banned from all the books [just kidding]). The world with the whole enslaved race of Djala! All of this were canon since 1est Ed!<br /> <br /> The main reason for the setting to be like that (sick, half-ruined and distorted) is to make challenge for Larger-Then-Life Heroes! If the Creation would be rainbow-pony-universe, would the Solars have then any reason to use their powers at all?<br /> <br /> Don't you like the attitude of uneducated peasants towards beastmen? Change it IC! Use <i>Taboo Inflicting Diatribe</i>, gain power and authority, deal with consequences!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-13-2018, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T02:19:13-07:00","id":1227092,"title":"","content":"As for the theme.<br /> In my game there was a teenaged faeblooded man of Earth. He lived in a small settlement near Mountain Folk City, and once found Royal Warstrider with female AI that was in love with warstrider previous owner. When the behemoth attacked the settlement, the faeblooded attuned to the Warstrider, and AI recognizes her beloved in him. The idea was, that once he would prove to be the same soul, that antient Eclipse Solar once was (the owner of the warstrider), and sooner or later he would Exalt with the same Exaltation and remember his past life. Alas, the player couldn't participate anymore and the game ended too early (too sad; his stunts were definitely the best I've seen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-13-2018, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T06:16:03-07:00","id":1227124,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6186\" data-vbnamecard=\"6186\">Aleksay</a> it is not considered an accurate reflection of Exalted because the dev team has stated it is not. The current game line is in the process of rolling back/refuting large swaths if it\u2019s lore. Now, this may rankle for some, especially if it\u2019s the only canon people really knew. Yet the discussion becomes counter-productive when discussing the setting because the current edition is repudiating it. Yes this forum is for all editions, but unless specificied, the discussion centers on 3e, and most of the regulars will give it or first edition (provided it doesn\u2019t conflict with something established in third) primacynover any piece of 2e lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T06:18:59-07:00","id":1227126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227032#post1227032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's fair to say 'I never assume the happy ending' but I think that also means you don't really have right to say everyone else is doing it wrong when they say 'ehh, sometimes good things happen.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you 10/10. I'd never say &quot;nope, that's impossible&quot;. <br /> <br /> My intention was more along the lines of &quot;I could see it not going smoothly - but I'd be totally down if players had some clever scheme to win over the locals&quot;. Note my response included trying to imagine ways the Rhinoman would sort of &quot;sell himself&quot; to the locals - not just &quot;eh, they hate you, die&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227062#post1227062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, C, use his superior human intellect and tool use to overcome the inherent limitations of his body without resorting to cannibalism - he may not be as swift as a fish, but he doesn't have to be, to make a net.</div> </div> </div> </div>Superiorintellect? There are <b>normal humans</b> today who resort to robbery and murder, despite an entire education system in place to give them the option to do <i>literally anything else</i>. It's a hell of a leap to - in one generation - go from &quot;half-animal barbarian born in the jungles/oceans where everything wants to eat each other&quot; to &quot;this week, tools!&quot;. <br /> <br /> And I still disagree with &quot;cannibalism&quot;, because not only are <b>real life humans</b> capable of it (and it's been practiced in different cultures/contexts without the modern taboo), but we have even <b>less qualms</b> about eating humanoid-looking animals. If humans <i>in real life</i> treat each other like <i>animals</i> for merely having the wrong skin-color - I can't see where a half-bat or half-shark <i>anything</i> would automatically have some deep empathy and love for us hairless apes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227062#post1227062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having everyone in town want to run out a character or skin him for his pelt, because his player wanted to play a cute boy with cat ears <i>seems like</i> imposing a penalty on players to me. Sure, once or twice, it might seem fun as an opportunity for drama, but not if it's the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out-of-character and in-character are two different beasts.<br /> <br /> IC, I expect the world to operate in a consistent way for everyone (regardless of whether-or-not one player wants to be a Foxkin or Bearboy).<br /> <br /> OOC, I'm 100% with letting players play whatever they want. And if they're looking for anime-style &quot;cute boy with car ears in a nice world&quot;, then I clearly wouldn't waste <i>either</i> of our time in such a game. They can do their thing, I do mine. But I don't go into Exalted <i>presuming</i> that cutesy anime is the default. This is a game with Conans, Cthulhu and epic Gods - not a harem anime at the Heptagram ft. totally kawaii ice-girls, cat-boys and the protagonist with the rainbow hair color.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227062#post1227062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Child of the Mighty. Sun-Born. Moon-Touched. Star-Blessed. Silver-/Golden-/Star-/Shadow-Child. God-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? I've been using those terms. <i>Children of Exalts</i> to be precise (and broad).<br /> <br /> I meant your quibble with the definition of racism vs bigotry, since it feels like you're conflating (any acknowledgement of differences) with (hatred of differences). People can discuss (differences in gender) without being misogynist or misandryst. People can discuss (differences in religion) without being a hateful zealot. I'm asking what your English word is for those subjects (without the implied hate).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227062#post1227062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it seldom is in-line with the rules for respecting the conversation, other people, the mods, et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagreeing with you isn't the same as disrespecting you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227062#post1227062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I asked for you to cite your &quot;mutations are behavioral, sometimes racists are right&quot; bit, you mean. You know, where catgirls and cuckoo-folk will just up and torture animals and abduct babies.<br /> <br /> And your cite of the book does not convince me that this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>And.... that's not my problem? How am I at fault because you don't agree with written material? The books are the only thing that unite everyone on the forums (regardless of where we live, culture, clicques, customs, genre preferences, etc).<br /> <br /> And yeah - Beastmen are 100% capable of being monstrous assholes. If Wyld derangements don't do it, if niche Debilities don't do it, then Creation treating you as an animal will suffice. The idea that they <i>don't exist</i> is just silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227062#post1227062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not the least bit outraged, though I <i>am</i> rather weary of you constantly bringing it to this racial place when there's a rich tapestry of subjects in this pulp revival fantasy game that <i>doesn't</i> make millions of real-world people miserable on a daily basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a rich fantasy game with necromancy, genocide, beastiality (I am forever dubious at why English spells it &quot;<b>best</b>iality&quot;), eugenics, war, oppression, empires and even creepy magical mind-control seduction on par with the Purple Man from Jessica Jones or the Shadow King in LEGION (the whole &quot;I will <i>seduce</i> you.... by magical power&quot;).<br /> <br /> <b>The Age of Sorrows</b> is not a happy place. <i>That's why it needs heroes</i>. <br /> <br /> But again, if you prefer light-hearted fare/fair, enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T06:28:49-07:00","id":1227129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227020#post1227020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that (a) they identify as &quot;a race&quot; and (b) they consider this distinctly &quot;racial&quot;. They're not trying to cure 1 disease - there's <i>a whole suite of diseases</i> they are uniquely predisposed to (complete with them making each other worse) - due to (like you say) marginalization and lack of genetic diversity. They literally called the website &quot;Jewish Genetic Diseases&quot; <b>because</b> they consider it Jewish. It's no different (again) with West Africans and sickle-cell, or East Asians and alcohol tolerance. Different populations have different needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHow do I put this...<br /> <br /> \u200bI feel as though, when you talk about this kind of thing in response to discussions concerning racism, it's crossing the idea of genetic variations between populations over with the manner in which racists categorize people, without regard to the motivations and implications of racist categories. Responding to discussion of racism by saying that races actually exist because of things like this is missing some of the point, because racists aren't categorizing and oppressing Jewish people on the basis of what kinds of genetic diseases are prevalent within their subgroups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate what you mean about American racism - but <i>dictionaries are how non-Americans learn English</i>. Dictionaries define meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, but I think there's a point at which some cues also need to be taken from communication with native English speakers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a little unrealistic for some people to expect <i>the entire world</i> to share their personal grievances?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about sharing them, but at least a bit of empathy for where people are coming from when they explain things that are hurtful to them wouldn't go amiss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">who confuse my <i>acknowledgement</i> of <i>normalized bigotry</i> in a <i>fantasy setting</i> as some kind of endorsement?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA lot of your posts are still honestly confusing; it can still be hard for me to tell what you're saying because of how dense they are, and the manner in which you divide them into numerous sub-categories.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, when I saw this thread first come up, I knew that one of the first responses would be somebody explaining why the term &quot;Half-Caste&quot; is one that they want to stop employing, and I <i>knew</i> that when you saw that, you would respond with lengthy posts defending and justifying the use of the term. That's what I mean when I say that you keep choosing to make a fight out of these things.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis started from <b>you</b> responding to how <b>somebody else</b> was employing language.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the term itself, whether or not it's a slur that characters inside the setting would employ to describe one another has no bearing on whether it should be the term used in the basic text. The text is not written in the voice of the characters, and the text is both how it conveys the information to the reader, and provides the readers with terminology to use between one another.<br /> <br /> Biases that might exist in the setting are not an excuse for the books or the community to casually employ terms that have a legacy of being used to attack or discriminate against people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T06:58:55-07:00","id":1227133,"title":"","content":"Haven't read the whole thread yet, just want to state my opinion that I fully approve of the term 'X-blooded' due to both the X-men shade of meaning (one cool thing gained from genetics) and the lack of confusion from the narrower actually-from-gods descendants getting mixed in with demon/fae/ghosts/Exalts. I will use this fanon term in my future posts on the topic!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T08:53:05-07:00","id":1227151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227124#post1227124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6186\" data-vbnamecard=\"6186\">Aleksay</a> <b>unless specificied</b>, the discussion centers on 3e</div> </div> </div> </div>How about the thread using a <b>non-3E</b>, explicitly 1E/2E term? Was that not a sufficient contextual clue?<br /> <br /> Does this mean the 3E-only crowd will politely excuse themselves? <b>Or at the least</b> quit pretending that the rest of us don't belong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227129#post1227129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis started from <b>you</b> responding to how <b>somebody else</b> was employing language.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1223781#post1223781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, the word &quot;Half-Caste&quot; is not being used further in the gameline for a number of understandable reasons (including but not limited to not all Exalt types having castes, the new edition not being as interested in shoving things into neat categorical boxes, and the negative associations attached to the word's history in real life).</div> </div> </div> </div>OP called the thread <i>what it is named</i>.<br /> <br /> Alucard was the <b>first</b> reply - and <b>began</b> with his <i>faithful</i> response to how OP employed language, making reference to the &quot;negative associations&quot;. His &quot;for the record&quot; was the first tangent.<br /> <br /> My initial post <b>stuck to the topic first</b> - and only in a <i>spoiler</i> (because I felt it was a tangent) did I interject to point out that Alucard's note <i>isn't universal</i>. If he gets to say &quot;some of us are offended&quot;, I don't see why others can't say &quot;but not all of us - some of us actually use these words in context&quot;.<br /> <br /> This <b>isn't</b> saying &quot;other people can't be offended&quot;.<br /> <br /> This <b>is</b> saying &quot;non-offended interpretations also exist&quot;.<br /> <br /> From there, I went into my historical/political tangent - because the 1E and 2E term set in the Age of Sorrows evoked for me a &quot;clash of civilizations&quot; with <i>the Children of Exalts</i> inhabiting an unhappy inbetween stuck with un-asked-for privilege (magic powers and parents who likely rewrite the landscape) and un-earned-disdain (mortals who resent or envy them - and rival empires who see <i>the Children</i> as extensions of their parents).<br /> <br /> It's a politically and historically loaded term.... <i>which does a great job</i> of succinctly evoking (for me at least) an angle for their themes and story (as opposed to &quot;generic magical wunderkids&quot; in some anime-inspired bildungsroman). I would hate the chorus of &quot;it's offensive&quot; to drown out the <i>rich narrative source-material</i> tied to the term. Let's not throw the baby out with the bathwater.<br /> <br /> And this <b>isn't a criticism</b> of United States historical knowledge.... this is &quot;hey guys, not <i>every</i> mixed-heritage individual is grouped with the 'oppressed' like in the US.... if you glance at other countries, the half-and-half types actually have a bunch of different experiences that could be <i>awesome</i> inspiration&quot;.<br /> <br /> I <i>understand</i> the US narrative in which half-and-half kids were grouped with the <i>oppressed class</i>.<br /> <br /> But it's <i>not universal</i>. I think there's a lot more diversity and awesomeness when we include other countries/cultures/histories in which sometimes they were <i>revolutionaries</i> and sometimes <i>tyrants</i> and sometimes <i>heroes. </i><b>Limiting</b> them to &quot;just victims&quot; (because &quot;the US&quot;) gets old.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227063#post1227063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, for something approaching on-topic</div> </div> </div> </div>Now we find common ground! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If the subject is (concrete X-Blooded examples) over (abstractions of X-Blooded as a group)....<br /> <br /> I played two Demon-Blooded I particularly enjoyed (the later of which we tweaked the house-rule somewhat).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Shoba Mirza</b></span> was unaware of her ancestry until the caravan she was accompanying stopped by a settlement on the outskirts of the Varang City-States. The caravan had been harassed by ape-beastmen scouts and hoped the settlement walls were secure enough to rest a few nights. Instead, a throng of ape-beastmen, a handful of Blood Apes, and their hybrid progeny swarmed the location, with ample casualties on both sides. (TLDR: Lots of fighting &amp; repositioning later, she ends up in a cellar - the structure above <i>collapses</i> - and she spends days trapped, her only food/drink being the meat and flesh of one of the blood apes.)<br /> <br /> She learned/acquired/developed her first charm then - but was <i>convinced</i> the power was a quirk from subsisting off a demon. She became a demon-hunter thereafter (with the quirk of doing <i>everything possible</i> to eat from them to get stronger). It became a fun power-motivator / power-limiter playing a demon-hunter who <b>only</b> purchased powers after stalking, spying and killing a demon. <b>Plus</b> it was a &quot;dirty secret&quot; that &quot;one of the heroes&quot; was potentially viler than her prey.<br /> <br /> I never got my name sake's <a href=\"https://news.marvel.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2016/09/555f45110133f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">flaming-hell-elephant</a> mount tho. ;_;<br /> <br /> I took that idea later (for another game) and we worked some homebrew to make it a &quot;thing&quot; of its own (as opposed to just a kooky misconception one character had). <i>Shades of Lunars hunting prey</i> but much more lower-power in scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":".  typos syntax typos bathwater 06-13-2018, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T09:18:12-07:00","id":1227158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227086#post1227086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, but... <b>what </b>is the accurate reflection of Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's been published thus far in third edition, and some first edition sources noted by the present developers. Beastfolk got a big change in that they're no longer strongly associated with Lunars, even though Lunars can turn people into them, so you can't take what 2e says about them as a reliable source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The world ruled by people whose souls are warped with Great Curse... the world full of monsters trying to kill you or eat your soul... The world, the greatest heroes of which, are feared and despised as A-letter-word. (very offensive for every orthodoxal Christian, so should be banned from all the books [just kidding]). The world with the whole enslaved race of Djala! All of this were canon since 1est Ed! </div> </div> </div>And Lunars used to wipe with pinecones and differentiate themselves with non-magical equipment use. That idea sucked, so the game's architects got rid of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main reason for the setting to be like that (sick, half-ruined and distorted) is to make challenge for Larger-Then-Life Heroes! If the Creation would be rainbow-pony-universe, would the Solars have then any reason to use their powers at all? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the way things were worded, the Imperium of Man from 40K looked more tolerant. If you go into the grimdark layer with Exalted, you're going in the wrong direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't you like the attitude of uneducated peasants towards beastmen? Change it IC! Use <i>Taboo Inflicting Diatribe</i>, gain power and authority, deal with consequences! </div> </div> </div>Given that beastfolk have likely been rubbing shoulders with humans for far, far longer than Solars have been around, that's really only going to be necessary in extreme circumstances. Also, it's possible to mend fences by just passing through - Demetheus does it all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T09:24:26-07:00","id":1227161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227151#post1227151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the thread using a <b>non-3E</b>, explicitly 1E/2E term? Was that not a sufficient contextual clue?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the OP was talking about God-Blooded in general. The use of the term seems more like a mistake or typo in this context. Also, the old term is a real-world slur (don't try to bring up the in-game use, it doesn't matter), so nothing excuses its use to mark a thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does this mean the 3E-only crowd will politely excuse themselves? <b>Or at the least</b> quit pretending that the rest of us don't belong?<br /> </div> </div> </div>Label the thread with a [1E/2E] in brackets or something of that like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T09:56:25-07:00","id":1227166,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a>, the 2E connotations of the term differe vastly from the 1E connotations, hence why I keep trying to push for the discussion to center on 1E if discussing something that 3E hasn\u2019t touched on yet. The problem seems to be that you approach 2E as the only canon in the setting, without noting where/ how it broke with framings before in 1E and where 3E uses 1E as it\u2019s foundation. Terms are used in all three editions, but the connotations, that is what those terms are associated with, has changed significantly edition to edition. This is not to say that 2E discussions can not occur, but rather that in terms of general setting, they have less weight when discussing the setting. Now you can always disregard other setting framings from both 1E/3E, but you might want to preface that you are interested purely at exploring 2E\u2019s reference points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T11:40:01-07:00","id":1227183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227158#post1227158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that beastfolk have likely been rubbing shoulders with humans for far, far longer than Solars have been around, that's really only going to be necessary in extreme circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have they addressed then &quot;why play human&quot; and &quot;why don't they outnumber us&quot;?<ul><li>Why ever play a human on a pirate-ship when a pair of gills would make me 10x better at piracy?</li> <li>Why ever play a human-turned-Exalt when I could go &quot;People of the Air&quot; and get free wings as a bonus?</li> <li>Why doesn't (Warlord X) create entire harems of war-prisoners as breeding-pens for his beastman super-soldiers? Pangolin-men with natural body armor, sharkmen who burn ships &amp; drown their foes, batmen who drop incendiaries over settlements at night.</li> </ul>I'm not even &quot;poo pooing&quot; the idea - I'm legitimately curious as to what curbs beastmen as (a) &quot;simply better than humans&quot; and (b) tactically superior troops. Entire kingdoms full of nothing but furry-folk.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like arguing &quot;we should have firearms in the setting because it's kewl&quot; without explaining how (a) it's limited in scale <b>or</b> (b) if not limited, how firearms rapidly changes warfare. Ripple effects are kind of important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227161#post1227161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The use of the term seems more like a mistake or typo in this context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're a telepath who can tell when other people make mistakes? A 10-letter phrase is a hell of a typo.<br /> <br /> There are mental gymnastics taking place that I just have no interest in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227161#post1227161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so nothing excuses its use to mark a thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't excuse it <b>for you</b>. (polite reminder)<br /> <br /> I can read the phrase without thinking OP (or the Exalted authors who used it in the first place) are bigots or clumsy typists. They used the phrase in non-offensive ways and I will only interpret it in a non-offensive way, because absolutely nothing in OP's post dehumanized or attacked anyone (on this thread, forum, game or planet).<br /> <br /> Thinking the best of people is a <b>nice</b> thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227166#post1227166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a>, the 2E connotations of the term differe vastly from the 1E connotations, hence why I keep trying to push for the discussion to center on 1E if discussing something that 3E hasn\u2019t touched on yet</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the differences you see? I'm <b>legitimately </b>curious, as I haven't glanced at the Player's Guide in ages.<br /> <br /> I don't have a preference of 2E over 1E - it was simply more readily available. If you see a difference in 1E, I'm all ears! <br /> <br /> Maybe I overlooked something in 1E, but my gameplay experience (with a mutation-laden human) was still very much &quot;local villagers freak out&quot; &gt; &quot;I get accused of being some Wyld-spawned fae-horror or beastman&quot; &gt; &quot;run for my liiiiiifffeeeee&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T13:53:16-07:00","id":1227219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227126#post1227126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with you 10/10. I'd never say &quot;nope, that's impossible&quot;.<br /> <br /> My intention was more along the lines of &quot;I could see it not going smoothly - but I'd be totally down if players had some clever scheme to win over the locals&quot;. Note my response included trying to imagine ways the Rhinoman would sort of &quot;sell himself&quot; to the locals - not just &quot;eh, they hate you, die&quot;.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is true, then English being your secondary language is obfuscating this. You act very declaratively when you talk, essentially talking down to other opinions; when you talk about the Rhino idea, you devote a lot of words to how such a thing could go wrong, and about how you'd imagine having to trick the people into accepting Rhinoman. I'm not really super invested in Rhinoman over anything else, it was just a random idea based on a questline in FF14, where a group of mortals, oppressed by a conquering Roman Empire, take in an orphan wolf-man and help him find a place in the world, not even through combat against invaders, but because he can smell out sick and injured crops before they can, thus perserving more of the harvest. When you post, your implied statements, if not your active ones, are somewhat 'yeah, that would be nice, but it's actually better and more correct to do it this way'. This is why these long discussions happen, because, presumably, your lack of ability to communicate in english results in your word choice being ever so slightly incorrect to make it seem like you're telling everyone off.<br /> <br /> In addition, when you respond to certain things, particularly word choice is a big one here, there is a definite feeling of an undercurrent of 'my observation of the word is better, and yours is worse, so use mine'. This is dismissive of other's opinions, and if you truly mean nothing by it, it's difficult to perceive that when you tell other mixed-race people your opinion and ignore if it's offensive to them. In a little personal anectdote of my own, one of my professors in college spoke at length about when he went down to Central America, in a particular little town, where almost everyone was mixed race, these racial markers were still used. The town bum and drunk was never called a 'White' Man, even though he was the whitest man in the town, while the Town's Mayor was a mixed race woman who was called 'The White Woman'. Even when the physical aspect isn't even there, these biases of racial distinction remain, even when they lack basis in reality; not just racism as a whole, but even in the idea of a person's skin tone not being what people acknowledge them as.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T14:20:24-07:00","id":1227232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1227183#post1227183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have they addressed then &quot;why play human&quot; and &quot;why don't they outnumber us&quot;?[*]Why ever play a human on a pirate-ship when a pair of gills would make me 10x better at piracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are probably pirates that do that, since Lintha don't have a corner on them, but by and large, such folk are better at picking up wrecks than in causing them, and the West is very low in population because it's generally limited to space around islands. Most people who take up seafaring can't swim, and anyone who's lost at sea is considered dead when they get tossed off the boat, because there isn't really a good way of surviving and retrieval in the open ocean. Generally, anyone who has marine animal features out in the west is probably going to be living like how the Pelagothropes do because of it, and they might have a better deal living with them than on the surface.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Why ever play a human-turned-Exalt when I could go &quot;People of the Air&quot; and get free wings as a bonus? </div> </div> </div>People of Air aren't beastfolk or even God-Blooded of any kind. In 1e, they were also very, very dead by the Second Age, because their continued existence was dependent on rare reagents when they were originally introduced. Even in 2e, they were part of a low-population insular enclave that shunned the outside world and dropped outsiders from the sky to conceal their home, so it'd be out of place to have many of them end up venturing outside and taking the Second Breath. In this present edition, if it leans closer to 1e, there literally aren't any other than possibly some lone survivors in numbers as low as ancient Dragon Kings in stasis, or more likely, lower, and they might not be able to survive if removed from stasis because of the strict dietary compound requirements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Why doesn't (Warlord X) create entire harems of war-prisoners as breeding-pens for his beastman super-soldiers? Pangolin-men with natural body armor, sharkmen who burn ships &amp; drown their foes, batmen who drop incendiaries over settlements at night.<br /> I'm not even &quot;poo pooing&quot; the idea - I'm legitimately curious as to what curbs beastmen as (a) &quot;simply better than humans&quot; and (b) tactically superior troops. Entire kingdoms full of nothing but furry-folk. </div> </div> </div>Because they don't have the resource base of the Solar Deliberative or Scarlet Dynasty to do whatever they want (elite soldiers with good gear are expensive, even if they grow some of the gear), and steel still tends to be stronger than the hides of beastfolk, so you'll be suffering greater losses than gains. Also, the people that you're putting into camps are going to get pissed off, revolt, and either die or have your head on a pike. tl;dr pick any reason that a &quot;super soldier&quot; program in fiction has failed, it applies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's kind of like arguing &quot;we should have firearms in the setting because it's kewl&quot; without explaining how (a) it's limited in scale <b>or</b> (b) if not limited, how firearms rapidly changes warfare. Ripple effects are kind of important. </div> </div> </div>No, it's nothing like that, because beastfolk have stronger limitations. Mechanically, they are humans with some extra marginal soak here or there, or the capacity to survive more easily in extreme environments. So for the former, they're going to need to still wear armor (which, given the odd shape, will be made at great cost), and the latter only have an advantage in extreme environments. Claws and teeth aren't much of an advantage in open-field battles, either, because the other side will be using spears and slings, which are cheaper, can be passed around, and tend to outrange claws and teeth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now you're a telepath who can tell when other people make mistakes? A 10-letter phrase is a hell of a typo.<br /> <br /> There are mental gymnastics taking place that I just have no interest in. </div> </div> </div>No, because in the OP, it was used as a general term for God-Blooded. Not everyone is so obsessed with the game as you or I to always recall every term; even writers have had off days, which is why Scroll of Heroes refers to a Lunar Charm from 1e that doesn't exist in 2e. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doesn't excuse it <b>for you</b>. (polite reminder) </div> </div> </div>Or most of the forum, it would seem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe I overlooked something in 1E, but my gameplay experience (with a mutation-laden human) was still very much &quot;local villagers freak out&quot; &gt; &quot;I get accused of being some Wyld-spawned fae-horror or beastman&quot; &gt; &quot;run for my liiiiiifffeeeee&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Except that the typical response of anyone is &quot;go get the local priest&quot;, not exactly running for your life. If you're not part of an invading war band, you can be mistaken for a god, which can have good and bad points, because if you go too far with your fraud, heaven will send someone to clean up. You can also banish the notion that you are fae by carrying around iron talismans like everyone else does, possibly by purchasing them from a trusted source in the town and putting them on immediately. If you don't burn on contact, that's one matter out of the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T16:33:53-07:00","id":1227267,"title":"","content":"Also, as far as &quot;why isn't everyone a beastperson&quot;,<br /> 1) The mutations don't always breed true, and Leafy McLeafface in the east intermarrying with orthodox humans may breed his mutations out and be left with children who just have a weird hair color.<br /> 2) There are in general far more orthodox humans than mutants, leading to point 1, except in small groups that happen to have similar mutations and potentially breed true, or are exposed to the same sort of transmutative effect (living in a particular demesne, consuming a certain magical fruit, etc).<br /> 3) It's not free because you pay for what you get. You want the agile wings and keen eyes of a person of the air or a birdperson? You don't get Wings [5] and Enhanced Sense: Sight [3] *on top* of your 7 [mortal], 10 [Solar], 3 [DB], etc, merit points. You pay the 8 points, and then you have 0 [1bp spent], 2, or 5 merit points left to spend.<br /> <br /> And while this may seem silly coming from me, your gameplay experience of &quot;the GM will actively disrupt his own story to fuck me over for being a mutant&quot; sounds like the aberrant example, and like you had a GM who just didn't want you to play a mutant at all but didn't want to say NO. There can be a gradient between &quot;the story will constantly fuck you over&quot; and &quot;nothing happens&quot;, and having occasional complications when your mutations are found out but not being utterly incapable of interacting with the plot is somewhere between these two extremes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 06-15-2018, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T20:21:49-07:00","id":1236276,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading the thread,<br /> As someone new to the forum, this thread brought into specific relief something that's been bugging me as I perused other threads, but hadn't really quantified until now. People are genuinely dismissive of 2E. I get that the mechanics are detested, and in several cases poorly-contrived tire fires of noodles-thrown-at-wall style concepts. I get that some or even most of the canon/fluff seems to be thought of in much the same way by many....Yet, I find it maddening that *some* people seem in such a rush for 3E that the 2E canon elements of things that either a) Don't seem to have been covered in any great detail by 3E as yet, or b) Haven't been covered at all, and may not be covered in any detail within 3E for perhaps years to come are disregarded as meaningless. I find that, puzzling.<br /> <br /> Now, &quot;core&quot; concepts that are obvious even from superficial treatment in an already-existing 3E source are one thing. If X detail concerning say, Lunars or Sidereals got mentioned in 3E Core or WFHW, for example, wonderful. 3E's caught up with that concept, and supplanted 1E/2E in that regard. At that point, people have the choice of adopting what is now canon, or romping off into house-ruling territory for their own activities, as always.<br /> <br /> I don't, OTOH, consider it unreasonable to continue clinging to 1E/2E canon-elements in the absence of 3E treatments of a subject. The CoCDs are some of my favorite books of all time. To me, they are the bread which surrounds the meat of the Splat-books. They give a great deal of context to many things that, at best, get a paragraph somewhere else, and then generally only as a gray Storyteller-sidebar style thing that relates to a broader element under discussion.<br /> <br /> More than that, 1E/2E are Exalted's past. They had to have done something right, else we all wouldn't be waiting on 3E. Hate on something that maddens you all you like, IMHO, but please don't rule out the notion others might find worth in that which you hate.<br /> <br /> Like many here, much of the Silver Pact as it relates to assimilation of young Lunars makes me want to throw my MoEP: Lunars at a wall. Yet, I adore the breakdown on Thousand Streams social engineering tactics. Lunar Charm Trees...I can howl about how taken out to the woodshed, beaten, and perversely abused Lunars were getting much of the Charm-set they did...but I know there are people who adore the whole &quot;Lunars as weakest of the Celestial Exalts&quot; model, and wouldn't ever want it any other way.<br /> <br /> Sorry, just felt like raising something I felt as an issue that this thread seemed to embody. Count up all the times someone said &quot;but that's 2E, it doesn't count&quot; or some variant thereof. Seriously? We don't even have L:FatG yet. Let alone anything but some developer &quot;this in, that out&quot; type statements for the entire concept of Exalt-Children. Certainly nothing resembling a treatment of them. For the record, I do seem to differ from the majority, in that I absolutely loved Lords/Lands of Creation. The context on the First Age informs my stories and the few games I've run in the 2nd Age like few other things. With all the Splats to cover, and all of the more high-priority supplemental stuff...I wouldn't be surprised if its ages before we saw something like Lords/Lands of Creation for 3E. That's not a bad thing, IMHO. So many Exalt-books, CoCD-type books, etc etc, only so many months of development in a year.<br /> <br /> Until those things get written though, 1E/2E is what we have in many areas. There are essays, dev-interviews, and podcasts about new stuff, and that's wonderful...but it doesn't really provide the same contextual narrative for discussion, because those sources are nowhere near as universally absorbed by the body of readers here as books everyone has had for years and years.<br /> <br /> Also for the record: Golden Children and Moon-Touched, of COURSE it's a racial issue. It's ALSO a &quot;child of Exalt-X, and subject to that individual Exalt-parent's legacy issue&quot;...but for the Golden Children/Moon Touched, THEY are a &quot;race&quot; in a way their parents are not. They're people whose performances in the fields of human endeavor are all affected in the same way, for the same reason, descent. I don't agree that many people are going to instantly pick them out for what they are, but on the occasion they are detected for what they are, I would expect them to suffer (or benefit) from the exact same social influences that affect how their parents are viewed. If anything, I would expect mortal reaction to Exalt-children to be MORE homogenous than the mortals' reaction to their parents..whose great deeds, for good or ill, will at least single the Exalt in question out for specific remembrance. Whereas the children of a Solar God-King-Warlord of a Hundred Kingdoms Duchy, begotten by the score on his two hundred concubines, are simply &quot;children of the God-King.&quot; Emphasis on their parent-tie first, but profound emphasis also on the &quot;children OF&quot; as a critical feature of their social identity.<br /> <br /> As for why Beastfolk have not supplanted regular mortals in Creation: I can't think of a very good reason why they haven't, beyond Developer Fiat. While mutations like fangs and claws are basically irrelevant if the beastfolk are in conflict with mortals armed with effective metal weaponry/armor, something like Elemental Adaptation means the Beastfolk who have it can exist in both the portion of the North (for example) warm enough for mortals to live in, AND the portion where it gets cold enough to frostbite a human's fingers and toes into gangrene-territory in seconds if those digits are left exposed. That kind of benefit is enormous, and it'd make a huge, HUGE difference demographically-speaking IMHO. Besides that, Lunar progenitors possess Charms that can preset the Attributes of Beastfolk-to-be, and logic says the Lunar progenitor would set those (physical) Attributes for a well-considered environmental optimization. To return to the Northern hypothetical, I could easily see all your tribe possessing a high Stamina and correspondingly lower Dexterity being of benefit. Stamina + Resistance (after external penalties from hypothermia-inducing temperatures) to not fall asleep and die before your hunting party caught in a blizzard by surprise can find/make life-saving shelter is a lot more survivable if everyone in the hunting party of seven individuals all have Stam 3/Resistance 3 (tribe-wide training), rather than 2 of the 7 having Sta 2, 1 having Sta 1, 3 having Sta 3, and 1 having Sta 4. (Which would be a likely spread for non-engineered humans, although perhaps a bit high)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T00:22:03-07:00","id":1236328,"title":"","content":"Not to necro the thread much further, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24378\" data-vbnamecard=\"24378\">Wyldwraith</a> what you may have missed from what I and others in the thread said was that 3E when it has not spoken in a thing is drawing upon 1E roots. In fact, we are not saying throw 1E out except where 3E has said something new on the matter. I think you don\u2019t seem to realize how huge of a gulf there in fact is between 1E and 2E and why we are emphasizing the break. A perfect example of this is an old elemental favorite of mine, the Mercury Ant. Mercury Ants in 1E (Games of Divinity) where communal builders who had some neat tricks about shaping tunnels and would attack only if provoked...2E gave them for some godforsaken reason an aphrodisiac bite that drove people insane overtime. And concocted a really dumb story to make mercury ants hostile to humans, more than jut having someone invade your territory already would mind you. THAT is what people push back against when they say 2E is...problematic. 2E took a perfectly serviceable and cool elemental and added needless sexual torture and emnity when it was not needed to the 1E base. It\u2019s why the Devs reference 1E as their starting point as distinct and different from 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:15:41-07:00","id":1236346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1236276#post1236276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're people whose performances in the fields of human endeavor are all affected in the same way, for the same reason, descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't accurate, though. We've been told multiple times across both sets of devs that the nature of God-Blooded is far different and more variable than it was in 2e. One child of an Erythmanus might just have a leathery, hairy hide, while the other might have a full-on suite of Charms. A Solar's firstborn might be able to see the patterns of the future by observing strange omens, while the next child she bears with her Lunar mate might turn into a gold-skinned ram by the moon's light. <br /> <br /> And <i>none</i> of them are just going to get a copy of their parent's Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-18-2018, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T06:49:56-07:00","id":1236391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223771-tell-me-about-half-caste-characters?p=1236346#post1236346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't accurate, though. We've been told multiple times across both sets of devs that the nature of God-Blooded is far different and more variable than it was in 2e. One child of an Erythmanus might just have a leathery, hairy hide, while the other might have a full-on suite of Charms. A Solar's firstborn might be able to see the patterns of the future by observing strange omens, while the next child she bears with her Lunar mate might turn into a gold-skinned ram by the moon's light.<br /> <br /> And <i>none</i> of them are just going to get a copy of their parent's Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true to the god blooded rules in the original Player's Guide before they went too far and overshadowed themselves by providing several of the characteristics of Exaltation as Merits with Flaws to offset them, fueling a fixation with trying to be like the Exalted rather than their own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:32:06-07:00","id":1236512,"title":"","content":"Apologies then,<br /> Perhaps I missed the 1E-return thing as an unspoken aside, as a new guy. Thinking on what you said Saipjas, I concur that 2E introduced a lot of unnecessary squick to things 1E had treated, and not sure why that was, honestly. So my sincerest apologies there.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;we've been told by Devs X, Y and Z factoid&quot; though...Honestly, after lurking through some of the explosions about people falling in love with some concept a Dev apparently brought up at one point, only for that concept to be subsequently abandoned (the mini-Loom of the Caul built by Lunars leaps to mind), I've adopted a &quot;It's real when the book gets published&quot; mindset. There's more than enough meat on the bone to tussle over when the meat is actually real, without tussling over the possibly-real/possibly-not marrow of the bone, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Personally, I am hoping for at least *some* homogeneity among the children of Celestial Exalts. Variance would be wonderful, given that Exalted shards are varied by Caste, and that there are two divergences of Solar shards, but I kind of fell in love with the notion of &quot;Golden Children&quot; and by extension Moon-Touched, Star-Blessed etc. I would be perfectly happy if the variances came in such beings mechanical aptitudes, and the similarities were in some more fluff-related element. Like a distinguishing cosmetic characteristic, or a personality influence. I'm glad to hear that God-Bloods and Exalt-children will be receiving different treatment, and hope the other X-Bloods get detailed treatment as well. The penetration of the supernatural into the mortal societies is at the heart of Exalted for me.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I would *adore* a well-delineated, well-balanced system for dealing with X-Bloods of various purity. I brought up a hypothetical in another thread, concerning the idea of a God-Blood themselves breeding with a God, and a Demon-Blood being ordered by their demonic progenitor to breed with a demon. Such &quot;three-quarters&quot; children, and the inverse more-mortal &quot;one-quarter&quot; children of X-bloods have always interested me greatly. The West is apparently loaded with islanders with various degrees of divine and elemental blood, and being able to chart that would be great.<br /> <br /> Not sure how I feel about the idea of distancing Beastfolk from their Lunar origins. I would prefer a demarcation of some sort, between those aware of their Lunar descent, and those either unaware of it or stem from another source. Fluff material could handle that well enough, if it's truly necessary in the first place. I hope it's well-written and considered if they do distance them from their Lunar roots, however.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I should probably admit a certain bias against some of the changes being made in 3E. I'm a huge &quot;Lunar guy&quot;, and this whole &quot;Primal howl in the souls of Lunars. Pushing them to tear down the Realm and destroy the reminders of their failures&quot; thing really feels like more of the Wyld-Taint in Lunar Exaltations thing, or &quot;Lunars are woad-painted barbarians, all in love with Amoth City-Smiter, and seeking to make Creation into one big barbarian anarchy-zone, and those who don't want to be that have to resist the primal howl in their souls just to be civilized.&quot; It feels like more, &quot;Must claim a Territory, must do X, Y and Z&quot; that Lunars NEVER seem to be able to escape, and I cannot for the life of me comprehend why incredibly talented writers, who are provably capable of designing amazing Splats, can't get off this Exaltation Homogeneity kick that has hounded Lunars for two editions and looks primed to run into the third. I find the DBs incredibly fascinating, especially Outcastes, but WFHW did not fill me with joy, mechanically. There's a thread someone just created which explains my feelings on the matter with such breath-taking articulation I wanted to applaud when I read it.<br /> <br /> So, personally, I'm experiencing something of a psychological impetus to cling to the old. Don't get me wrong, Heaven knows the mechanics needed an overhaul, and I love some of the new. The very idea of the Caul makes me want to applaud again. I'm just not so sure how much 3E-Love is actually 3E-Love, and how much is 2E-Justified Squick and Mechanic-Hate being expressed as a desperate hope for better in 3E. I also realize the inherent hypocrisy in saying &quot;don't argue over what isn't published yet&quot; and then going on to platform for my own 3E-hopes-and-fears. Sorry about that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}